window.FWN_GODLY_EMPRESS_DOCTOR_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_GODLY_EMPRESS_DOCTOR_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":3701,"title":"Chapter 3701: Pursuit (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3701: Pursuit (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","According to Mr. Sakiya, Feng Wu was the culprit.","The man stared at Feng Wu and scolded her. “Stop crying!”","The girl was supposed to be someone who could give General Xue Zhibei a hard time so she had to be tough. As it turned out, the girl stopped crying as soon as the man threatened her.","She stopped crying and looked at the man with teary eyes. She was such an innocent and pitiful girl!","The man wondered if he had caught the wrong person again.","“Are you really Feng Wu?!” He stared at Feng Wu.","Feng Wu put on a long face. “Can I say that I’m not?”","The man said, “Are you the culprit behind all the chaos in Sun Castle?”","Feng Wu said, “Maybe not?”","The man threw a dirty look at Feng Wu. What was that supposed to mean?","“Stop pretending! It has to be you!” The man snorted. “To tell you the truth, capturing you is the unanimous decision of the Dongsang Kingdom. You won’t get away. ”","Feng Wu put on a long face. “Is everyone in the Dongsang Kingdom trying to catch me?”","The man nodded.","Feng Wu was confused. “But why?”","The man said, “Because of something Mr. Sakiya said.”","Feng Wu asked, “What did he say?","The man stared at Feng Wu in bewilderment.","Feng Wu asked curiously, “What did he say?”","Feng Wu decided that she would talk to Mr. Sakiya when she had the chance to meet him. She wouldn’t let him set her up like this.","The man stopped talking at that point.","Rising to his feet, he looked at Feng Wu and said coldly, “I think this is as far as I can go.”","Feng Wu panicked at those words!","What did he mean by that?","That was to say...","Feng Wu looked around and wondered if this pool was where she would be buried.","Her imagination was running wild when she heard footsteps a short distance away.","Soon, a person wearing a silver butterfly mask appeared behind the man. The two of them walked to the side and exchanged signals before they started talking in the Dongsang language.","Feng Wu didn’t know who it was, but she knew that if she stayed with the man, her life would be in danger.","She had figured it out already.","Sakiya must have given that man two sets of instructions.","It would be great if he could take her back alive, but if not, he would kill her right here and now.","Feng Wu could sense how intimidated Sakiya was.","So, she couldn’t stay here anymore.","Feng Wu looked at the deep pool a few meters away.","There was nothing she could do at first, but then she found the hidden river under the pool, which gave her a chance.","Feng Wu rose to her feet when she saw the two people talking in the Dongsang language.","So what if she had no spiritual essence?","She could dive!","She slowly slid into the pool without splashing any water.","She didn’t make a sound, so neither the man in black nor the silver-masked person noticed what was going on until...","He was about to hand Feng Wu to the silver-masked person when he realized something.","Where was she?","The two people looked at each other in bewilderment.","They had used some very well-hidden spies to catch Feng Wu, but now, their target was gone!","The silver-masked person stared at the black-robed man, who was dumbfounded.."]},{"number":3702,"title":"Chapter 3702: Recover Her Power (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3702: Recover Her Power (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","The silver-masked person stared at the black-robed man, who was dumbfounded.","“Where is she?” The silver-masked person stared at the man.","The man was very powerful, but his voice was trembling when he spoke. “She was just here!”","The silver-masked person quickly walked up to the pool and examined the ground.","Soon, the person noticed something.","“She’s in the pool.” After that, the silver-masked man jumped into the pool.","With a stern look on his face, the black-robed man rushed into the pool without another word.","Feng Wu felt the cold water in the pool.","But she had no other choice now. She had to run for as long as she could. Jun Linyuan would definitely come for her.","She headed directly for the river at the bottom of the pool.","She didn’t know where it led to, but she decided to run first.","Feng Wu almost fainted when she dove into the cold water.","Luckily, she was a water-element cultivator.","wait!","Feng Wu realized that she began to feel the spiritual essence in her body.","That was to say, she was gradually recovering.","At that thought, Feng Wu felt that there was hope again.","Feng Wu activated her spiritual essence as she swam in the underground river.","She didn’t have much spiritual essence at this point because she had only just recovered and was only at the Spiritual Master Stage.","Come on...","Feng Wu said in her head.","The river was so dark that one couldn’t see their own fingers.","Because of that, her hearing became much more acute.","All of a sudden, Feng Wu heard a faint noise behind her.","Soon, there was another faint sound.","Feng Wu frowned.","Were those two people chasing her already?","As expected, someone cried out a short distance away. “There’s a hidden river down there!”","They were even able to speak in the water, which wasn’t something just anyone could do.","Feng Wu was certain that Jun Linyuan was capable enough to do that.","Were they both at Jun Linyuan’s level?","That thought frustrated Feng Wu.","However, no matter how frustrated she was, her top priority now was to get away.","It was obvious that the man wanted to kill her.","Run, run, run!","Just then, the black-robed man said, “I think that girl is right ahead of us!”","The silver-masked person asked, “Can you still sense her?”","The black-robed man nodded. “I’ve marked her. I can sense her wherever she goes!”","After a pause, he went on. “It was Mr. Sakiya’s idea. He said that the girl was as slippery as a loach and could run away at any moment. He was right. She slipped away in no time!”","The silver-masked person said, “We’ll kill her when we catch her.”","The black-robed man said, “That’s what I thought.’","What they didn’t know was that because of the echo, Feng Wu could hear everything they said.","Feng Wu was several kilometers away from them.","She was furious.","They would kill her when they caught her.","“I’d like to see you catch me!” Taking a deep breath, Feng Wu activated her spiritual essence again.","When her spiritual essence was back, Feng Wu could open up her ring space again.","She had some blood origin crystals with her, so she bit one without hesitation and let the dense spiritual essence rush into her dantian.."]},{"number":3703,"title":"Chapter 3703: Recover Her Power (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3703: Recover Her Power (2)","In a matter of seconds, Feng Wu had risen from a Spiritual Master to a Spiritual Grandmaster.","But that wasn’t enough!","She could clearly feel the two men getting closer and closer.","Had he put something on her?","Feng Wu tried to sense it, and she was right.","It was a streak of spiritual essence that the black-robed man had sealed in her meridians when she had no spiritual essence left.","She wouldn’t have been able to sense it if she hadn’t recovered her spiritual essence, but now that she had, there was no way that this could fool her.","Feng Wu saw a tortoise swimming casually in the river. An idea struck her, and she grabbed the old tortoise.","The tortoise was over 5kg in weight, and its black shell was hard and tough.","Luckily, Feng Wu was a Spiritual Master now, so she was able to break the shell.","Feng Wu extracted the black-robed man’s spiritual essence and injected it into the old tortoise.","The old tortoise cringed, fearing that Feng Wu would do something to it.","Feng Wu saw a fork in the road ahead.","The fork was much smaller than the main one and was only wide enough for one person to get through.","Moreover, after some calculations, Feng Wu realized that she would soon be able to reach the shore through this fork.","Should she go ashore?","Feng Wu shook her head.","She had more advantage in the water than on land.","If they were on land, she wouldn’t be able to run very far.","Therefore, Feng Wu chose to keep swimming in the river and put the tortoise in the fork.","Feng Wu patted the shell of the big tortoise. “Let’s go. It’s best if you can lure both of them away from me.”","Although deep down, Feng Wu knew that it was impossible. Feng Wu would feel so lucky if one of them was lured away/","After releasing the big tortoise, Feng Wu moved faster in the river.","Maybe fate was on Feng Wu’s side as well. In a matter of minutes, Feng Wu had risen from a Spiritual Grandmaster to a Spiritual Elder.","But those two people were so powerful that a Spiritual Elder would do nothing to them.","The water was flowing faster and faster.","Feng Wu felt a tightness in her chest and almost spat out a mouthful of blood.","But deep down, she was over the moon.","Let the current move faster.","Otherwise, they would soon catch up with her.","Meanwhile, the two people had indeed reached the fork in the river.","They saw the two paths in front of them.","One was the main branch of the underground river, and the other one was the fork.","They looked at each other with brooding looks in their eyes.","If the girl really got away this time and the higher-ups blamed them, they would probably have to take their own lives.","The black-robed man said decisively, “Let’s split up.”","After that, he wanted to swim into the fork.","The silver-masked person stared at him. “Can you sense her going that way?” The man said, “Well...","He wished he hadn’t shared that piece of information.","The person with the silver butterfly mask said, “You go that way, then.”","The black-robed man asked, “Are you going to let me take all the credit?”","The silver-masked man said, “I don’t want any meritorious service, but I don’t want to make mistakes.”","The black-robed man immediately took the hint.","A useless girl with zero cultivation ability had slipped away right under their noses. If word got out, the two of them would be so humiliated that they would have to kill themselves even if Mr. Sakiya didn’t punish them.","“Alright. I’ll kill her when I catch up with her. I won’t take her back to the","Dongsang Kingdom. It’ll be a long journey.. I’m sure she’ll run away again!”"]},{"number":3704,"title":"Chapter 3704: Desperate Situation (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3704: Desperate Situation (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","The silver-masked person nodded and headed down the main stream way.","The black-robed man suggested, “How about you come with me? I can sense her. She’s right ahead of us.” The silver-masked person only said, “Just to be safe.”","The black-robed man agreed.","Just to be on the safe side, they would split up so that nothing could go wrong.","However, he was glad that he had thought it through. He could sense that he was getting closer and closer to Feng Wu.","500m. 300m.","loom.","10m!","The man’s stomach lurched, and he looked pleased.","“You’re so good at running, aren’t you? Why don’t you move fast?”","The man smirked inwardly as he took out a broadsword from behind his back.","There was no time to waste. He would cut the girl into little pieces.","However...","Wait, where was she?","The man realized in amazement that the girl wasn’t there.","But he could sense her...","Was that her ghost?","The man’s stomach lurched.","However, he was a capable cultivator and didn’t believe much in ghosts. In the end, he found a big turtle buried under the mud.","The man didn’t know what to say.","The big turtle was just unlucky. Having been caught by Feng Wu once, it was so sacred that it hid in the mud, but the man dug it out again.","Sensing the spiritual essence he had buried in Feng Wu in the turtle, the man was speechless.","He frowned.","“That girl has found out about my spiritual essence?","“And she had removed it.","“That is to say, the girl has broken her confinement. “Has she recovered her spiritual essence?”","The more he thought about it, the more convinced he was.","What a cunning girl. How could she run away in a situation like this?","However...","The man smirked. “Even if you’re back to your peak state, you still won’t be able to withstand a single strike from us. You’re not going anywhere!” The man abandoned the unlucky turtle and headed for the main stream way.","But he soon stopped.","That didn’t make sense. With the girl’s intelligence, how could she have such a simple plan?","Although there was only a big turtle here, maybe she had left it here on purpose so that he would go the other way. Maybe she was right ahead.","Since his colleague was already on the other route, the black-robed man decided not to turn back. Instead, he kept moving forward.","This time, the man was genuinely infuriated. Blue veins popped on his forehead, and he looked like he was going to explode.","All he wanted was to catch Feng Wu.","However...","For the time being, he wouldn’t be able to find Feng Wu anywhere nearby.","The silver-masked person, on the other hand, followed Feng Wu down the main route.","The undercurrent grew stronger, but it didn’t stop the man. Instead, he picked up his speed.","The distance between them grew shorter and shorter.","They were kilometers apart at first, but now, he was only a few hundreds of meters behind Feng Wu.","“That person is coming after us!”","Feng Wu heard a familiar voice in her head.","It had to be Little Phoenix.","Feng Wu was excited. “You’re awake!”","Little Phoenix was very anxious. “That man is very capable. Although he’s not a Spiritual Saint yet, he’s definitely a peak Spiritual Overlord! Did you offend him?”","Feng Wu had lost contact with Little Phoenix before, so it knew nothing about what was going on.."]},{"number":3705,"title":"Chapter 3705: Desperate Situation (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3705: Desperate Situation (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Therefore, Feng Wu told Little Phoenix the problem she was facing.","Little Phoenix said, “So, you’re in a desperate situation.”","Feng Wu was speechless. The little bird was so calm.","Just then, the silver-masked man closed in and sensed Feng Wu’s presence.","Keeping his unblinking gaze on Feng Wu, he picked up his speed again!","Feng Wu had reached her limit.","Right now, she was a Spiritual Lord again, and she wouldn’t be able to move much faster even if she tried her best.","“Get up here.” Little Phoenix appeared beneath Feng Wu.","Feng Wu looked perplexed.","Little Phoenix said solemnly, “He’s catching up with us.” As it spoke, Little Phoenix grew bigger.","The palm-sized bird suddenly grew to a meter long.","Feng Wu moved before without thinking. She landed on Little Phoenix’s back and wrapped her arms around its neck.","By then, the silver-masked man was only a hundred meters away.","Although the river was dark, they could still see each other.","Feng Wu looked over her shoulder and saw the smirk on the man’s face. It was the gloating smile of someone who was sure of victory.","“Kiddo, where do you think you’re going?” he yelled. The next second, Little Phoenix picked up its speed.","Whoosh!","Little Phoenix dashed off like a little motorboat!","The silver-masked man looked surprised.","He watched as Feng Wu flew away on an object.","They were only loom apart before, and the man thought he could catch Feng Wu with a wave of his hand. But now, the distance between them had widened.","200m, 300m, 400m...","The silver-masked man wouldn’t stand it.","He picked up his speed as well.","Feng Wu did some calculations and saw that they were running at the same speed.","They remained 1000m away, and the distance didn’t change for a while.","Feng Wu was secretly relieved, but she was still nervous.","Because to a top cultivator, the 1000m was nothing.","If she was caught, she would really die.","Feng Wu knew that she couldn’t disturb Little Phoenix now. If it lost its speed, she would be caught right away.","She touched Little Phoenix’s forehead and was surprised when she felt the sticky sweat.","Little Phoenix spoke first.","“Don’t worry! I can hold on for a little longer!”","“Luckily, his speed isn’t his forte. If we were anywhere but in this river, he would have caught up with us already.”","Feng Wu nodded. “That’s right. He’s very capable.”","“Moreover, if it’s like you said, he’s at the peak of the Spiritual Overlord Stage, he’ll be much more endurant than us. Therefore, he’ll definitely win in the end. ”","Little Phoenix nodded. “Three minutes, tops.”","That was to say, Little Phoenix would slow down in three minutes, and they would be caught.","Feng Wu had three minutes to figure out a plan. Otherwise...","“There has to be a way.”","Feng Wu closed her eyes and was lost in her thoughts.","Little Phoenix said, “I’ll know what to do if you can stall for 15 minutes.”","Feng Wu asked, “What’s your plan?”"]},{"number":3706,"title":"Chapter 3706: Desperate Situation (3)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3706: Desperate Situation (3)","Little Phoenix said solemnly, “I know this underground river well. There’s a way out, but it’ll take me at least 15 minutes to get there.”","Feng Wu said, “Alright. I’ll think of something in the 12 minutes after you slow down!”","Feng Wu took a deep breath and gradually calmed down.","It seemed that she would have to use poison.","Feng Wu had stored quite a few bottles of poison in her ring space. She would make them whenever she had time, so that she could use them to set other people up in critical moments like this.","Feng Wu couldn’t open the space earlier because the man had sealed her spiritual essence, so there was nothing she could do.","But now that she could open up the ring space, she could use all the bottles.","Hence, while Little Phoenix was running as fast as it could, Feng Wu lay on its back and started throwing out poisons.","She calculated the speed of the silver-masked man and threw out bottles.","The transparent bottles would explode in a matter of seconds.","Of course, the explosion couldn’t hurt the man, but the potion that splashed out was poisonous.","Soon, Feng Wu heard the crackling sound behind her.","No matter how hard the man tried to dodge, he couldn’t avoid the potion.","Because the potion was right there in the water.","The man had no choice but to slow down.","As soon as he slowed down, Little Phoenix and Feng Wu quickly moved away from him, and they were soon 5km ahead.","The silver-masked man smirked. He wasn’t worried at all.","The toxin wouldn’t hurt him much and would soon be forced out of his body. It wouldn’t affect his cultivation level much either.","As time went by, the giant bird would grow tired and slow down. Therefore, he wasn’t worried at all.","“I’d like to see how many bottles you have and when you’ll run out!” The man smirked.","As expected, there were no more bottles after a while.","The man grinned.","“I knew she wouldn’t last much longer!”","Hence, the man picked up his speed and closed the distance between them again.","3km, Ikm, 500m...","When they were loom apart again, Feng Wu started throwing out bottles again.","She couldn’t control the time of the explosion from afar, but she could do it from a few hundred meters away.","“Explode!” Feng Wu threw out poisonous bottles one after another.","The man with the butterfly mask was speechless.","He already knew what kind of bottles they were, so he didn’t think much of them and waved the water away.","However, this time...","The silver-masked man let his guard down, but he didn’t notice the steel needles shooting out of one of the bottles after it exploded. Most of the needles were brushed away, but some still stuck into him.","There was even a needle in his eye.","The silver-masked man screamed. It was really painful.","He choked on a mouthful of water.","It wouldn’t be so bad if it was just ordinary water, but it was poisonous.","The man rose to the surface and spat the water out.","By then, black water was coming out of his eyes.","“It’s poisonous!” The man removed the tiny needle, his face contorted with rage.."]},{"number":3707,"title":"Chapter 3707: Desperate Situation (4)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3707: Desperate Situation (4)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","The silver-masked man wasn’t good at medicine. Therefore, after being poisoned, he could only use the most primitive method, which was to use spiritual essence to force out the poison.","But this time...","For some reason, the poison stuck to his eye sockets and couldn’t be forced out.","Moreover... it seemed to have a life of its own as it drilled into his brain.","The man’s face turned pale.","It seemed that he could only...","A ruthless expression appeared on his face. Without hesitation, he stabbed the finger of his right hand into the injured eye!","The man screamed in pain.","He dug out his eyeball.","The poison was also brought out.","It hurt...","The worst thing wasn’t the pain, but the loss of an eye.","He used flames to stop the bleeding from his wound.","The next moment, he dove into the underground river again!","Feng Wu was already dozens of kilometers away.","She heaved a sigh of relief. “Looks like he won’t be able to catch up anytime soon. It’ll give us some time to catch our breath.”","However, Little Phoenix was still frowning. It said solemnly, “That’s a ruthless person. He’ll catch up soon.”","Feng Wu said, “I still have some poison. He won’t be able to catch up so easily.","By the way, how are you?”","The phoenix said, “I can still hold on.”","She stuffed a Blood Origin Crystal into its mouth.","Little Phoenix was delighted when it saw the crystal.","It was indeed a good thing to replenish spiritual essence.","Little Phoenix finished the crystal in a few bites.","Feng Wu said, “I took them from the Hua and Zuo families. There are only a dozen left.”","Feng Wu counted. There were 16 in total.","Hence, she divided them into two portions, eight for herself and eight for Little Phoenix.","The journey ahead was arduous, and no one knew if they could get away.","Therefore, neither of them spoke after that. They only chewed on the Blood Origin Crystals, trying to recover their spiritual essence as soon as possible.","Soon, they reached a fork in the river.","Feng Wu had a little more time now, so she began to set up a formation.","She didn’t have much time, so she made it very simple. All she needed to do was to get the silver-masked man lost.","“Let’s go.”","Feng Wu spent a precious minute setting up the formation, hoping to confuse the man. Even if she couldn’t fool him, she could at least buy them some time.","Little Phoenix carried Feng Wu along the main waterway.","Before long, the silver-masked man caught up with them. He frowned when he saw the two paths ahead of them.","His right eye had been gouged out, and his left eye glinted in the darkness","“Feng wu!”","He gritted his teeth.","Mr. Sakiya was right. The first thing he had to do when he saw the girl was to cut her into pieces. He couldn’t let her brain work.","Her ability had been sealed, and she had run out of spiritual essence, but they still had to chase her in such a sorry state... This girl was unbelievable!","The man looked away and stared at the two routes.","Which one should he choose?","After some thought, the man couldn’t make up his mind, so he had to come out of the water again.","He had a special way of communicating with the black-robed man, so he soon found the latter.","Poor black-robed man...","He swam for a long time without seeing any trace of Feng Wu, so he knew that he had made a mistake. Hence, he was on his way back.."]},{"number":3708,"title":"Chapter 3708: Escape (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3708: Escape (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","The black-robed man ran into the silver-masked man on his way back.","He frowned when he saw the latter. “You’ve lost her, too?”","The man with the butterfly mask said, “Come with me.”","The black-robed man frowned. “Why should I go with you? You don’t have her!”","The silver-masked man said, “I know where she is.”","The black-robed man’s eyes lit up. “Where?!”","The silver-masked man said, “Just come with me!”","This time, the black-robed man didn’t say another word. He followed the silver-masked man and swam very fast.","Soon, they reached the fork in the river.","The black-robed man was frustrated. “Why are there so many forks again? I can’t believe it!”","The silver-masked man looked at him. “She was right in front of me, and I almost caught her a few times, but she’s so cunning!”","He said angrily, “She slipped away from me every single time!”","The black-robed man agreed with him. “I caught her a while ago, but she still managed to get away. I can believe it.” He suddenly noticed the silver-masked man’s eye. “Your right eye...’","The silver-masked man felt so humiliated.","He asked coldly, “Which one do you want to choose?”","The black-robed man was still trying to figure out what was going on in his eye.","“Did that girl poison your right eye?”","The silver-masked man flew into a rage out of humiliation. “Go back to your fork!”","After that, he turned around and swam toward the main waterway.","The black-robed man knew that he was right. His friend had really been poisoned by the girl.","“Although you’re not as capable as I am, you’re still a capable cultivator.","However, you ramea co caccn a gooa-ror-notmng ana were poisonea DY ner. How humiliating!”","The silver-masked man was frustrated and didn’t know what to say. He ignored the man and kept rushing forward.","The black-robed man stopped him. “Hey, wait.”","He frowned and said, “I’m not going to take the wrong path this time. I think the girl is going to take the main waterway, so I’m going to choose that path.” The silver-masked man stared at the black-robed man, displeased.","The black-robed man said, “Well, I lost that girl first, and I’m more responsible than you are. You should at least give me a chance to make up for it. When Mr.","Sakiya asks...”","The silver-masked man threw a dirty look at him and headed for the fork in the river.","Since the black-robed man had finally gotten the chance, the man didn’t say anything else. He only frowned and charged forward.","He was a little faster than the silver-masked man, so it didn’t take him long to sense someone up ahead.","The man was elated.","The chance of finding another living person in this river was very slim. It had to be that girl!","At that thought, the man was elated.","“You brat! Just wait and see. Once I catch you...”","The next second, Little Phoenix sensed his presence as well.","A chill ran down its spine, and it picked up its speed again. Feng Wu sensed it right away and asked, “Are they coming after us again?”","Little Phoenix nodded. “This one is even faster than before.”","Feng Wu smiled bitterly. It seemed that the man in black had caught up with her.","However, catching up with them wasn’t that easy.","Feng Wu grabbed a cuttlefish swimming next to her, injected it with a needle, and patted it on the head. “Go ahead..”"]},{"number":3709,"title":"Chapter 3709: Escape (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3709: Escape (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","The cuttlefish was still trying to figure out what was going on when it ran into the man in black.","The man didn’t know what was going on. Seeing the half-meter-long cuttlefish blocking his way, he waved his hand. “Get lost.”","What he didn’t know was that the cuttlefish was poisonous.","It wasn’t at first, but because of the injection Feng Wu gave it, it was covered with poison now.","The cuttlefish exploded in front of the man.","The man was at the peak of the Spiritual Overlord Stage, so he couldn’t have been injured by the explosion. However, he was so surprised that he opened his mouth and swallowed some water.","Cough.","The man coughed violently.","He knew that he had swallowed some of the cuttlefish’s ink, but he didn’t think much of it. It was just some juice.","However, his first reaction was to cover his eyes, so nothing happened to them.","“You Drat! you really are poisonous!”","The man was furious. ‘You’ll regret this when I catch you!”","The incident slowed him down a little, but he was very angry, so he picked up his speed.","Luckily, Little Phoenix had swallowed the Blood Origin Crystal, or it would have been drained by the acceleration.","“We’re almost there! The tomb hall is right ahead of us!” Before Feng Wu could ask, Little Phoenix told her.","Feng Wu was confused. “What’s that?”","Little Phoenix said, “I’ll tell you later. This hall can at least stall him for a while!”","After that, Little Phoenix shouted, “Hold on!”","Feng Wu wrapped her arms around Little Phoenix’s neck.","The next moment, Little Phoenix jumped out of the water and landed on the bank.","Looking up, Feng Wu saw a hall.","The building was so tall that one couldn’t see the top. The walls were so wide that one couldn’t see the end of it.","It was enormous!","Standing in front of the hall, Feng Wu felt so tiny.","“This is the biggest hall I’ve ever seen...” Feng Wu stared at it.","There was such a hall by the river?","By then, Little Phoenix had used its last strength to get Feng Wu out of the river. It was too weak to move, and its meter-long body was shrinking rapidly.","In the end, it shrunk to the size of a fist.","Panting, Little Phoenix told Feng Wu, “Quickly, hide in that hall! Maybe it’ll save our lives!”","After that, Little Phoenix fainted.","Feng Wu knew that Little Phoenix was exhausted, so she carefully picked it up and put it away in her ring space.","She found the door Little Phoenix showed her.","There was a small hole in the side of the hall.","Feng Wu was confused. Where did this hole come from? Why did it look like a dog’s den?","Well...","However, it wasn’t easy to get in, for the opening was sealed.","Luckily, Feng Wu had some corrosive potion with her, so she was able to quickly make a hole wide enough for her to go in.","Feng Wu was only halfway in when the black-robed man jumped out of the river.","He looked around and couldn’t hide the excitement on his face.","“That’s...","“Is that the legendary Immortal Palace?”","“It’s said that countless capable cultivators of the current generation have entered the hall!","“It’s said that Master Mu Jiuzhou, the only ruler of this continent, is buried there!”"]},{"number":3710,"title":"Chapter 3710: Escape (3)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3710: Escape (3)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","“Master Mu Jiuzhou is the master teacher’s master!”","He was so excited that he was shaking from head to toe.","Just then, he glanced around and spotted the little hole and Feng Wu’s butt.","“Feng Wu! Where do you think you’re going?!” The man tried to grab Feng Wu’s leg.","But Feng Wu reacted quickly as well.","In a moment of life and death, she had to be fast.","Feng Wu quickly went through the hole, and the man missed his target.","The man was furious.","“You brat! Where do you think you can go?!” He tried to crawl in through the hole.","However, Feng Wu had calculated the opening beforehand. She had only corroded a space wide enough for her to get through. As for the man in black, he was too big to get in.","The man wanted to break down the door, but it was made from some unknown material, and he couldn’t break it no matter how hard he tried.","Inside, Feng Wu made faces at him.","The man was furious.","Feng Wu ran away after making the face. She knew that the door wouldn’t stop the man. He would come in eventually.","Therefore, her top priority now was to get into the hall and run as fast as she could.","It was a spacious square paved with white marble.","Seeing the white jade brick of the same size, Feng Wu didn’t rush toward the main hall. Instead, she carefully observed her surroundings.","She was right. There was a trap.","If she stepped on the wrong brick, she might trigger the hidden trap. At her current level, she would be killed in no time.","Luckily, she was good at formations.","Pressing her fingers together, she tried to deduce the formation in her head.","It was the Nine-Layered Maze Formation.","The formation would trap people here so that they wouldn’t be able to leave the square. They would keep walking until they died of exhaustion.","It wasnt easy to get out.","After figuring out the right path, Feng Wu began to walk with her eyes closed.","If one opened their eyes, they could easily make a mistake because the most impressive thing about this formation was that it could confuse one’s eyes.","Feng Wu covered her eyes with a black cloth, and it took her fifteen minutes to walk from the square to the main hall.","Feng Wu only let out a breath of relief when she stepped into the hall.","By then, her forehead was covered with sweat.","Wiping away the sweat on her forehead, Feng Wu heard some noise behind her. Turning around, she saw the black-robed man come in.","The silver-masked man came in with him.","She had no idea how the two men got in, but they were already there.","They looked up to find Feng Wu standing outside the main hall, and their eyes went bloodshot red. They wanted to fly to Feng Wu’s side right away.","But reality surprised them.","Because when they rushed in, they realized that they couldn’t control where they were going.","Feng Wu was less than ten meters away from them, but they realized that they couldn’t make it to her side.","They kept walking and even ran as fast as they could, but they still couldn’t get within ten meters of her.","Only then did Feng Wu let out a breath of relief and waved at them.","“Stop! Stop right there!”","Seeing that Feng Wu was leaving, the black-robed man shouted at her. Feng Wu smiled at them. “Don’t worry about chasing me. Just stay here.”","“Stop right there!” The black-robed man was furious.."]},{"number":3711,"title":"Chapter 3711: Escape (4)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3711: Escape (4)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","She turned around and smiled at him. “If you keep running around like that, you’ll trigger a trap.”","Maybe the black-robed man was unlucky because the moment she said that, he really triggered a trap.","“Whoosh!”","Immediately, black arrows shot toward him like meteors.","Fortunately, the two men were very capable. They managed to withstand the wave of arrows and smashed them down. Even so, they both had injuries afterward.","Dark black blood flowed out of the wounds.","It was obvious that arrows were poisonous.","After the wave of arrows, they thought they could finally walk out of the formation, but that didn’t happen.","She waved her hand. “I won’t tell you the way in, but I can tell you the way out. I’ll let you live. Listen carefully...”","After reciting the incantation, she didn’t care about the expressions of the two men. She waved at them and walked into the hall with the weakened phoenix in her arms.","“Hey, stop right there! Stop right there!”","The black-robed man almost exploded.","Mr. Sakiya was right. She was such a cunning brat. As long as she was given a chance, she would be able to slip away, regardless of whether she had cultivation ability or not!","In the end, the two men could only watch helplessly as Feng Wu entered the hall and disappeared.","“What should we do?” The black-robed man turned to glare at the silver-masked man.","The silver-masked man was obviously infuriated as well, and his chest was heaving.","What should they do? He also wanted to know what to do!","He stared at the black-robed man. “Have you sent back the news of catching this girl?”","The black-robed man’s face turned red.","There was no need to say anything else. It was obvious that the black-robed man had already sent the news back.","The black-robed man almost flew into a rage out of humiliation. “At that time, she was my prisoner! She’s just a little piece of trash without any spiritual energy. Isn’t that almost certain? So I...”","The silver-masked man said, “It would have been fine if we didn’t send the news back. Now that we did, we’ve also lost her. Will we be able to live if we go back?”","The black-robed man said, “If we’re going to die, why don’t we catch that girl first? That way, we can atone for my crime. Plus, even if we’re going to be punished, we can take that girl down with us!”","The silver-masked man said, “Let’s find our way, then!”","Neither of them knew much about formations, so they soon triggered the mechanism again, and a second wave of weapons flew out.","They were simply too capable and managed to withstand the second wave of attack.","But soon, there was a third, a fourth, and a fifth wave...","Meanwhile...","Feng Wu was quickly entering the hall with Little Phoenix.","“Why did you tell them the way out?” Little Phoenix asked grumpily.","Feng Wu looked around as she answered Little Phoenix. “If they’re unlucky enough to trigger another wave of hidden weapons, their morale will weaken in the end. Maybe they’ll give up.”","Little Phoenix shook its head. “You underestimate the Dongsang people. They won’t give up.”","Feng Wu said, “Even if they don’t, we’ve walked so far ahead of them. It won’t be that easy for them to catch up with us..”"]},{"number":3712,"title":"Chapter 3712: The Ginseng Sown Back Then (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3712: The Ginseng Sown Back Then (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Little Phoenix nodded. That bird had a point.","Things were much better than when they were in the river.","Feng Wu raised an eyebrow. “I’m afraid they’ll be covered in wounds when they get out of the maze and catch up with us. Plus, I think those weapons are poisonous.”","Little Phoenix thought otherwise. “The Dongsang Kingdom is much better than us in medical skills. I’m sure they have some medicine with them. It’s not as optimistic as you think.”","Feng Wu agreed and felt a little disappointed. In the end, she said, “At least we can stall for a while. That’s good enough. By the way, there are so many paths.","Which one should we take?”","Three paths appeared in front of Feng Wu.","The one on the left said Life, the one in the middle said Danger, and the one on the right said Death.","The three doors were white, red, and black respectively.","The white and black doors seemed to be in disarray, and the red one in the middle was the only one that didn’t seem dangerous.","But Little Phoenix pointed at the door on the left.","Feng Wu looked at Little Phoenix in bewilderment. “Are you sure?”","Little Phoenix nodded. “That’s right. Just do as you’re told.”","Feng Wu asked, “Are you familiar with handwriting?”","Little Phoenix chuckled. “Of course. I know who did it right away.”","Feng Wu asked curiously, “Who?”","Little Phoenix only said, “You’ll know when the time is right. Quickly, let’s go through that door.”","Feng Wu was still hesitating when she heard a faint noise behind them.","That was...","Were the two men here already?","Without thinking, Feng Wu pushed the door open and walked in.","Behind the door was a black portal. Feng Wu stepped into it, and the next second, she felt dizzy.","Two figures showed up as soon as Feng Wu stepped into the door.","Feng Wu was right, They were indeed those two men.","“Look! There are footprints on the ground!” Pointing at the footprints, the man turned around and looked at the silver-masked man in pleasant surprise.","The man with the silver mask crouched down and examined the footprints.","They weren’t big, and one could tell that they belonged to a girl.","“It’s her!” the man said affirmatively.","The man gritted his teeth. “I didn’t know she could move so fast. It’s only been a little while, and she’s already here!”","Right now, the two of them didn’t look too well.","They had gone through a lot to get out of the maze.","They used the dumbest method. They triggered all the traps and withstand the impact with their physical bodies. They were covered in wounds, but in the end, they still got out of the maze.","However, they still let Feng Wu slip away when they arrived at the scene.","“Her footprints are here.” Pointing at the door, the black-robed man turned to the silver-masked man. “She must have entered the door.”","The silver-masked man frowned. “Are you sure?","The black-robed man wasn’t so sure anymore.","The silver-masked man said, “Don’t you know how cunning she is?”","Recalling how he had been tricked by that girl, the black-robed man was furious again.","The silver-masked man said, “With her intelligence, why would she leave footprints in front of the door for you?”","The black-robed man smacked his head. That made sense.","He stared at his colleague.. “What do you think?”"]},{"number":3713,"title":"Chapter 3713: The Ginseng Sown Back Then (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3713: The Ginseng Sown Back Then (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","The silver-masked man rubbed his chin and was lost in his thoughts. The black-robed man prompted him. “Tell me. Which door do you choose?”","The silver-haired masked man said, “The Life door is a possibility. What if she’s trying to set us up? What if she went through that door, but she’s leaving a trail behind so that we’ll think that she has taken another route?","“Although this door is marked with the word ‘Danger’, it feels safer than the two doors on either side. Therefore, it’s very likely that she went this way.”","“The Death door looks so creepy that no normal person would go in, but what if the girl thinks that we won’t pick it and chose it on purpose? So, that’s possible too.”","The black-robed man stared at his colleague. ‘Which one should we choose, then?”","The silver-masked man couldn’t make up his mind either, and he was frowning.","The black-robed man asked, “Have you made up your mind?”","The silver-masked man shook his head.","The black-robed man frowned. “I don’t think we should try to set her up. Even a hundred people put together won’t be able to do that, and she’ll lead us astray. So, we should use the dumbest method!”","The silver-masked man asked, “What’s that?”","The black-robed man said, “Let’s leave it to fate, and we’ll choose whichever one it tells us to choose.”","The silver-masked man asked, “What if it’s wrong?”","The black-robed man said, “So be it. We’ll choose another one after you come out!”","The silver-masked man thought about it and agreed.","By “leave it to fate”, the black-robed man was referring to the lucky draw.","One couldn’t tell if he was lucky or not, but he picked out the note that said “Life”.","The silver-masked man said, “If you choose Life, I’ll choose Danger. If we don’t find any trace of that girl, we’ll go into the Death door together.”","The black-robed man nodded. “Let’s do it.”","After that, they stepped into the door they had chosen.","Feng Wu stepped on the black portal as soon as she entered the door. When she realized what had happened, she was in a snowfield.","The wind was chilly.","Feng Wu sneezed right away. It was freezing...","“Where am I?” Feng Wu cringed. The wind was so cold that it felt like blades on her face. The pain was unbearable.","Little Phoenix stuck its head out of Feng Wu’s arms and looked around curiously.","“Wait...” Little Phoenix looked suspicious.","Feng Wu asked, “What? What’s wrong?”","Little Phoenix scratched its head. “This isn’t what I remember. I remember this place used to be like spring all year round. The weather was warm, the birds sang, and the flowers smelled nice. Why is it a snowfield now?","Feng Wu stared at Little Phoenix. “Are you sure you remembered it correctly? Maybe we should take the Danger or Death door instead?”","Little Phoenix hesitated. Could it be...","The look on its face gave Feng Wu the creeps. “Have we chosen the wrong door?”","Little Phoenix put on a long face. “I can’t say... I really don’t remember anything.”","Feng Wu said, “Weren’t you so confident when you told me to go this way just then?”","Little Phoenix felt a pain in its chest. “But, after so many years, I don’t even recognize this place anymore..”"]},{"number":3714,"title":"Chapter 3714: The Ginseng Sown Back Then (3)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3714: The Ginseng Sown Back Then (3)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","“However, there’s no telling what changes might happen. Look for a way and see if you can find a cave.”","“What kind of cave?” Feng Wu asked.","Little Phoenix said, “That mountain is in the shape of a cross. It’s very easy to recognize. Take a look.”","Feng Wu wasn’t standing very high up yet, and she could see a steep mountain peak ahead of her.","She stuffed Little Phoenix into her chest pocket and rubbed her hands. “I’ll go to the top and have a look. I can see further from there.”","Little Phoenix was concerned. “Are you sure you can do it?”","Feng Wu said, “I’m a Spiritual Lord now. This mountain won’t be a problem for me.”","Little Phoenix felt a little guilty. “If I can recover, I won’t need you to climb up and down. If you can find the cave, I’m sure I can recover.”","Feng Wu didn’t have much hope, but she still comforted Little Phoenix. “Don’t worry. I’ll find that cave for you.”","Feng Wu started climbing with her bare hands.","It was already very difficult to climb up this steep slope. To make it worse, it was covered with layers of ice.","The snow seemed to have frozen over for thousands of years and was slippery.","Luckily, Feng Wu wasn’t just any ordinary girl. She had a dagger with her, and when she needed it, she could use it to climb up the mountain.","She quickly climbed up the mountain that was thousands of meters high.","Standing on a mountain peak, Feng Wu looked into the distance.","They were in a snowfield, and there was no cover, so Feng Wu could see very far.","A cross-shaped mountain...","Feng Wu narrowed her eyes and looked around, but she didn’t see anything on the first try.","Little Phoenix was dumbfounded when it heard the news.","“No? I can’t believe it!","“What about all the ginseng I planted back then? Have they all gone missing?” Little Phoenix pressed a hand to its chest, feeling uneasy.","By the look of it, it was worse than taking its life.","Feng Wu looked at the bird in resignation. She had to admit that the bird was very good at hiding things. It had done it last time, and it had done it again this time.","Her eyes lit up all of a sudden!","“I see it. There’s indeed a mountain in the shape of a cross to the northeast, but the protruding part has been eroded by the wind, and there’s only a T left.”","That was why she didn’t notice it at first glance.","Little Phoenix was thrilled and told Feng Wu, “Quickly! Let’s go!”","Feng Wu knew that anything that could be hidden by the bird had to be good stuff, so she picked up Little Phoenix and ran in that direction.","The mountain didn’t seem very far in the snowfield, but one wouldn’t know how far it was until they started running.","It didn’t seem to get any closer.","When Feng Wu reached the mountain, it was four hours later.","Little Phoenix said, “Climb. When you’re 5,000 meters up, you’ll see a protruding rock. I planted a tree there. See if it’s still there.”","Feng Wu followed Little Phoenix’s instructions and climbed up. She stopped when she was exactly 5,000 meters up the slope.","The protruding rock was long gone, but the cave was still there.","Little Phoenix’s eyes lit up when it saw the cave. The next second, it jumped out of Feng Wu’s arms and disappeared into the cave.","“Slow down. Slow down.” Feng Wu ran after the bird as well.","The cave was pitch black at first, so dark that one couldn’t see their own fingers.. However, it didn’t last long..."]},{"number":3715,"title":"Chapter 3715: Opportunity (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3715: Opportunity (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","By Feng Wu’s estimation, they had run into the belly of the mountain, and everything suddenly opened up.","Wow...","Even Feng Wu’s eyes lit up when she saw this.","They were in an open space in the middle of the mountain. Luminous pearls the size of bowls hung above their heads.","Yes, they were indeed the size of bowls...","Any one of them could feed a family of hundreds of people for more than a lifetime. How extravagant.","Feng Wu also noticed that those hundreds of luminous pearls were arranged in a neat formation according to the stars in the sky.","What surprised her the most wasn’t the luminous pearls, but the ground beneath it.","There were rows of ginseng in the ground.","They had to be the legendary ginseng that Little Phoenix was talking about.","There was one every ten meters, and each one had six leaves. The leaves were full and dark green, and they were frighteningly big.","Feng Wu often used this kind of snow ginseng when she refined medicine, and she used all the top-grade ingredients. However, she had never seen such a big","one before.","Little Phoenix was already there. It crouched down next to the first ginseng and pulled it out.","The roots were almost ten meters long!","That ginseng was bigger than the biggest white radish Feng Wu had ever seen!","It was white and juicy and weighed at least 5 kg!","Feng Wu was astonished.","The ginseng was indeed as amazing as Little Phoenix said. It was almost a spiritual creature!","Little Phoenix bit down and tore through the ginseng’s skin.","It buried its head in and began to suck.","Feng Wu could hear the gurgling sound when the bird sucked on the ginseng.","The ginseng was drained in no time.","Little Phoenix didn’t let anything go to waste. With a wave of its sharp claws, the ginseng turned into thin stripes.","Little Phoenix stuffed the stripes into its mouth.","It only took Little Phoenix a moment to finish the ginseng.","Feng Wu was amazed.","Little Phoenix was only the size of a fist. After swallowing the ginseng, which was ten times bigger than it, it didn’t feel any discomfort at all. Right now, it was going to start on a second one.","Feng Wu sensed something in the ring space as if someone was pounding on the door.","Looking down, she saw that it was the cub.","Feng Wu could guess what the cub wanted, so she immediately released it from her ring space.","After jumping out of the ring space, the cub was even more excited than Little Phoenix. It ran toward the ginseng right away.","It did exactly the same thing as Little Phoenix. After pulling out the snow ginseng, it lowered its head and started sucking.","Feng Wu was intrigued by that slurping sound.","After eating the second one, Little Phoenix looked up and saw that Feng Wu was still standing there. It said, “Eat.”","Before Feng Wu could ask, Little Phoenix said, “I buried it back then. How many years has it been since then? It’s very potent. Eat it. It’ll help you recover your cultivation ability.”","Feng Wu was a Spiritual Elder now.","A Spiritual Elder could be considered a capable cultivator anywhere else, but Feng Wu was being chased by two peak Spiritual Overlords... So, a Spiritual Elder was nothing.","Feng Wu wished that she could become a Spiritual Overlord again.","She crouched down, copied Little Phoenix, and began to eat the snow ginseng.","One sniff and Feng Wu’s eyes lit up.","It was indeed a rare treasure!"]},{"number":3716,"title":"Chapter 3716: Opportunity (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3716: Opportunity (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Feng Wu only had to take a breath before she felt the heat travel from her throat to her dantian!","The blood origin crystal had already provided her dantian with a lot of pure and dense spiritual essence. Now that she had the ginseng...","Feng Wu felt her dantian burning!","“I’m a Spiritual Lord now.” Feng Wu was amazed and told Little Phoenix right away.","Little Phoenix nodded and went back to eating the ginseng.","One, two, three...","It was an hour later when Little Phoenix finally looked up from eating the ginseng.","By then, the cub had passed out from eating too much snowy ginseng.","Feng Wu didn’t know what to say.","Holding its plump belly, Little Phoenix burped. “Finally, I’m full...”","Feng Wu rolled her eyes. “You make it sound like I starve you all the time.”","Little Phoenix glanced at Feng Wu. “They’re not as dense as my spiritual ginseng. I planted them myself.”","Throwing the sleeping cub back into the ring space, Feng Wu sat down opposite Little Phoenix and met its gaze. The look on her face suddenly became very serious.","“What is this place?","“How could you grow that ginseng here before?”","Little Phoenix said, “Do you want to hear the truth?”","Feng Wu nodded.","Little Phoenix said, “The rumors are only half true. Many people say that this place is the tomb of my master and your beautiful master, but in fact, this is only a fake tomb.”","Feng Wu frowned. “What’s that about?”","Little Phoenix burped, and its breath smelled like ginseng.","It sounded a little drunk when it said, “Too many people in this world have been searching for Master Mu, and they all covet his cultivation technique or simply admire him. That’s why when Master Mu went missing, the world was so chaotic that many people fought with each other.","“That’s why Huyan built this place back then. He set up three doors, the Life, the Danger, and the Death so that those people would get in.”","Feng Wu frowned. ‘You tricked them into coming here just like that?”","Little Phoenix said, “Well, we didn’t exactly trick them. They were so desperate to get in that no one could stop them. All the ancestors of the four forces and nine families have been here before.”","Feng Wu asked, ‘Where are they now?”","Little Phoenix shrugged. “You won’t be able to get out once you get in.” Feng Wu looked perplexed.","Little Phoenix nodded. “That’s right. Of course, we wouldn’t let them go.” Feng Wu didn’t know what to say.","Little Phoenix said, “Many masters were trapped in this place back then, and they were from all the major families. I wonder if any of them are still alive. If they are, they can help us defeat those two villains.”","Feng Wu asked, “Will they do as you say?”","Little Phoenix smiled. “They came here for their cultivation, and no one stopped them from cultivating. If they’re still alive, they must be very capable now. Come, let’s have a look.”","Little Phoenix was in high spirits after its meal, so it took Feng Wu out with a wave of its wings.","“Hey, don’t tell them about our relationship with this tomb. Otherwise, those old men may be angry at us,” Little Phoenix warned her.","Feng Wu nodded immediately.","She was amazed. She still hadn’t digested the information.","When they came out of the cave, Feng Wu smacked her forehead.. “What about the ginseng? What if that black-robed man finds us?”"]},{"number":3717,"title":"Chapter 3717: Opportunity (3)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3717: Opportunity (3)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Little Phoenix realized the problem as well. “How about we pull them all out?”","Feng Wu’s eyes lit up.","“There’s no need to remove them all. We can leave a few left.”","Little Phoenix was dumbfounded.","However, judging by the look on Feng Wu’s face, Little Phoenix knew that their pursuer was in trouble.","As planned, Feng Wu removed most of the ginseng.","They had eaten a lot of it already, so Feng Wu only had a dozen or so left in her storage ring, and there were only two more in the ground.","As for these two...","Feng Wu had to do something to them.","But she had reason to believe that the black-robed man would fall into her trap even if he found out.","As expected, Feng Wu and Little Phoenix saw the man when they went out.","Seeing the man’s ragged clothes and bloody skin, Feng Wu smiled a little. Feng Wu was soon out of sight, and the man ran after her as fast as he could.","“Feng Wu, stop right there!”","The man was pleasantly surprised to see Feng Wu.","He had searched high and low for her, but she just so happened to be there!","He wouldn’t rest until he caught the girl!","But before he could catch up with Feng Wu, he saw the snow ginseng.","The Dongsang Kingdom had snow ginseng as well, but the man had never seen one with such a dense spiritual essence. “It’s a great ingredient,” the man drooled.","But where was Feng Wu?","She was out of sight in a split second.","The man wanted to catch Feng Wu, but he also wanted the ginseng. He hesitated.","Forget it. Feng Wu was in the snowfield, and she wouldn’t be able to get away.","He was badly injured and poisoned, so he had to use ginseng to treat his wounds.","At that thought, the man tried to pull out the ginseng that was the closest to him.","wow!","Soon, he pulled the ginseng out.","He couldn’t believe his eyes when he saw the ginseng that was over 5kg.","“That’s so rare. If I can take it to the Dongsang Kingdom, I’ll be promoted right away!” Seeing that there were two of them, the man decided to eat one and take one back.","He moved closer and sucked all the juice of the ginseng into his mouth.","That taste...","Why did it have a special fragrance?","But the man didn’t care. He thought that the nearly-spiritual snow ginseng probably tasted like this.","He tore the shriveled trunk of the ginseng into pieces, chewed on it, and swallowed it. He even washed the roots clean before swallowing them whole. He didn’t want to leave anything behind.","As for the other one...","Needless to say, he wouldn’t let it stay in the ground.","He took off his robe, dug out the ginseng, and carefully wrapped the robe around the 10-meter-long root before tying it to his back. These two ginseng alone would make the trip worthwhile.","“Feng Wu, where do you think you’re going?!”","After that, he turned his attention to Feng Wu again.","“You’re bound to leave a mark on this vast snowfield. Do you think you can get away? Tsk, tsk.” The man smirked. The next second, he set out.","No one knew how he found his way, but he was right. It was indeed the way Feng Wu left.","If Feng Wu were here, she would be very surprised.. How did the man know that she was going this way?"]},{"number":3718,"title":"Chapter 3718: Too Dangerous (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3718: Too Dangerous (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Little Phoenix knew this place like the back of its hand.","Therefore, it led Feng Wu through the snowfield after it recovered its strength. Little Phoenix said, “I remember clearly that many old masters used to live here.”","Feng Wu asked curiously, “Why are they living here?”","Little Phoenix said proudly, “Of course, it’s because of the traces left behind by my master and some incomplete manuals. As a result, they all came here like flies smelling meat.”","Feng Wu asked, “Won’t they leave after they come in?”","Little Phoenix gave Feng Wu a strange look. “Leave?”","Feng Wu said, “That’s right. Won’t they leave?”","Little Phoenix smiled again. “To do that, they have to know how to leave.”","Seeing Feng Wu’s confusion, Little Phoenix was even more pleased. “Little Yanbo and I built this place together. I was in charge of the drawings, and he took care of the construction. They can’t just walk away from the place we built together. Hmph.”","Little Yanbo? He was the most capable man in Northern Yan, but Little Phoenix had just called him “Little Yanbo”...","Soon, they reached a mountain peak.","The mountain peak wasn’t very tall. It was round and plump, and the top of the mountain was bare. There was no greenery, and the ground was covered with white snow.","Little Phoenix’s eyes lit up. “It’s right here.”","Feng Wu didn’t see any path.","Little Phoenix told Feng Wu, “Climb. When you’re loom up the slope, you’ll find a protruding stone with the pattern of a bird on it.”","Feng Wu nodded. She knew that Little Phoenix was a living navigator here, and she would do whatever it said.","Just then, Feng Wu heard a gust of wind behind her.","Feng Wu’s pupils contracted when she turned around.","The man in the black robe?","Whv was he so fast?","They were only a few kilometers apart.","With the man’s speed, he would catch up with them in no time.","“Run!” Little Phoenix cried out, and its voice wasn’t as calm as before.","The difference between Feng Wu and her opponent was simply too great.","Even at her peak, Feng Wu was only a Level-3 Spiritual Overlord.","However, the man was at the peak of the Spiritual Overlord Stage and was very close to the Spiritual Saint Stage.","Of course, Feng Wu knew that her top priority was to run as fast as she could. She didn’t know if she could get away.","Following Little Phoenix’s instructions, Feng Wu quickly reached the loom mark and began to search for a safe route.","But she couldn’t find it!","Feng Wu circled around and searched for it, but she still couldn’t find it.","The man was closing in.","Although he was injured and poisoned, he still looked terrifyingly powerful.","Feng Wu didn’t panic. Instead, she calmed down.","1000m, 500m, 300m...","The man was almost there.","Frustrated, Little Phoenix ran around in circles on Feng Wu’s head. “It’s right here. It’s within a hundred meters. I made a mark on it. 1–10w can it not be there?”","Feng Wu smacked her head all of a sudden.","“We’re on ice, and it’s very likely that the ground is way beneath us. That stone was loom above the ground before, but it may not be the case now.” Feng Wu thought of that possibility, but it was too late.","Because in a split second, the black-robed man was at the foot of the mountain.","Looking up, he saw that Feng Wu was only a hundred meters away.","The man smirked and let out a breath of relief.."]},{"number":3719,"title":"Chapter 3719: Too Dangerous (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3719: Too Dangerous (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","The man smirked.","After all the chasing, he finally caught up with her.","However, he didn’t let his guard down in the last loom. After all, he had been tricked by Feng Wu before. Therefore, he was on guard.","“Explode!”","He was about to charge out when Feng Wu threw something at him.","The man was already alarmed, so he dodged to the side.","Wait, why didn’t it explode?","The man turned around and saw the thing rolling down the cliff, but it didn’t explode.","It was a lump of snow.","The man was furious.","She was indeed a cunning girl!","The man smirked inwardly and kept climbing.","The ground was covered by loose snow, and it would take an ordinary person some time to climb up. However, the man could easily cover a distance of loom.","The next second, Feng Wu threw something down again.","“Die!” Feng Wu shouted again.","The man had been tricked once by Feng Wu and decided that he wouldn’t be fooled this time. Instead, he charged at her.","But this time...","It still looked like a snowball, but there was a bomb inside.","Not only that, but it was also a very fancy bomb!","There was a loud bang, and the snowball exploded in front of the man.","The explosion was unprecedentedly bright.","Involuntarily, he covered his eyes with his right hand to prevent them from getting hurt.","To his astonishment, the next second, the snow on the slope began to fall.","The man was indeed very capable, but he wasn’t powerful enough to defy gravity, so he began to fall with the snow. They were only a hundred meters apart...","The girl was still resisting!","The man smirked. “Kiddo, do you think that trick will work?”","Feng Wu ignored him, but she was fiddling with something.","She was very busy.","The man smirked. “How petty!”","After that, the man charged at her again.","He hadn’t exerted his full power just then, but this time, he was going to make her...","However, before he could exert his full power, he heard the sound of an avalanche.","The man cursed inwardly.","Why did it have to happen now?","And it just had to be in his position.","Looking up at Feng Wu, the man saw snow rolling down the mountain peak toward her like tidal waves.","“I can’t let her get buried!” That was the man’s first thought. The girl was so scheming that she would never be buried alive!","Hence, he rushed over and tried to grab Feng Wu.","At that critical moment!","Little Phoenix growled, “Now!”","The man watched as Feng Wu charged out at the last moment, and the bird picked her up with its beak.","The tons of snow swept toward him like a tidal wave!","He had used all his power to reach Feng Wu, so when the avalanche caught him, he was unable to escape.","Damn it!","The man finally realized that Feng Wu had set him up.","The girl had deliberately given her weakness away so that he could grab her, but as it turned out, she had tricked him!","“Damn it!!","The man was furious.","She had tricked him over and over again.."]},{"number":3720,"title":"Chapter 3720: Too Dangerous (3)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3720: Too Dangerous (3)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Infuriated, the man struck down Feng Wu.","Little Phoenix hadn’t carried Feng Wu far yet.","The man could have used his spiritual essence on himself so that he wouldn’t get hurt, but he didn’t!","He struck Feng Wu from behind.","Sensing the danger, Little Phoenix fell to the ground. Even so, Feng Wu was still severely injured.","Pffft!","Feng Wu spat out a mouthful of blood! Little Phoenix asked anxiously, “Are you alright?” “Cough, cough...”","Feng Wu coughed and couldn’t utter a word.","The avalanche had devoured the man and was coming at Feng Wu and Little Phoenix.","Little Phoenix knew that the avalanche would only stop the man for a while, so it and Feng Wu had to make sure that they were buried inside.","“Let’s go!”","Little Phoenix opened its mouth, picked Feng Wu up, and flew a few kilometers away.","But an avalanche didn’t happen in just one place. There was a chain reaction.","It had spread to other snowfields in the surrounding area.","Little Phoenix was exhausted.","It looked back in the direction it came from.","The man had been completely buried.","However, the road leading to those capable cultivators had been buried as well, and they couldn’t get in to ask for help even if they wanted to. Infuriated, Little Phoenix shouted, “That man is abominable!”","The avalanche hadn’t ended yet.","The snow was moving up and down as if it was going to devour everything!","Little Phoenix panicked and was scared out of its wits.","Before Feng Wu hit the ground, Little Phoenix swooped down, picked her up, and flew into the sky.","It had been hit by the man’s last strike as well and was in pain all over. Luckily, it had swallowed a lot of snow ginseng earlier, and the medicine was quickly taking effect, repairing its body.","Little Phoenix carried Feng Wu all the way out of the snowfield until they reached a dense forest.","Exhausted, Little Phoenix couldn’t take it anymore. It fell to the ground and fainted.","Feng Wu had been unconscious, to begin with. Her head was bleeding from the impact, but it didn’t wake her up either.","No one knew how much time had passed after that.","The hot sunlight slowly woke Feng Wu up.","Involuntarily, she covered her eyes with her hands, and it took her a while to open them again. She then saw an old tree.","Where was this place?","Feng Wu sat up involuntarily, but the pain made her grunt.","That hurt!","It wasn’t just her chest, but her back as well...","Feng Wu recalled what happened before she fainted.","Back then, she had tricked the man, but the angry man had also hit her from behind. She was on the verge of collapsing, and there was an avalanche. Little Phoenix had carried her all the way.","Where was Little Phoenix?","Looking around, Feng Wu soon saw a meter-long colorful bird lying on its back.","It was very quiet and didn’t seem to be breathing.","Feng Wu immediately went up to Little Phoenix and checked its breathing.","Luckily, it was breathing, but there was little sign of life.","“Wake up, wake up!”","Feng Wu poured some Semi-divine potion into Little Phoenix’s mouth.","Little Phoenix slowly opened its eyes when it heard Feng Wu’s voice. It was relieved to see her.","With that, it relaxed and fainted for good.","Feng Wu didn’t know what to say.."]},{"number":3721,"title":"Chapter 3721: Too Dangerous (4)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3721: Too Dangerous (4)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Luckily, its life wasn’t in danger.","Putting Little Phoenix back into her ring space, Feng Wu rose to her feet and looked around.","She could sense something.","Someone was watching her with a dangerous look in their eyes.","Feng Wu wasn’t doing well at the moment. She had severe internal injuries and couldn’t withstand any more blows... However, her life was in danger, and she had no other choice.","The intimidating feeling grew stronger. Feng Wu gripped her Fallen Star Sword.","Whoosh!","All of a sudden, someone charged at her.","It was too fast for Feng Wu to react!","Feng Wu had been prepared for this and dodged to the side.","When she looked again, she finally saw what it was.","It was indeed a big guy!","Feng Wu recognized it right away. It was a Fire Cloud White Lion!","The lion was at least a peak Spiritual Lord.","Feng Wu almost had a heart attack. She had recovered to the Spiritual Lord Stage, but the man had injured her, and she could only exert the power of a Spiritual Elder now.","She wasn’t the lion’s match.","What a pity. If Little Phoenix had been here, it would have been able to intimidate the lion. Unfortunately, it was too severely injured and had passed out.","Before, Feng Wu could have killed the lion with one strike, but now, it was the other way around,","The lion stared at Feng Wu with a resolute look in its eyes, which was filled with murderous intention.","It wanted to kill her...","Feng Wu could sense that the lion was going to kill her.","If she couldn’t defeat the lion, she would have to outsmart it.","Feng Wu stared into the lion’s eyes. She wasn’t intimidated at all. Instead, she was filled with a fighting spirit.","Because if she gave in, she would be dead for sure. Feng Wu quickly scanned the lion from the corner of her eye.","wait!","She saw a streak of red on the side of the lion.","It was blood.","The lion was injured?","Feng Wu shook her head inwardly. The lion wasn’t injured. It wasn’t his blood.","Could that blood be the result of the lion devouring its prey?","Feng Wu rejected that idea again.","If the blood came from its prey, the blood should be on the corner of its mouth or its front paws. It was very unlikely that there was blood on its sides.","So, it was very likely...","“Is your friend injured?” Feng Wu narrowed her eyes and stared at the lion. “Are they badly injured and dying?","The lion was going to kill the human prey, but it was surprised by Feng Wu’s words.","Feng Wu was only trying to sound it out. After that, she kept her gaze on the lion, trying to see the look on its face.","As expected, the look on the lion’s face changed a little.","Feng Wu’s stomach lurched. “I see that your wife is the one who’s injured!”","As a majestic male lion, it wouldn’t stay with other male lions. The only one that could live with it was probably a female lion.","The lion kept its cold gaze on Feng Wu without saying a word.","Feng Wu said, “You should know that here are great human doctors, and I’m one of the best in the human race. I can help you.”","The lion eyed Feng Wu suspiciously.","Seeing that it wouldn’t believe her, Feng Wu raised her right hand, and a streak of green light flew toward the lion.."]},{"number":3722,"title":"Chapter 3722: Midwife","paragraphs":["Chapter 3722: Midwife","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","The lion stared at Feng Wu with an indecipherable look in its eyes.","Feng Wu stared back at it. “I’m the only one who can save your kin. Otherwise, it’s going to die.","“I have some food if you’re short of it.” With a wave of her hand, a pile of fresh food rolled out of her ring space.","They were chunks of fresh beef.","Together, they weighed hundreds of kilograms.","The lion looked from Feng Wu to the beef on the ground and nodded at her.","It also told Feng Wu to put away the food and take it out when they got there.","Feng Wu knew perfectly well that the avalanche wouldn’t bury the man for long, so she had to leave as soon as possible.","She followed the lion into a dry cave.","When they got there, Feng Wu saw another lion lying in the cave. It was covered in blood, and there was a lot of blood on the ground as well.","Feng Wu went up to the female lion in a hurry. One look and she knew what it was.","“It’s not just an injury. It’s difficult labor.” Feng Wu looked at the lion. “She’s pregnant, and the cub’s legs are facing out. That’s why she can’t give birth.” The male lion ran around in circles and bellowed at Feng Wu.","Feng Wu said, “Has she been injured before? Did she roll off a snow mountain?” The lion nodded.","Feng Wu said, “Luckily, you ran into me. Otherwise, you would have lost two lives. No, four, because she’s pregnant with three cubs.”","This was the first time that the male lion had heard of that, and it was baffling.","Feng Wu said affirmatively, “Be careful when you’re pregnant with three cubs. You’re all so careless.”","Feng Wu put her hand on the female lion’s belly. Emerald spiritual essence flowed out of her fingertips and jumped around.","The lion was barely breathing after the blood loss, but it soon regained some of its vitality.","But it was still on guard.","Animals were instinctively on guard against humans.","Feng Wu comforted it. “Don’t worry. I don’t need to cut you open to take the cub out. We’ll go with the flow.”","Feng Wu turned the first cub around so that its head was facing the exit. Only then did she tell the female lion, “Save your strength and give birth to it in one go. One, two, three!”","The female lion could understand what Feng Wu meant. She didn’t trust humans at first, but there was something soft in Feng Wu’s eyes that made her trust her.","Just then, the first cub came out.","Feng Wu let out a breath of relief. She had never given birth to a magical beast before and had to work as if she was delivering human babies.","Feng Wu gave the cub to the mother lion.","The lion burst into tears when it saw the cub.","Feng Wu said, “Keep up the good work. There are two more.”","As she spoke, she took out a recoverv D0tion and fed it to the lion.","The lion no longer looked at ???????? with caution and trusted her a lot.","Before long, the second and third cubs came out, and both were very healthy.","Feng Wu stuffed the three cubs between the lion’s forelegs and rose to her feet.","The male lion looked at her uneasily and was about to say something when Feng Wu waved at it. “She’s no longer in danger, and that’s all I can do. If someone asks you about it, don’t tell them that you’ve met me. Otherwise, they’ll kill you..”"]},{"number":3723,"title":"Chapter 3723: Contingency","paragraphs":["Chapter 3723: Contingency","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Feng Wu turned to leave the cave after that. Something then occurred to her, and she asked the lion, “Where were you injured?”","The lion was very grateful for Feng Wu’s help, so it led the way.","Feng Wu followed the lion to a cliff.","She looked around, and her eyes lit up.","She said to the lion, ‘You can go back now. You should keep the cave safe.” The lion suddenly bent its front legs and knelt down in front of Feng Wu. It then turned to leave.","“Magical beasts can be more grateful than humans sometimes,” Feng Wu sighed inwardly.","“You’ve been staring at this mountain. Do you have a plan?” Little Phoenix came out of Feng Wu’s sleeve.","Feng Wu glanced at it. “Have you rested enough?”","Little Phoenix nodded at Feng Wu. “I’ll be fine for now.”","Little Phoenix looked at Feng Wu up and down. “I see that you’re going to set someone up again.”","Feng Wu chuckled.","Little Phoenix had to hand it to Feng Wu. She was still in the mood to trick other people.","“We’ll have a much better chance if we run now,” Little Phoenix reminded Feng wu.","Feng Wu shook her head. “That man has to die. Otherwise, I’ll never be able to get away from him.”","Little Phoenix looked at Feng Wu in bewilderment. “Are you saying that he...”","Feng Wu nodded solemnly. “I suspect that he has a special way to track me. No matter where I go, he’ll catch up with me. So, if he’s not dead, we won’t be able to get away.”","Little Phoenix sighed.","Before, the bird wouldn’t have to be afraid of that man at all. One strike and the man would be dead. But now...","Little Phoenix looked at Feng Wu. “How confident are you?”","Feng Wu said seriously, “I wasn’t sure at first, but after seeing the terrain here, I think I have a 20% chance.”","“20%? That’s too little!” Little Phoenix objected.","Feng Wu said, “That lioness fell down from here, but it’s not dead. Let’s go have a look. Maybe there’s a surprise in the terrain down there.”","After falling for a few hundred meters, Feng Wu saw a protruding stone platform.","It was at least five meters wide and thick.","It was stained with the lion’s blood.","Looking around, raised her eyebrows a little. She was 20% more confident now.","Before long, Feng Wu looked around and told Little Phoenix, “I’m 60% confident now. I have to give it a go. I can’t keep running like this.”","Seeing that Feng Wu wouldn’t give up, Little Phoenix said in resignation, “We’ll give it a go, but we still have to run. Don’t forget that my master’s life depends on you.”","Feng Wu patted her chest. “Don’t worry. I cherish my life more than you think.”","Before the black-robed man arrived, Feng Wu started working on the formation.","She Imew better than anyone else that the man in black would catch up with her.","One, two, three, four, five... Because of the good location, Feng Wu had made more than five backup plans.","All the poisons, bombs, and other resources she had accumulated in her ring space were used up this time.","She hoped that with all the arrangements, she would be able to trap the man for good.."]},{"number":3724,"title":"Chapter 3724: Caught up Again","paragraphs":["Chapter 3724: Caught up Again","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","As soon as Feng Wu made the last preparations, a gust of wind blew, and the black-robed man appeared in front of her.","Feng Wu didn’t know what to say.","Feng Wu was right in front of the man, and behind her was an abyss.","The atmosphere suddenly became very tense.","If the man stepped forward and gave Feng Wu a little push, Feng Wu would fall into the abyss and disappear forever.","It was obvious that the man thought the same. He grinned maliciously and took a step forward.","Feng Wu feigned a panicked tone. “Stop right there! Don’t come any closer!”","The man smirked at Feng Wu’s reaction.","“You didn’t see it coming, did you?” The man laughed.","Feng Wu glared at her. “Stop right there!”","The man took another step forward and smirked at Feng Wu. “Didn’t you say you were going to run? Run!”","Feng Wu didn’t know what to say.","The man said, “But you’re really good at running. You found the underground river and accidentally entered the tomb. I didn’t expect you to get this far.” Because Feng Wu was right here, the man wanted to tell her everything.","Feng Wu had been giving him a hard time.","Feng Wu said, “I...’","She stepped back, and a gust of wind blew at her from behind. Her clothes flapped in the wind, as if she was going to fall off the cliff at any moment.","Her face was ghastly pale, and she looked like she had lost all hope and didn’t know what to do.","The man noticed that although the girl still looked stubborn, she had clenched her fists so tight that her knuckles had turned white.","“So, you’re scared now.” He stared at the girl, who was only a meter away from him.","Feng Wu raised her head. “I’m not afraid!”","The smirk on the man’s face grew more obvious. “If you’re not afraid, why are you trembling?”","Feng Wu didn’t know what to say.","The man sighed. “Why are you so stupid? If you hadn’t run away, I could have brought you back to the Dongsang Kingdom and handed you to Mr. Sakiya. No matter what happens after that, you’ll still be alive. “You shouldn’t have tried to run away. You’ve given us a lot of trouble.” “I’m alright, but I still have a superior. He’ll be mad at me.","“Do you know how much manpower the Dongsang Kingdom has mobilized to catch you? You have no idea.","“I would love to take you back alive, but you’re so slippery. Even if I knock you out and carry you back, I’m worried that you’ll wake up earlier and poison me on our way back!”","There was a ferocious look on the man’s face.","“You’re a poisonous girl! You’re so good at poisoning people! If I hadn’t reached the peak of the Spiritual Overlord Stage, I would have been killed by now!”","The man glared at Feng Wu. “Even if I’m a peak Spiritual Overlord, you’ve still poisoned me to the point that I only have half of my power. How vicious can you be? I can’t let you live!”","The man took another step forward.","Feng Wu took a deep breath. “I’m more useful alive than dead. Won’t you consider that?”","The man smirked. “You’ll be more obedient to me when you’re dead. Die!”","Feng Wu said, “In that case...” After that, she fell backward.","It was like bungee jumping!"]},{"number":3725,"title":"Chapter 3725: The Poisonous Girl","paragraphs":["Chapter 3725: The Poisonous Girl","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","The man paled.","Feng Wu was falling into the abyss!","The order was very clear. He had to bring her back, dead or alive!","The man needed Feng Wu’s dead body to make up for his mistake. He wouldn’t let her fall.","Hence, he reached out involuntarily to grab Feng Wu.","But he couldn’t catch her. All he could catch was the lower hem of her clothes.","And the cloth..","It was poisonous!","Argh! The man wanted to scream.","Caught off guard, he was stabbed in the palm!","There wasn’t much blood, but her poison would seep into the wound!","Moreover, the cliff was so close that the man could fall into it if he wasn’t careful.","The man watched as Feng Wu fell. Unable to catch her, he was about to jump in to find her body, but the next moment...","There was a loud bang!","The ground under the man’s feet shattered.","Some unknown liquid splashed onto the man’s legs.","The man cursed inwardly. What a vicious girl. She still had that trick up her sleeves.","Half of the cliff had been blown up, and the man had nowhere to stand, so he couldn’t stop the fall.","As for the thing that had splashed on his feet, the man didn’t feel any discomfort, so he ignored it for the time being.","How many toxins had the girl thrown out along the way? She probably didn’t have anything lethal left. She was probably just trying to scare him.","The falling man didn’t think much of the slime on his feet.","The ground below was covered by thick fog, and visibility was very poor.","The man didn’t notice Feng Wu.","Had the girl fallen to the ground and died?","However, he couldn’t care less about Feng Wu now, for he wasn’t doing well either.","Both sides of the cliff were covered by loose snow, and the man couldn’t stop himself even if he wanted to. He kept falling.","However, the man was able to withstand the fall.","He dug his fingers into the cliff to steady himself.","But...","Why did the snow feel different? The man’s eyes lit up before he had time to think.","He saw a protruding stone platform a few hundred meters below.","Although it was covered by a thick fog, he couldn’t be mistaken.","He quickly landed on the stone platform.","However...","As soon as he set foot on the stone platform, something stuck to his feet.","He wanted to lift his foot but couldn’t.","He then remembered something.","He didn’t care about the slime on his feet before, but now, something was","wrong!","His feet were stuck to the stone platform, and he couldn’t move a muscle.","The man wanted to take off his boots.","However...","He would have been fine if he had taken off his boots from the very beginning, but the slime had seeped into the soles of his feet and glued them together. He couldn’t separate his feet from his boots, so of course, he couldn’t take them off.","That wasn’t all.","Feng Wu had designed a series of traps, and of course, she wouldn’t give the man any break.","Whoosh!","A storm of needles struck down at the man.","The man was furious.","Feng Wu was such a poisonous girl! Damn it!"]},{"number":3726,"title":"Chapter 3726: Feng WII’s Tricks","paragraphs":["Chapter 3726: Feng WII’s Tricks","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","“What a poisonous girl!”","The man bellowed inwardly.","He thought he had overestimated the girl, but as it turned out, she hadn’t started yet.","The man stood there, looking like a sitting duck.","Countless needles poured down at his head from the tree on the left and the cliff on the right.","The black-robed man’s defensive shield had been worn down by Feng Wu’s poison over and over again, and there was only a thin layer left. It wasn’t something that could be recovered instantly.","As a result, the needles that shouldn’t have been able to injure him began to sting him like a death warrant.","He could handle most of the needles, but...","What if a venomous snake jumped out of nowhere?","No one knew where Feng Wu found the hibernating snake, but judging by its sharp fangs, it was very venomous!","The thin snake crawled into the man’s trousers and slithered all the way up.","The man was indeed a capable cultivator, but no matter how capable he was, Feng Wu had worn him out on their way here. Moreover, he had been immobilized and was surrounded by needles. He was overwhelmed! Hence, the snake moved all the way up until it found the man’s softest part.","The man stiffened. What was that?","He was only distracted for a moment before he was pricked in the face by several needles. Luckily, they didn’t go into his eyes. When he reached for his softest part, he felt a sharp pain.","“Argh!!!”","The man screamed in pain.","This was the saddest battle the man had ever fought with Feng Wu because he realized that he had been bitten by a venomous snake in his private part.","Although he had caught the snake and crushed it to death, the wound wouldn’t disappear.","He felt a numbing sensation in his groin. It was painful and itchy at the same time, and he felt awful.","Was he poisoned? The man wanted to throw up.","Just then, an arrow flew at him!","An arrows?","Where did that arrow come from?","Looking up, he saw a red figure shooting arrows at him from a cliff in the distance.","That slender figure in red... The man found it rather familiar and almost blurted out a name!","But he refused to believe it because he would look like a fool if he did.","That arrow had distracted him. That was why he had been bitten by that venomous snake!","Just then, more arrows came at him again!","Three shots in a row!","The man thought his lungs were going to explode.","It was her!","It was Feng Wu!","She really wasn’t dead!","Not only wasn’t she dead, but she had also set up so many traps for him, which he had foolishly jumped into!","Recalling what he said to Feng Wu, the man felt utterly foolish.","Argh!!!","The man flew into a rage out of humiliation.","What he didn’t notice was that when he lost his temper, countless ants had climbed onto his back.","When he realized what had happened, he was covered in ants.."]},{"number":3727,"title":"Chapter 3727: Feng Wu l s Tricks (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3727: Feng Wu l s Tricks (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","There were so many cuts on his body, and ants loved the smell he gave off.","It was Feng Wu! It was her doing again! !!","Did she think these ants could hurt him? That was ridiculous!","With a wave of his hand, the black-robed man sent a streak of green flame out of his body. Immediately, the ants that had climbed onto him were reduced to ashes... They were all dead.","The man smirked. What a petty trick!","However, as soon as he said that, he realized that his wounds were itchy.","It was getting more and more itchy. Even with his willpower, he could barely control it.","He immediately took off his robe. One look and he felt a chill run down his spine.","The wounds on his body began to turn red and swollen, and pus was seeping out.","That wasn’t all. If the wounds were his only problem, he could always cut into his own flesh to treat his wounds, but... Since when did his body turn blue?","It was so itchy...","The man was so frustrated that he felt itchy all over.","As powerful as he was, he couldn’t stop the sensation.","Although he didn’t know how Feng Wu was able to get back to the cliff after falling, he had decided to fly back up.","Moreover, with his capability, he could easily fly back up the cliff.","However, when he stomped his foot and was about to fly up, he suddenly remembered...","No.","His boots were stuck to the ground, and he couldn’t fly.","The man was furious.","With a sudden movement, he directed his spiritual essence toward the stone platform beneath him.","He wanted to take the stone platform up with him.","Under normal circumstances, he could do it because he was a peak Spiritual Overlord. But now...","He was dragged down by a force.","Looking down, he saw that a lot of iron had been tied to the stone platform.","The iron block dragged him down the cliff, and he couldn’t keep his balance in mid-air.","For right now, the man’s feet were stuck to the stone platform, and he was falling down with it as if he was riding on clouds.","This time, he really panicked.","Whoosh!","Another arrow flew at him.","Only then did he notice that one of Feng Wu’s feet had been tied to a rope.","In a split second, he figured it out.","He had thought that Feng Wu had fallen off the cliff, but that wasn’t the case!","Feng Wu’s leg was held by that rope, which stopped her from the fall. She could then climb up like a little monkey with the help of the rope.","He, on the other hand, had been completely fooled by Feng Wu!","The man gritted his teeth and stared at Feng Wu. He was so angry that he couldn’t think straight.","wait!","The man smacked his head. How could he have forgotten?","Since he was able to remove the stone platform from the cliff, he should be able to break it as well!","Without the falling stone and the giant chunk of iron under it, he would be able to get back up on his own.","What happened was quicker than words could describe!","The black-robed activated his spiritual essence.","“Explode!”","Having been tricked by Feng Wu for so long, the man had less than 30% of his capability left, but he was still a capable cultivator. Hence, he cracked the stone.","However...","Feng Wu had anticipated that as well.","When the man used his spiritual essence to blow up the stone, white smoke rose from it.."]},{"number":3728,"title":"Chapter 3728: Feng Wu’s Tricks (3)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3728: Feng Wu’s Tricks (3)","Translator: Henvee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","The man was surrounded by white smoke.","He panicked.","What was that?!","Was the white mist poisonous?","Because Feng Wu had tricked him so many times, he could only hold his breath and didn’t dare to activate his spiritual essence.","Because once it was activated, the toxin would circulate in his system at an even faster speed!","Without activating his spiritual essence...","He had no choice but to fall.","He spotted a suspension bridge a short distance away.","All he needed to do was stand on it, and he would be safe for a while!","The man hated Feng Wu more than words could describe. He made a mental note that as soon as he could find his footing, he would take his revenge on Feng Wu.","He wouldn’t give Feng Wu any chance!","The man stood on the suspension bridge in expectation, but...","He didn’t even have time to heave a sigh of relief.","Sizzle!","An unknown electric current came from one end of the suspension bridge.","The man was electrocuted before he had time to react.","The electric current was so strong that there were sparks everywhere.","The man stiffened and was dumbfounded.","What was going on?","What on earth was going on?!","His first reaction was that the suspension bridge had been tampered with as well.","He was right, but Feng Wu didn’t have time to test it. She didn’t expect the electric current to be so strong.","Feng Wu was elated when she saw the man’s face turn black.","She hoped it would work this time.","However, the man was at the peak of the Spiritual Overlord Stage, and Feng Wu was indeed much weaker than him. Therefore, she had underestimated him.","In a moment of life and death, the man broke his own leg.","Yes, he had shattered his leg from the knee down!","He finally rolled off the suspension bridge and fell all the way down!","He wouldn’t survive if he was stuck on the suspension bridge. He would be electrocuted to death!","Maybe he still had a chance now.","The man thought, “After everything she’s done, she must have run out of tricks!”","Seeing the relieved look on the man’s face, Feng Wu smiled.","Running out of tricks? Not necessarily!","Just then, Feng Wu saw the man fall toward an old tree.","The tree was hundreds of meters tall, and ten people could wrap their arms around it.","Seeing the old tree, the man tried his best to move in its direction. The tree could offset most of the falling momentum so that he wouldn’t be so badly injured.","But...","It had never occurred to him that Feng Wu would have more tricks up her sleeves.","She could do more!","Black mist scattered when the man fell into the old tree.","The man was too dizzy to notice the black mist, but soon, he heard a buzzing sound.","What was that?","He opened his eyes with much difficulty and looked around. One look and he was filled with despair.","The buzzing sound came from the big black wasps!","There were tens of thousands of them, and they were all staring at the man.","The man felt something sticky behind him. When he touched it, he saw that it was a yellow hive that he had destroyed, as well as a wasp queen!","The man looked terrified.."]},{"number":3729,"title":"Chapter 3729: Feng Wu l s Tricks (4)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3729: Feng Wu l s Tricks (4)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","As a peak Spiritual Overlord, he shouldn’t be afraid of the big black wasps at all, but now...","He was covered with cuts and bruises, and his internal injuries were severe. Both his legs were broken at the knees, and he was drained of spiritual essence...","He had suppressed the toxin in his body, but now...","He had stirred up a wasp’s nest!","The man wanted to run.","But he had lost his legs. How was he supposed to run?","Buzz!!!","The wasps were furious!","Their only queen was crushed just like that!","Tens of thousands of wasps charged at the man.","Feng Wu was quickly climbing down with the help of the rope. When she reached the bottom, she saw the man being attacked by the big black wasps.","The man was frustrated.","He was a peak Spiritual Overlord...","The wasps were very poisonous, and they all stuck their stingers into the man.","While the big black wasps were poisoning the man, the toxin in him exploded as well.","Therefore, the man killed the big black wasps in an instant, leaving only cold stingers in his body. The rest of the wasps fell to the ground and died.","Soon, the ground was covered with dead big black wasps.","They were half the height of a grown man.","The look gave Feng Wu the creeps, so she turned to look at the man.","The man was in a miserable state.","He was hanging from the tree at first, but he had already fallen to the ground.","His face was dark, and his skin was as black as ink. He was covered with cuts and bruises, and his legs were missing from his knees down. Even the blood that was oozing out was black.","The toxin was so potent.","When Feng Wu stood there, the man slowly opened his eyes. The moment he saw Feng Wu, he was furious.","“You!!!”","The man coughed violently and spat out blood.","Feng Wu knew that it was because the man had run out of spiritual essence and couldn’t suppress the toxin anymore.","“You deserve to die!” The man stared at Feng Wu, spat out a mouthful of blood, and closed his eyes.","Feng Wu didn’t know what to say.","She took a few steps forward and stopped when she was a few meters away from the man.","“Wait, is that man really dead?” Rubbing her chin, Feng Wu asked in bewilderment.","The man lay there, motionless.","Feng Wu didn’t go any closer. Instead, she walked around the man and murmured, “Is he really dead?","“Since you’re already dead, I’ll burn your body for you. It’ll save you from getting exposed.”","Feng Wu got to work right away.","Orange flames came out of her fingertips and landed on the man.","The man still didn’t move.","Behind the man were big black wasps, which were easy to set on fire. The flames immediately surrounded the man.","Right at that moment...","The dead man jumped into the air and charged at Feng Wu.","“Then let’s die together!”","He could no longer see, but he could still sense where Feng Wu was.","What he didn’t know was that Feng Wu already knew that he was faking it.","Everyone had terminal lucidity, and Feng Wu wasn’t going to test how a peak Spiritual Overlord would react. She had long hidden herself.."]},{"number":3730,"title":"Chapter 3730: He l s Finally Dead (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3730: He l s Finally Dead (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","When the man charged at her, Feng Wu stuffed a log she had prepared into his arms.","The man only had one chance.","He thought that he had caught Feng Wu, so he punched the object coming at him.","There was a loud thump!","The log was pulverized.","The man used his only chance. He swayed and fell to the ground.","There was a loud thump!","The impact created a human-shaped pit in the ground, and he was completely submerged.","Only then did Feng Wu walk out from behind a big tree and slowly walk up to the man.","Lying in the pit, the man stared at Feng Wu but couldn’t utter a word.","Feng Wu noticed that he was shaking from head to toe, and his lips were trembling as if he wanted to say something.","Feng Wu crouched down next to him and sighed. “Why did you have to come after me? Why did you come all the way from the Dongsang Kingdom just to die thousands of kilometers away from home?","“You’re a peak Spiritual Overlord. Aren’t vou ashamed to be killed by me?” “Pffft!”","The man spat out the last mouthful of black blood and stared at Feng Wu. “Do you think the Dongsang Kingdom is the only one after you? Hahaha!” He was finally dead after that.","With a wave of Feng Wu’s hand, a streak of flame landed on the man, which immediately engulfed him.","Just then, Little Phoenix cried out.","“Let’s go!”","Before Feng Wu could ask, Little Phoenix said anxiously, “There’s another person after you. He has broken through the Death door. Run!”","The silver-masked man!","Feng Wu’s stomach lurched!","“He’s not dead?”","Little Phoenix nodded. “Not only that, but I also feel that he’s even more powerful than before!”","Feng Wu was astonished. Little Phoenix urged her again. “Let’s go! ”","Feng Wu asked, “Where?”","Little Phoenix said, “I know a secret passageway that leads to the Northern Yan","Kingdom and another one to the Junwu Empire. Which one do you want to go","Feng Wu couldn’t help but recall what the man said at the end. “People of the Dongsang Kingdom aren’t the only ones after you.” So, who else was after her?","Feng Wu recalled the families she had offended...","Was it possible...","Feng Wu said, “We’re going to Northern Yan.”","This time, Feng Wu decided to blend in until she met up with Jun Linyuan at the Northern Yan Palace.","“Let’s go to Northern Yan, then,” Little Phoenix agreed. “Little Yanbo has the final say. As long as we get in touch with him, no matter who comes, we’ll kill them all!”","Feng Wu cleared her throat. Meeting up with Jun Linyuan will have the same effect, but Jun Linyuan was so elusive now that she didn’t know where to find him.","“That person is here!” Little Phoenix reminded Feng Wu. “Let’s go west!”","Little Phoenix gave the hall a regretful look. There were a lot of good stuff here, but Feng Wu was still too weak. It would wait until she was stronger.","Little Phoenix took Feng Wu to the west. As soon as they disappeared into the woods, someone showed up.","Little Phoenix was right. It was indeed the silver-masked man.","He saw a body on fire, which made him think that it was Feng Wu. He quickly went up to the spot.."]},{"number":3731,"title":"Chapter 3731: He’s Finally Dead (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3731: He’s Finally Dead (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","What he saw astonished him.","It wasn’t Feng Wu’s body, but...","“Blackie!” With a wave of his hand, the silver-masked man doused the fire with a streak ot rainwater.","He rushed over and pulled the body out.","It was indeed Blackie!","When he checked the man’s breathing, he realized that the latter was no longer breathing, and there was no pulse either.","The man was long dead, and most of his body had been burnt to a crisp.","The silver-masked man’s face twisted, and there was a cold look in his eyes.","Feng wu!","It had to be her!","He looked around, but Feng Wu was nowhere to be found.","After killing Blackie, she was able to get away without leaving a trace. How could someone as weak as her do that?","The silver-masked man wouldn’t believe it. He began to examine his surroundings.","He kept searching until he reached the edge of the cliff.","Looking down the cliff, he deduced what the black-robed man had gone through..","The silver-masked man took a deep breath.","“Mr. Sakiya, you told me to be on guard against that girl, but you didn’t tell me how evil she could be!”","A chill ran down his spine.","A girl so much weaker than Blackie had slowly killed him...","The silver-masked man took a deep breath. It seemed that his judgment of the girl had to change again.","If she could slowly kill Blackie, she could probably do the same to him.","Once the silver-masked man calmed down, he began to examine Feng Wu’s footprints.","She had to leave a trace behind.","But Little Phoenix had taken Feng Wu away, so there were no footprints, which frustrated the man.","His eyes lit up all of a sudden.","Meanwhile, Feng Wu had flown out of the hall, led by Little Phoenix.","According to Little Phoenix, the silver-masked man couldn’t take anything away from this place. Even if he could, Huyan Yanbo would kill him later.","Little Phoenix kept urging Feng Wu. “We’ll be fine when we get to Northern","Yan. Let’s go!”","Under Little Phoenix’s instruction, Feng Wu quietly left the tomb hall.","When Feng Wu came out of the water, she found herself in the middle of a wide river.","The river bank was dozens of meters to her left.","Before Feng Wu could reach the shore, she heard a cry for help a short distance away.","“Help! Help us!”","Looking up, Feng Wu saw a dying boy pressing down on the girl behind him, while he craned his neck upward.","Feng Wu knew perfectly well that the boy had lost all his senses and reason. All he could do now was struggle as if he was grasping at straws.","The boy was only five or six years old, and the girl was only in her teens.","Right now, the little girl was being held down by the boy’s struggle, and she couldn’t breathe... She couldn’t hold on much longer.","Feng Wu went up to them and lifted them out of the water.","Instinctively, they struggled with all their strength, but Feng Wu was able to pull them ashore.","Once they were ashore, Feng Wu saw a group of people running toward them, one of them holding a little boy."]},{"number":3732,"title":"Chapter 3732: Rescue (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3732: Rescue (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Feng Wu could hear the boy crying. “Uncle, I really didn’t push Xiaoshu into the river. He wanted to catch the fish himself, and Sister Sanya jumped in to save him. I don’t know what happened...”","Then, they saw Feng Wu come ashore with the two children.","The middle-aged man rushed over and snatched the two kids from Feng Wu’s arms.","“Xiaoshu! Xiaoshu!”","“Sanya! Sanya!”","No matter how loudly he shouted, the two children didn’t move and kept their eyes shut.","The man almost pushed Feng Wu to the ground, but judging by how nervous he was, he was probably their father.","Feng Wu dried her clothes with her spiritual essence. When she looked up again, she saw that the middle-aged man was wiping away his tears. Next to him, a few others were all weeping and trying to comfort him.","Condolences?","Feng Wu walked up to them and frowned. “They’re not dead yet.”","Immediately, all eyes were on Feng Wu.","Only then did Feng Wu notice their shabby clothes. They looked no better than beggars.","But that wasn’t the point. She said, “They’re not dead yet. Why condolences?”","The middle-aged man was speechless. A younger man glanced at Feng Wu and said, “Who are you? What are you talking about? They’re dead!”","The father pulled the young man away. “Calm down. She’s the one who fished","Xiaoshu and Sanya out of the river.”","Everyone saw that, so the younger man didn’t say anything else, but he still gave Feng Wu a stern look.","Wiping away his tears, the father bowed at Feng Wu. “Miss, thank you for what you did!”","Feng Wu saw him bend down, and his tears fell into the mud.","Feng Wu didn’t know what to say.","She knew what was the most important thing to this father.","Feng Wu didn’t want to take action at first, for doing so would only delay her. Moreover, if she used her spiritual essence to save the kids, the silver-masked man might be able to track her.","Little Phoenix had been urging Feng Wu to leave.","But Feng Wu couldn’t bring herself to do it.","For a father to lose two children in one day... Feng Wu shook her head and told the man, “I can save them.”","The others looked at one another in bewilderment before giving Feng Wu strange looks.","Save them?","But the two kids had stopped breathing.","The boy was in a worse condition, so Feng Wu decided to save him first.","Feng Wu didn’t have any medicine left. She didn’t have any venom left because she had used it all on the black-robed man. Therefore, all she could use now was the Supreme Level essence of the plant.","Feng Wu opened her right hand, and a streak of green light flowed out of her fingertips. It then jumped onto the little book, lingered on him, and slowly seeped into his body.","Feng Wu knew that these people were all ordinary people with no spiritual essence and couldn’t understand her moves, so she didn’t try to avoid them.","Meanwhile, everyone was looking at Feng Wu in amazement.","No acupuncture and no medicine. Did she think she could bring back the dead by opening her palm? Who was she kidding? The younger man snorted.","Meanwhile, the others frowned as well.. That was so preposterous!"]},{"number":3733,"title":"Chapter 3733: Rescue (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3733: Rescue (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","No one believed that Feng Wu could save the kids, so they all frowned.","Feng Wu injected the essence into the Xiaoshu, and after a short while, she couldn’t inject anymore.","The rest of the essence jumped onto Sanya.","It slowly disappeared into her mouth and nose.","“What did you do to them?!” The younger man stared at Feng Wu. “You’re not allowed to...","However, before he could finish, he saw Xiaoshu, who had closed his eyes and wasn’t breathing or having a heartbeat, moving his eyes a little.","The father had been watching Xiaoshu the whole time, so he reacted quickly.","He grabbed Xiaoshu and was so excited. “Xiaoshu, you’re awake! Xiaoshu!","Xiaoshu!”","The boy opened his eyes and looked at his father in bewilderment. Tears welled up in the father’s eyes as he held the boy in his arms. “My son!” His brother stared at Feng Wu in astonishment, as if he had seen a ghost.","“You!","“How could you...","“How did you do it?”","They had seen with their own eyes that Xiaoshu was no longer breathing.","Feng Wu glanced at the children’s uncle but didn’t say anything.","Recalling his attitude toward the girl, the uncle blushed.","He looked at Sanya and sighed inwardly. Xiaoshu was alive, but Sanya...","Well, at least one of them was still alive.","Before he could finish sighing, Sanya opened her eyes.","“Argh!” The uncle had been staring at Sanya the whole time, and he jumped when he saw this.","“You!” The uncle pointed at Sanya in astonishment.","Rubbing her eyes, Sanya looked at her uncle in bewilderment, but she soon realized what was going on. “Uncle! Help me save Xiaoshu! Quickly!”","After that, she dragged her uncle toward the river.","“Sister! ”","Xiaoshu jumped out of his father’s arms and threw himself at Sanya.","Seeing Xiaoshu, Sanya was dumbfounded. “Am I seeing things?”","Her uncle chuckled. “Of course not. Look at Xiaoshu. He’s so loud! Listen!”","Sanya didn’t listen carefully. Instead, she grabbed Xiaoshu and smacked him on the butt. “I told you not to go into the river! Why wouldn’t you listen?!” “Sister! Sister! That hurts!","“I’m sorry. I won’t do it again. I’m sorry!”","Despite the pain, the boy still wrapped his arms around the girl’s neck and burst into tears.","Sanya couldn’t bring herself to hit him anymore. She and her brother were so close to sinking together and never seeing their parents again!","The siblings sobbed.","The other men watched with tears in their eyes.","“Hey...” The uncle nudged Feng Wu with his elbow.","Feng Wu glanced at them.","The young man smiled obsequiously. “Sorry about what happened just then. I guessed I offended you.”","Feng Wu nodded. “Yes, you did.”","What?","Shouldn’t she say it was alright? The uncle didn’t know what to say.","Feng Wu glanced at the crying siblings and turned to leave.","“Hey, don’t go!” The uncle tried to grab Feng Wu.","Feng Wu dodged and frowned at him.","All eyes were on Feng Wu and the young man.","The father came back to himself. He went up to Feng Wu and knelt.. “Miss, Gao","Mingjiang will be forever in your debt!”"]},{"number":3734,"title":"Chapter 3734: Rescue (3)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3734: Rescue (3)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Feng Wu shook her head. “Don’t worry about it.”","She went on walking after that.","She had to leave as soon as possible. Otherwise, if the silver-masked man found her, he might kill all those people.","Feng Wu put a hand on her chest.","Just then, her internal injury acted up!","Yes, she had been suffering from internal injuries.","The black-robed man’s strike had severely injured her.","In order to trick the black-robed man, she had concocted all her medicine into poison to kill him. Hence, she didn’t have any left.","Feng Wu shook her head with a wry smile and quickly walked away.","“Miss...” Gao Mingjiang wanted to catch up with Feng Wu, but she was too fast for him to catch up with. He could only watch her leave.","“Brother, who’s that girl? He looks so arrogant.” The uncle frowned and didn’t like Feng Wu’s attitude.","Gao Mingjiang threw a dirty look at his brother. “She’s my savior! Show some respect”","His brother waved his hand impatiently. “Fine, fine. I’m not disrespecting her, but her attitude is a little too aloof!”","Gao Mingjiang said, “She has her own plan. We won’t be able to guess it.” Holding her brother’s hand, the teenage girl stared in the direction Feng Wu had left in.","Feng Wu turned a corner and coughed loudly.","She coughed so hard that she thought she was going to cough her lungs out.","Little Phoenix jumped. “Are you alright? Are you alright?”","Feng Wu waved it off. “I can still hold on. Let’s go.”","Little Phoenix said, “I’ll carry you.”","Feng Wu glanced at it. “You’ve been hit by that man yourself. You can’t carry me now. Let’s go.”","Little Phoenix nodded reluctantly.","“Wait...’","Standing by the side of the road, Feng Wu found the scene rather strange.","Why did everyone look like they were running away?","Their clothes were all tattered and dirty, and their faces were covered with dirt. It was so muddy that she couldn’t see their faces.","They panicked and headed north in a hurry.","Some carriages were galloping past, but most of them were ordinary civilians. Some came in twos and threes, some came in one or twos, and some came in whole processions.","Feng Wu and Little Phoenix looked at each other.","Something was going on here!","Feng Wu then recalled the family of the children she had saved earlier. They looked like a big family as well.","Feng Wu asked Little Phoenix, “Where are we?”","Little Phoenix said, ‘We’re in Northern Yan now.”","Feng Wu asked, “Already?”","Little Phoenix nodded matter-of-factly. “That’s right. Didn’t I tell you to choose a path in the tomb? One led to Northern Yan and the other to the Junwu Empire. Since you chose the shortcut, we came out in Northern Yan.”","Feng Wu asked, “Where are we in Northern Yan, then?”","Little Phoenix gestured at Feng Wu to take the map.","Feng Wu had a map of Northern Yan in her chest pocket, which she had prepared beforehand.","Little Phoenix pointed at the center and told Feng Wu, “We’re right here.”","Feng Wu said, “It’s not that far from the royal palace.”","Little Phoenix nodded. “1500 km. With your original capability, it won’t take you long to cover that distance, but now... ”","Feng Wu hadn’t fully recovered yet. With her current cultivation level, it would take her a while to run 1500 km.."]},{"number":3735,"title":"Chapter 3735: Refuge (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3735: Refuge (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Feng Wu saw a lot of people on the road, and some of them didn’t seem to be doing well.","She tried to ask a few people about the situation, but they weren’t in the mood to talk, and their eyes were numb. All they told Feng Wu was that the war in Southern Yan was coming, and the soldiers at the front wouldn’t be able to hold their ground. Therefore, they were running as fast as they could toward the imperial capital.","Feng Wu was surprised. Southern Yan? Was it at war with Northern Yan? When was that? Why didn’t she know anything about it?","But these people didn’t know much either. They left in a hurry.","Feng Wu put a hand on her chest again.","“Your wounds are too severe. You need to find a place to treat them!” Little Phoenix had never looked so serious.","Feng Wu waved her hand, but blood rushed out of her throat, and she almost couldn’t hold it down.","“You have to treat your wounds now, or you’re going to die!” Little Phoenix coughed and spat out a mouthful of black blood.","Feng Wu asked, “Are you that badly injured?”","Little Phoenix rolled its eyes at her. “We were hit by that man together, and I’m more capable than you. I’m already in this state, which shows how badly you’ve been injured. You’re lucky to be able to walk out of the tomb alive.” Feng Wu only gave it a wry smile.","Little Phoenix was right. She needed to treat her wounds now. Otherwise, she wouldn’t be able to make it to Northern Yan.","Just then, Feng Wu saw a checkpoint up ahead.","A row of wooden fences blocked the road, and two people sat at tables by the side. Behind them were soldiers covered in heavy armor.","The two people sitting on the chairs were obviously capable cultivators. Right now, they were staring coldly at the person standing in front of them.","Men went through soon enough, but for the women, especially the teenage ones, the two cultivators kept a very close watch on them.","Were they doing it on purpose?","No, Feng Wu shook her head inwardly. She didn’t see any lewd look in their eyes. That was to say, they were on official business.","What kind of official business would make them so alarmed by teenage girls?","Feng Wu suddenly felt alarmed.","Little Phoenix frowned. “Something doesn’t feel right. I’ll go have a look.”","After that, Little Phoenix quietly flew toward them.","Feng Wu thought that it would be a while before Little Phoenix came back, but as it turned out, the bird came back in a split second and hid itself in Feng Wu’s arms.","Little Phoenix buried its head and talked to Feng Wu in its head.","“Let’s get out of here!”","Feng Wu stood at the back of the line. There were at least a few hundred people in front of her, so the people at the checkpoint didn’t notice her.","Feng Wu trusted Little Phoenix and knew that something dangerous was happening. That was why it was behaving this way.","While no one was looking, Feng Wu quickly backed away. She turned a corner and started running. She didn’t use any spiritual essence the whole time, for if there was any fluctuation...","The two junior Spiritual Overlords would notice her.","Right now, two junior Spiritual Overlords were enough to kill her.","Feng Wu spotted a valley and quickly headed for it.","The woods were dense, and no one would notice her once she hid inside.","Feng Wu asked Little Phoenix in a low voice when they were in a secret corner,","“What happened? What did you find?”","“Something’s wrong!” Little Phoenix didn’t want to be spotted either, so it lowered its voice.. “They’re looking for you! You’re a wanted person!”"]},{"number":3736,"title":"Chapter 3736: Refuge (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3736: Refuge (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Feng Wu looked at Little Phoenix in surprise. “I’m a wanted person?” Little Phoenix nodded solemnly.","Feng Wu said, “That’s impossible. I don’t have any dealings with the Yan","Kingdom. Why would they...”","Little Phoenix shook its head. “I don’t know. I can ask around later, but I’m sure that they’re indeed looking for you now!”","Feng Wu had to accept the truth and smiled bitterly. “I guess I’ll have to find another way.”","However, Little Phoenix shook its head again. “There’s no point changing the route. They’ve set up obstacles and people at all the checkpoints of Northern Yan. Plus, they also have your portrait.”","After a pause, Little Phoenix had to remind Feng Wu, “The portrait looks a lot like you!”","Feng Wu rubbed her chin. ” ..Why is Northern Yan so hostile toward me? They even sent two Spiritual Overlords. They won’t be easy to handle.”","Little Phoenix wouldn’t give in. “When you’re strong enough, you can easily defeat a junior Spiritual Overlord.”","Feng Wu mumbled, “I don’t know when I’ll be able to fully recover. If that’s the case now, things will only get harder. Is this what Master Linghu meant by wandering in the mortal world?”","Little Phoenix didn’t get it. “What did you say?","Feng Wu cleared her throat. “Can we go back to the path that led to the Junwu","Empire?”","“Aren’t you afraid of running into the silver-masked man?” Little Phoenix rolled its eyes at Feng Wu.","Feng Wu cleared her throat.","Little Phoenix frowned. “I heard them talking just then. The one on the left told the one on the right that Princess Rao had given a death order. She wanted to see you in person, dead or alive. Yes, she was talking about you.”","Feng Wu said, “Princess Rao? I’ve never heard her name before.”","Little Phoenix shrugged. “I don’t know what you did to offend her, but she wants you dead now, and you can’t go back even if you want to, because she has sent a lot of people to search for you in this vast land.”","Feng Wu was astonished.","They had just escaped the silver-masked man, and the danger wasn’t over yet. Who was this Princess Rao?","Little Phoenix frowned. “I heard from those two that Princess Rao was close to a family of the Junwu Empire. Maybe it’s a family you’ve offended.”","Feng Wu said, “I’ve offended the Zuo and Hua families the most. Could it be one of them?”","Little Phoenix nodded. “It’s possible. By the sound of it, Princess Rao is very influential in Northern Yan. She’s the second in line to inherit the throne, and Prince Min is the first.”","Little Phoenix glanced at Feng Wu. “I’m impressed. You’ve offended their second in line to the throne before even meeting her.”","Feng Wu rubbed her forehead with a wry smile. She really had no idea...","Feng Wu coughed violently.","Despite its displeased tone, Little Phoenix was heartbroken to see Feng Wu like this.","“There’s a cave over there. Go inside and get some rest. I’ll go ask around. I’ll tell you when I’m done.”","Little Phoenix flew around the woods and knew where to find a safe place to live.","Feng Wu pulled the plant away and saw a small cave.","The cave was 10m long and 2m wide. It wasn’t spacious, but it was big enough to fit Feng Wu inside.","It took Feng Wu a lot of effort to get in, and she felt another pain in her chest..."]},{"number":3737,"title":"Chapter 3737: Recover (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3737: Recover (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","It took Feng Wu a lot of effort to walk in. She felt another pain in her chest and almost spat out a mouthful of blood.","Feng Wu found a spot by the wall and sat down. Meanwhile, Little Phoenix had gone out to gather information.","Feng Wu recalled what Little Phoenix said earlier.","Princess Rao wanted to catch her...","Leaning against the wall, Feng Wu sighed in resignation. She put on a disguise and found some shabby clothes, which made her look like a beggar.","As for that face, it belonged to the “ugly girl” she had disguised herself as.","Jun Linyuan, Feng Xun, and Yu Mingye could all recognize her...","It took Feng Wu a lot of effort to disguise herself.","She rested for five minutes, then sat down cross-legged and began to spread her spiritual essence throughout her body, repairing her blocked energy channels.","After some time, Feng Wu heard the sound of rain.","But Feng Wu was too absorbed in her cultivation to be disturbed by the rain. After an unknown period of time, Feng Wu heard rustling sounds, which went on and on.","In such an environment, it would be very difficult for Feng Wu to repair her body, for she was constantly disturbed by the noise.","There were men and women of all ages... It was like a village, and they couldn’t control their voices at all.","Feng Wu opened her eyes in resignation.","She was shocked when she saw what was going on.","There were so many people...","The cave was only big enough to fit a dozen people, but it was packed.","Feng Wu estimated that there were at least 30 of them.","When Feng Wu opened her eyes, an old lady saw her, and she cried out, “Ah!” Immediately, all eyes were on them.","A girl ran up to the old lady and pointed at Feng Wu. “You’re not dead?!”","Feng Wu said, “Have you ever seen a dead person leaning against the wall?” Those people were speechless.","Just then, a man came up to them, bowed at Feng Wu, and said apologetically, “Miss, sorry to bother you, but you did find this cave first. It’s indeed yours.","“But...” The man gave her a wry smile. “It’s raining heavily outside, and it’s late at night. We can’t travel, so we’ll have to stay here for the night. Please forgive us.”","Feng Wu gave the man a strange look.","It was a familiar face.","Feng Wu had saved a girl and a boy before, and one of the men was their father. She was looking right at him.","His name was Gao Mingjiang.","Just then, a teenage girl arrived with a four-year-old boy and looked curiously at Feng Wu.","That was right. It was indeed Sanya and Xiaoshu, the two children Feng Wu had saved.","“Ahem... ”","Blood rushed to Feng Wu’s chest, and she coughed violently.","Her cultivation had been interrupted, and she had only recovered a little.","“Pffft!”","Feng Wu spat out a mouthful of blood.","The old lady’s face darkened when she saw the blood.","She stepped back, tugged at Gao Mingjiang’s sleeve, and pulled him to the side.","Feng Wu heard the old lady clearly.."]},{"number":3738,"title":"Chapter 3738: Recover (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3738: Recover (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Feng Wu heard the old lady clearly.","She could hear the old lady’s words clearly.","“Is this girl a beggar? She looks sick. I’m afraid she won’t live for long.","“And, and look at her... Doesn’t she look like she’s been infected with the plague?”","The old lady moved further away from Feng Wu.","The plague?","Feng Wu was speechless.","Gao Mingjiang looked at Feng Wu and then at Old Madam Gao. He said seriously, “Mother, she doesn’t have a high fever.”","The old lady was still worried. “She doesn’t have a high fever, but she vomited blood!”","Gao Mingjiang still shook his head.","The old lady’s tone became stern. “Hurry up and let her go.”","Gao Mingjiang looked at the pouring rain outside and shook his head awkwardly. “Mother, in terms of first come, first served, she came first.” The old lady said, “I don’t care! Anyway, there are many people on our side!” Gao Mingjiang was speechless.","The old lady stared at Gao Mingjiang solemnly. “If you can’t do it, I’ll get your brother to chase her away!”","“Mother!” Gao Mingjiang frowned.","The old lady glared at Gao Mingjiang, her finger almost poking Gao Mingjiang’s face. “I don’t understand it. Are you disobeying your old mother because of an outsider?!”","Gao Mingjiang frowned and didn’t say anything.","The old lady said, “It’s not like you! What’s going on today!”","Gao Mingjiang looked at the old lady and let out a long sigh. “Mother, Xiaoshu and Sanya almost lost their lives today. I’m thinking that good and evil will be rewarded. We can’t bully her like that just because we have more people.”","Feng Wu couldn’t help but give Gao Mingjiang another look. He was an interesting man.","Fortunately, she had disguised herself as an ugly girl. Otherwise, with how pretty she was, the old lady might want to sell her off.","The old lady glared at Gao Mingjiang. “So, you’re not going to do as I say, are you?”","Gao Mingjiang stood between Feng Wu and the old lady and shook his head seriously.","The old lady was infuriated. She glared at Gao Mingjiang and stormed off, probably looking for another way to get what she wanted.","Gao Mingjiang turned around and saw Feng Wu leaning against the wall, panting. He looked apologetic. “Miss, what’s your name?”","She thought for a moment, then said, “You can call me Feng.”","Gao Mingjiang nodded. ‘Miss Feng, you should rest first. You were the one who found this place first. We can’t possibly do such a thing.","“I’ll get you something to eat.” Gao Mingjiang nodded at her and left.","Feng Wu didn’t know what to say.","She looked at the people in the cave in confusion.","Because there were a lot of people, the cave was packed.","She was surprised to find that they were all carrying blankets and sleeping bags with them. It looked like they were refugees of some kind. After a while, a young woman in her twenties walked up to Feng Wu.","Her face looked gentle, and her voice was soft.","She sat down next to Feng Wu and took out two pancakes and a bamboo tube.","She smiled and said, “Miss, the pancakes are soft. Eat them while they’re hot.” Feng Wu found that the woman looked a little like Sanya.","Sure enough, she went on introducing herself, saying that she was Gao Mingjiang’s wife.","She had been chased by two powerful Spiritual Overlords, and it was only now that she had a chance to eat something hot.."]},{"number":3739,"title":"Chapter 3739: Recover (3)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3739: Recover (3)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Feng Wu’s stomach growled before she could say anything.","Feng Wu didn’t know what to say.","Mrs. Gao smiled at Feng Wu and said, “Eat it while it’s still hot. It’s hard to reheat, and if you don’t eat it now, it’ll harden again. It’ll be such a hassle when it becomes as hard as rock.”","Feng Wu nodded at her, then started eating the pancake.","She was really hungry, so she ate very fast. Before she knew it, she had finished two pancakes and emptied the bamboo tube.","Only then did she realize how hungry she was after all the injuries she had suffered during the escape. How embarrassing. Feng Wu smiled bitterly.","Just then, Feng Wu heard a lot of whispering.","There were men and women.","“The little beggar doesn’t look like she’s been infected by the plague. People who are infected don’t eat that way. I think she can eat a cow!”","“It’s a pancake made from fine flour, so of course it’s delicious. I can swallow a pancake as big as a cow!”","“Mingjiang’s wife is so generous. Where did she get those pancakes? We only ate porridge with grass in it!”","“That’s right. Why wouldn’t she care about her family? Why did she give anything to us?!”","“Even if there’s not enough for the adults, she can always give some to the kids.","Each of them can at least have a taste of the pancake!”","With all the noise, Feng Wu could see that Mrs. Gao didn’t look too happy.","What made her even more speechless was that they were bickering over two plain pancakes. Was this world still the same as the one she knew?","Mrs. Gao turned to the others and said coldly, “The pancakes didn’t come from the family kitchen. My mother’s family risked their lives to send them here. They’re for Xiaoshu and Sanya. There are only so many of them, so what’s wrong with me giving them to this girl?!","“As you all know, Sanya and Xiaoshu almost drowned today, but their savior left after saving them, and my family didn’t have a chance to thank her. I just happened to run into this girl, and I want to save her life. I’ll consider it as repayment for my savior. Can’t I do that?!","“If you really want to eat pancakes, ask your own family to send some!” Mrs. Go glanced at the others.","Many turned away at her gaze, but by the looks of it, they were complaining inwardly.","Feng Wu was confused. What was going on in the Yan Kingdom?","She was so confused that she asked Mrs. Gao.","Mrs. Gao looked at Feng Wu in bewilderment. “Don’t you know?”","Feng Wu smiled bitterly. She could only make up stories about how she had been ill in the cave these days and had no idea what was going on outside.","“You’ve been ill for a long time.” Mrs. Gao gave Feng Wu a sympathetic look and smiled wryly. “The Yan Kingdom is in chaos because of the war and the plague.","Feng Wu asked, “War and plague?”","Mrs. Gao nodded solemnly. “I don’t know much about the war, and my husband can explain to you later. As for the plague...”","Tears welled up in her eyes at the mention of the plague.","She wasn’t the only one. The others had tears in their eyes as well, and no one cared about the two pancakes anymore. They all went back to their work in silence.."]},{"number":3740,"title":"Chapter 3740: The Plague (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3740: The Plague (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Feng Wu looked at Mrs. Gao, “Yes?”","Mrs. Gao looked around and said to Feng Wu, “Everyone here is from the Gao family. You’ve met the old lady already. As for my father-in-law, he didn’t survive the journey...","“The old lady has five sons, and my husband is her fourth son.","“These are our children.” Mrs. Gao put her arms around Xiaoshu and Sanya.","“Before he died, my father-in-law told us to run as fast as we could to the north because a plague broke out in Maple Forest City of Southern Yan, and it’s spreading very fast!","“They’ve sent someone to shut down Maple Forest City. Everyone there is going to die!","“The infected were from Maple Forest City, and Gao Village was fine, but we were going to be burnt to death anywvay! So, the people of our village ran out in a hurry.","“We were in such a hurry and didn’t take many things with us. It was very inconvenient.","“It just so happens that it’s been a drought for the past six months, and we’re running out of food. There’s been a famine in many places, and we can’t get any food at all on our way north.”","Feng Wu frowned. “You should have some food stored up from last year, right?”","Gao Mingjiang was standing behind his wife. He shook his head and smiled bitterly. “Even if there is, it’s still in the hands of the officials. We can’t buy it.","“But I heard that there’s no war, no plague, and no drought in Northern Yan, so we’re heading there.” Gao Mingjiang looked at Feng Wu. “Miss...”","Feng Wu made up an identity for herself, saying that her parents were dead and she had to beg for a living. She then ate some unknown fruit and had a stomachache. That was why she had been living in this cave.","Feng Wu only said it in a casual tone, but Gao Mingjiang and his wife saw pity in each other’s eyes.","Even the woman, who had been very harsh before, softened her tone when she glanced at Feng Wu. “You had a harder time than us.”","Feng Wu smiled bitterly. She was being chased around, and of course she had a hard time.","The Zuo family, the Hua family, the Dongsang Kingdom, and Princess Rao of the Northern Yan Kingdom..","Seeing that Feng Wu was lost in her thoughts, that woman thought that she had hit the nail on the head, so she waved at Feng Wu. “There, there. Eat that pancake. I won’t hold it against you.”","After that, she gave a wave of her hand and lay down on the bed she made for herself.","The cave was quite small, and each branch of the family formed a little group.","Everyone was lying on the ground, and there wasn’t even room to walk around.","Mrs. Gao had taken care of Feng Wu well. She put Feng Wu on the spot closest to the inner circle, while she lay down next to Feng Wu, blocking the other people’s gaze.","Seeing that Feng Wu had been lost in her thoughts, Mrs. Gao patted her on the shoulder. “Don’t worry. Go to bed. We still have to travel tomorrow.”","Feng Wu knew that she was talking about the Gao family.","They were short of clothes, food, water, and everything else. They had to get to Northern Yan as soon as possible to survive.","Feng Wu nodded, closed her eyes, and went into deep thought.","With her disguise skills, she could enter Northern Yan on her own, but it would be much more risky.","It was mainly because of the silver-masked man.","The Dongsang Kingdom was very good at hunting people. Somehow, they seemed to be able to get to her.."]},{"number":3741,"title":"Chapter 3741: The Plague (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3741: The Plague (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","The Dongsang Kingdom was very good at hunting people. Somehow, they seemed to be able to get to her.","Therefore, it would be much more dangerous if she was on her own.","Could she go back to the Junwu Empire instead of going to Northern Yan?","Feng Wu rubbed Little Phoenix, who had flown back to her and was lying in her arms.","According to Little Phoenix, it had indeed sensed the masters of the Zuo family and the Hua family searching for her. Moreover, they were hiding in the crowd.","As for Jun Linyuan...","Little Phoenix said regrettably that it didn’t sense Jun Linyuan’s energy.","Feng Wu could only sigh.","She had no choice but to go to Northern Yan now. Moreover, with what Master Linghu had said, she had to finish the journey within three months.","More than half of the time had passed.","After some thought, Feng Wu decided that she should be able to hide from her pursuers if she stayed with the family and hid her spiritual essence.","At that thought, Feng Wu put a hand over her dantian. She had to seal up the little bit of cultivation she had recovered.","“Are you really going with them?!” Little Phoenix’s voice rang out in her head.","Feng Wu nodded. “Yes.”","Little Phoenix grew anxious. “But they’re defenseless. They’re just ordinary farmers. How are they supposed to protect you?!”","Feng Wu smiled and replied to Little Phoenix in her head. “These defenseless people are the ones that can protect me now.”","Little Phoenix wanted to say something, but Feng Wu waved it off. “Don’t worry. Everything will be fine.”","Feng Wu couldn’t sleep at all among all the snoring.","Mrs. Gao and the others woke up early the next morning.","Gao Mingjiang was obviously the leader of the team. He divided each branch into a team. Some were collecting firewood, some were cooking, and some were digging plants.","Mrs. Gao was given the job of cooking.","Feng Wu saw that she was making pancakes on the stove.","This time, it wasn’t flour pancakes, but corn flour and some miscellaneous grains. Feng Wu frowned when she saw the chaff.","The texture seemed so rough. How was she going to eat that?","Mrs. Gao couldn’t help but smile when she saw Feng Wu. “By the way, Miss","Feng, go wash your face.”","Feng Wu didn’t want to wash her face, for it would be easier to hide her identity with all the dirt. Moreover, dirtv little beggars were a common scene.","Feng Wu gave her a wry smile. “My face is bruised. It’ll be better if I put someash on it. It won’t work once I wash it off.”","Mrs. Gao gave Feng Wu a sympathetic look and said, “You’re sick. Sit down and take a break. The coarse chaff pancakes will be ready soon. They smell nice.”","They were indeed coarse chaff pancakes. Feng Wu saw that more than half of them were coarse chaff, but there was very little corn flour.","As for the smell...","Feng Wu smiled bitterly. She really couldn’t bring herself to eat them.","Feng Wu looked around then at Mrs. Gao.","Mrs. Gao was smart enough to know that Feng Wu wanted to say something.","She smiled. “It’s still early, and there’s firewood in the mountains, so I’ll make some more coarse chaff pancakes. When we’re in a hurry, we don’t have to cook anymore. The pancakes can be washed down with cold water, and it’ll be quite filling.”","Feng Wu smiled bitterly. Coarse chaff pancakes and cold water... That was hardly edible.","However, for the sake of her plan, Feng Wu had no choice but to ask, “Mrs..","Gao, where are you going?”"]},{"number":3742,"title":"Chapter 3742: Fugitive (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3742: Fugitive (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","However, for the sake of her plan, Feng Wu had no choice but to ask, ‘Mrs. Gao, where are you going?”","Lady Gu smiled bitterly. “All we want is to get to the Northern Yan Kingdom.","Once we’re there, we can stay anywhere. We just want to live.”","Feng Wu cleared her throat. “Can I come with you?”","Before Mrs. Gao could say anything, the third son’s wife, who had come back with some firewood, threw a dirty look at Feng Wu. “No!”","Concerned that Feng Wu would be upset, Mrs. Gao smiled bitterly. “Actually...”","Her sister-in-law rolled her eyes at her. “Don’t be so nice! You can’t pick up a beggar by the side of the road! We’ll have one more mouth to feed!”","Seeing that Mrs. Gao still wanted to say something, the sister-in-law smirked.","“I’ll tell my mother. Just wait and see!”","After that, she threw away her firewood and headed for the slope.","Old Mrs. Gao was on the mountain slope with the kids looking for edible plants. According to her, if they mixed some leaves into the porridge, they would be able to survive for another meal.","“Mom! Mom!” Her third daughter-in-law shouted as she ran.","Hearing her sister-in-law’s exasperated tone, Mrs. Gao was angry. She turned to Feng Wu and sighed. “Miss Feng, I don’t think my mother will agree.”","Feng Wu already knew what was going to happen. She nodded at Mrs. Gao, then quickly walked away.","By then, Mrs. Gao’s sister-in-law had dragged old Mrs. Gao to her side. “Mom! My dear sister-in-law has agreed to take that little beggar with us! I can’t believe it!”","Old Mrs. Gao was still holding a handful of leaves. Hearing that, she stared at Mrs. Gao and questioned her.","“Is that true? Did you really agree to take that little beggar with us?! ”","Mrs. Gao, who went by the name Li, wished she could bring Feng Wu along. She turned to the old lady. “Mum, Miss Feng is so tiny. She can’t eat much food.","She... ”","However, the old lady reacted violently.","“Go to hell!” The old lady threw all the leaves at Mrs. Gao’s face, but it still didn’t appease her.","“I’m still the head of this family! You’re just a daughter-in-law! How dare you bring a little beggar with you? There are so many beggars along the way. Can you help them all?","“I’m the one who feeds you! You’ll starve to death if I don’t give you anything to eat! And you’re trying to take other people with you? You’re not the only kind person here, but now isn’t the time to be kind!","“I don’t care what reason you have! Get her out of my sight now! If she doesn’t leave, you’re leaving with her!”","“Mum...","Frightened, Xiaoshu and Sanya wrapped their arms around the old lady’s legs, fearing that she would hit their mother again.","Li blushed at the old lady’s words.","Many people were watching, and most of them were her brothers-in -law, sisters-in-law, and their children.","Li was so embarrassed that she wanted to dig a hole and hide in it.","Gao Mingjiang walked up to his wife, wrapped her in his arms, and frowned at his mother. “Mother, you’ve crossed the line.”","Seeing that her son had turned against her, old Mrs. Gao was furious.."]},{"number":3743,"title":"Chapter 3743: Fugitive (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3743: Fugitive (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Old Mrs. Gao pointed at her son. ‘What did you say? What did you just say?!”","Gao Mingjiang frowned. “Mother, you’ve crossed the line. We didn’t have much food with us when we ran away. As for what we’re eating now, it’s all from me.” He was telling the truth, and no one dared to contradict him.","His other brothers and sisters-in-law had wanted to side with the old lady, but they felt rather guilty when they heard this.","Old Mrs. Gao was shocked. Her son’s words were like a slap on her face.","“Mingjiang, what’s that supposed to mean?!”","Gao Mingjiang looked at his mother and said seriously, “Mother, if you hadn’t made such a scene, I wouldn’t have bothered, but if you really want to go there, we can split the food among the branches and go our own way. We don’t have to stay together. I’ll only protect my wife and children. Mother, if you want to come with us, that’s fine. As for the others, it’s none of my business.”","Everyone looked at Gao Mingjiang in astonishment.","He was going to abandon his brothers!","“Mingjiang, what’s that supposed to mean?”","“Mingjiang, how could you do that to your brothers?!”","“Mingjiang...”","Everyone panicked a little.","It was common knowledge that Gao Mingjiang was the head of the 30 -member team.","If it hadn’t been for Gao Mingjiang, they would have been killed a hundred times by now because he was the one who knew where to go and how to find food, water and avoid bandits.","Because of that, they wouldn’t let go of Gao Mingjiang.","The second son of the Gao family tried to mediate the situation. “Mingjiang, Mom didn’t mean it. Don’t be mad. Don’t take it to heart.”","The third was also trying to persuade Gao Mingjiang.","In the end, the eldest son showed up with a stern look on his face.","He frowned at Gao Mingjiang. “Mingjiang, don’t bring that up again. Mom’s still here. Are you trying to separate the family? That’s enough!”","Gao Mingjiang smirked. “Everything will be fine if you people have nothing to do with Xiaoshu and Sanya falling into the river yesterday, but if you do...” “Of course, it has nothing to do with them!” Old Mrs. Gao said hastily.","Gao Mingjiang snorted and didn’t say anything else.","Just then, someone spotted Feng Wu and cried out.","Feng Wu cleared her throat. “Are you having a row? I’ll come back later...”","The third son’s wife turned around and smirked when she saw that it was Feng Wu. The quarrel would never have happened if it hadn’t been for the girl. She stared at Feng Wu. “Didn’t you leave just then? Why are you back?!”","Feng Wu pointed at the sack in her hand. “I didn’t leave. I just went to get something.”","Feng Wu could open up her ring space now. She didn’t have any medicine or toxins left, but she had put a lot of supplies in it.","She had only thought about keeping them there as a precaution, and they came in handy right now.","Feng Wu found the worst sack and the worst rice and flour...","“When I was lying in the cave, I saw someone burying something in the mountain, so I went to dig it out..”"]},{"number":3744,"title":"Chapter 3744: Fugitive (3)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3744: Fugitive (3)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Feng Wu found an excuse for herself and went on. “I’m going to Northern Yan with you. I can’t leave empty-handed. I’m not a freeloader.”","The third son’s wife smirked at Feng Wu. “You little beggar. Are you saying that you’re not a freeloader?”","She wasn’t the only one sneering at Feng Wu.","Food was scarce at the moment, and with the famine everywhere, every morsel of food was very expensive. No one would want to take this little beggar with them.","Old Mrs. Gao glared at Feng Wu. “We’re not taking you! Just forget about it!”","However, the next second, Feng Wu picked up a corner of the sack and began to pour out the contents.","It was flour.","It was pure white flour.","As a matter of fact, Feng Wu still had all kinds of good rice in her ring space. They were much more expensive than the flour, but she couldn’t take them out now.","The flour alone was eye-catching enough.","“Ahhh!!!”","Everyone cried out enviously when Feng Wu threw the flour onto the ground.","“White flour! Isn’t that white flour?!” “There’s no coarse grain in it!”","“How many pancakes can we make with it?!”","“I want egg noodles! I want a poached egg on the thick noodles.”","“I want some dumplings...”","Everyone was drooling.","Immediately, all eyes were on Feng Wu.","Feng Wu asked the old lady, “What do you think of this flour?”","Old Mrs. Gao was so excited that her legs trembled.","Even in peaceful times, they still could only have dumplings on special occasions and couldn’t afford to eat them on a daily basis.","This world belonged to the cultivation masters. Common folks like them could live happily for a whole year just by eating some noodles.","“What? What did you say?” The eldest son estimated that the flour had to weigh at least 50 kg.","A lot of flour had been smeared with mud. The silly girl had poured the flour all over the ground! Old Mrs. Gao was so heartbroken.","Feng Wu smiled at old Mrs. Gao. “Well, I’m only saying that I can feed myself with flour. Can I join your team and go to Northern Yan?”","Yes! Of course, she could!","When the old lady saw the flour, she knew that it was hers. Even if it wasn’t, she had to make it happen!","“Ahem!” Granny Gao put on a long face. “Why do you want to team up with my family?”","Feng Wu smiled bitterly. “I only have this bag of flour, but I don’t have any company. There are so many people on the road, and I can’t take all the food to Northern Yan all by myself. But you have a lot of people. It’ll be safer for me to go with you.”","Old Mrs. Gao snorted. “I see that you know what you’re doing. Since you’re so eager to join us, we’ll have all the flour!”","Feng Wu was about to nod when Gao Mingjiang frowned. “Wait.”","Old Mrs. Gao was about to jump into the flour pile when she heard what her son said. She was furious. Was he trying to sabotage her plan? Gao Mingjiang glanced at her and said, “The flour has to be at least 50 kg.” They used the same metric system here as in the Junwu Empire.."]},{"number":3745,"title":"Chapter 3745: Fugitive (4)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3745: Fugitive (4)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Old Mrs. Gao shielded the flour and stared at Gao Mingjiang. “What do you want?!”","Gao Mingjiang said casually, “Miss Feng is sick. I need to leave some for her.” “No!” Old Mrs. Gao refused right away.","Gao Mingjiang smirked. “No? Mother, do you know how much this white flour is worth? How about I let her join another team?”","“No!” The old lady was exasperated. She threw a dirty look at Gao Mingjiang. This son of hers was taking the side of an outsider! She was so mad!","Gao Mingjiang went up to them and filled an empty sack with 15kg of flour.","Old Mrs. Gao pressed a hand to her chest and cried out, “That’s enough! That’s enough! ”","Feng Wu wanted to tell them that she still had more, not to mention that she could buy food everywhere when they got to Northern Yan.","However, Uncle Gao was doing her a favor, so she didn’t say a word.","Gao Mingjiang filled the bag with 25 kg of flour, put it in front of his wife, and said, “Make these into pancakes. They’ll be Miss Feng’s food.","Gao Mingjiang was about to say something when the old lady rolled into the flour.","Yes, she was lying inside, regardless of the fact that they needed to eat that food later.","“No, no, no. I can’t let you take any more of it. If you do, I’ll smash my head into this rock! You’ll be killing your mother!”","Gao Mingjiang looked at old Mrs. Gao in resignation before turning to Feng wu.","Feng Wu smiled. “I’ll use the rest as my payment for tagging along. What do you think?”","The old lady felt she was going to faint. Feng Wu was now much more pleasing to the eye than her heartless fourth son.","“Sure, sure...” The old lady nodded repeatedly.","Seeing all the flour, Li was elated as well. Without another word, she was already making the pancakes.","As for old Mrs. Gao...","With the help of her daughters-in-law, the old lady rose to her feet. However, she was covered by flour now.","The old lady couldn’t part herself from the food.","When she opened her eyes, she saw her third daughter-in-law hiding flour in his sleeve.","“How dare you steal my flour?! Go away!” The old lady was exasperated. She picked up a stick and lashed it at her daughter-in-law, who immediately ran away.","After chasing her daughter-in-law away, the old lady called after her other two daughters-in-law. “What are you waiting for? Do you know how valuable these flour are?! Put it in a bag!”","It was indeed very precious because one couldn’t buy food with money now.","The two wives immediately packed the flour for her.","By the time they had filled most of the bag, there was only a thin layer of flour mixed with mud on the ground.","The second daughter-in-law looked at the old lady.","The old lady threw a dirty look at her. “What are you looking at? Scrape the soil up and put it in the water. The flour will float, and the soil will settle down! How can you be so dumb? You didn’t even think of that!”","The two daughters-in-law did as they were told.","If the old lady hadn’t said anything, they would have licked the flour clean as well.","Feng Wu was helping Li with her cooking at the moment, and she was rendered speechless when she saw how much the old lady loved the flour. “You can eat it when it’s covered in dirt?”","Li chuckled. “You have no idea how precious flour is nowadays.”","She sighed at Feng Wu after that. Feng Wu was confused. “Why are you sighing?”","Li smiled bitterly.. “It’s not worth it...”"]},{"number":3746,"title":"Chapter 3746: Fugitive (5)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3746: Fugitive (5)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Feng Wu chuckled. “It’s worthwhile. I won’t be able to protect so much food anyway.”","Li agreed with her. “It’s just that I feel sorry tor you when you had to give away so much nice flour.”","Both sides were making pancakes.","Because of Gao Mingjiang’s words, Li was making pancakes out of pure wheat flour, but not the old lady.","Wheat flour was such a precious commodity that the old lady couldn’t bring herself to make plain flour pancakes. She had mixed some corn flour, sorghum powder, and other coarse grains into the flour, and there was a big bowl of the mixture.","They didn’t have much time to rest and cook because they had been moving as fast as they could. No one knew when the plague would arrive, or when the Southern Yan Kingdom would catch them.","Li made 300 pancakes with about 30 kg of flour, and she was exhausted. However, her eyes lit up when she saw all the pancakes, for food meant they could live.","Li put the pancakes into a sack once they cooled down and handed the sack to Feng Wu.","Feng Wu shook her head. “I can’t carry that much. Please keep it for me. I’ll get it from you when I need to eat.”","Li also realized that Feng Wu was going to sit in their carriage, so she nodded and helped Feng Wu put the pancakes in the carriage.","Feng Wu looked curiously at the three carriages.","From their conversation, she could tell that they were all ordinary farmers. Having a cow was already supposed to be a big deal, but the Gao family had three carriages.","Seeing that Feng Wu was perplexed, Li explained to her with a smile. “My husband found them.”","Found them?","Seeing that Feng Wu was confused, Li whispered in her ear and told her about their most dangerous journey.","As it turned out, they ran into bandits a few days after they left the Southern Yan Kingdom. The bandits were attacking a large family, and many of them were killed or injured.","Both sides were well-matched in strength and lost about the same number of people. In the end, the bandits killed the last member of the family, but they didn’t have many men left either.","Gao Mingjiang took the lead, killed the remaining bandits, and took the three carriages. As for the wealth of that family, it wasn’t that they didn’t want to take them, but that family had set their chests on fire before they died.","“But with these three carriages, we can travel much faster. It was supposed to take us ten days to get here, but it only took us three to four days.”","Feng Wu asked, “Are carriages only twice as fast?”","Li smiled bitterly. “It would have been much faster, but there are so many of us here, and we can’t fit all 30 people inside. The elderly and children can take the carriage, together with all the food we have. The carriages are packed to the brim. As for the adults, we still have to walk on foot.”","It was almost noon when a young man came to inform them that they were leaving in 15 minutes.","Feng Wu recognized the man. Li told her, “This is Gao Mingkun, my husband’s fifth brother.”","Feng Wu nodded.","Gao Mingkun looked at Feng Wu and found the little beggar familiar. He narrowed his eyes. “Have we met before?”","Feng Wu’s stomach lurched, and she said indifferently, “Really? I don’t think so. ”","Li immediately said, “Mingkun, you must be mistaken. Miss Feng has been sick in the cave this whole time. I don’t think you’ve ever met her..”"]},{"number":3747,"title":"Chapter 3747: Fugitive (6)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3747: Fugitive (6)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Gao Mingkun didn’t reply. He only left after giving Feng Wu one last look.","Fearing that Feng Wu would be frightened, Li tried to calm her down. “Don’t be afraid. Mingkun is usually very kind. He’s not that scary. He’s just trying to intimidate you.”","Feng Wu realized that Li was the kindest person she had ever met.","Patting her chest, Feng Wu coughed a little.","Li smacked her forehead. “How could I forget? You’re still sick. Get in the carriage now...”","Feng Wu was indeed going to get into the carriage and have some rest. She didn’t even dare to use her spiritual essence to repair her body because she had a feeling that if she activated her spiritual essence, the Dongsang man with the silver mask would lock onto her.","Feng Wu didn’t know what kind of ability it was, but she had a hunch.","Feng Wu was pushed into the carriage, and there was indeed a lot of stuff inside. There were coarse grain, dried rations, buckets, and some clothes...","With Feng Wu inside, the carriage was almost full.","Soon, Xiaoshu and Sanya were brought in as well.","Feng Wu moved back to make some room for them.","Feng Wu sighed inwardly at the musty smell of the bedspread. She hoped that she could get away with it this time.","Soon, they arrived at the checkpoint where Feng Wu had lined up the day before.","The roads were still heavily guarded, and the atmosphere was very tense.","“Miss Feng, please come down.” After taking the two children out, Li reached out to help Feng Wu.","After lying down for a while, Feng Wu had recovered a little, and the pain in her chest wasn’t as bad anymore. She feigned a confused tone. “What’s going","There was a long line ahead, and Feng Wu estimated that it was at least hundreds of meters long.","Because of the meticulous inspection, the line didn’t move forward for a while.","Li whispered to Feng Wu, “I heard from my husband that the Yuan territory is right ahead of us. It’s off-limits!”","Feng Wu had heard of the Yuan territory before.","There was a no-man’s-land between the Southern and Northern Yan. The terrain was either tall mountains or dense forests. Neither side cared about it, and the land had remained deserted.","Li was equally confused. “Why is there an inspection? Are they stopping us from going to the other side?”","Feng Wu knew why they were stopped. Princess Rao wanted to catch her.","Just then, Gao Mingjiang came back, and Li waved at him.","Before Gao Mingjiang could reach Li, she asked anxiously, “What happened? What happened?”","Gao Mingjiang smiled bitterly. “I heard that they were looking for a wanted criminal, but they didn’t tell me who the person was.”","Li frowned, looking concerned. “Why is this happening? What do they want?”","Gao Mingjiang tried to appease her. “Don’t worry. It has nothing to do with us. We just have to be careful. By the way...”","Gao Mingjiang looked at Feng Wu in frustration. “Miss Feng, do you have your travel permit and identification?”","Seeing that Feng Wu was dumbfounded, Li patted Gao Mingjiang on the shoulder. “Miss Feng is a beggar now. How can she have a travel permit or proof of identity?”","Gao Mingjiang was speechless.","Li suddenly clapped her hands. “Fengya, the daughter of my sister, is 13 or 14 years old, and she’s as slim as Miss Feng.. How about we let her take Fengya’s place? What do you think?”"]},{"number":3748,"title":"Chapter 3748: Fugitive (7)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3748: Fugitive (7)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Gao Mingjiang realized that this was the only way, so he gave Feng Wu an inquiring look. Feng Wu nodded.","Gao Mingjiang went to tell the other members of the Gao family so that they wouldn’t make any mistakes if they were asked.","Everyone knew who Fengya was. All they needed to do now was to treat Miss Feng as that girl.","Gao Mingjiang stared at his third brother’s wife.","The woman had tried to do some damage because she resented Feng Wu for taking too much flour.","Gao Mingjiang looked around before turning to his sister-in-law. “If one of us makes a mistake, all 30 members of the Gao family will die!”","Everyone felt a chill run down their spine.","“Of course, if you don’t want to do that, we can split up now,” Gao Mingjiang said indifferently.","“We’re going to stick together!”","“I’ll do whatever Mingjiang says! This family has to stay together!”","“Miss Feng is Fengya. They have similar names. She’s our Fengya!”","Granny Gao looked around and said coldly, “If anyone dares to make a mistake now and incriminates everyone in the Gao family, I won’t forgive them even if we’re safe later! I’ll feed them to the dogs!”","Everyone was scared..","Especially the wife of the third son. Both Gao Mingjiang and old Mrs. Gao was giving her threatening looks.","She smiled obsequiously. “Mother, you’re right.”","Luckily, they were so far away from the others that other members of the family didn’t hear them.","After that, they went back to the line.","It was their turn four hours later.","Feng Wu noticed that the cliff was right ahead of them.","The cliff was only wide enough for one carriage, and they had to go through it to get to Northern Yan. The pursuers had chosen the right spot.","The same two people sat there with stern faces and brooding eyes. They kept their gazes on each person in turn.","Moreover, Feng Wu realized that they would summon the leader of each group.","As expected, a soldier walked up to them and asked coldly, “Who’s the leader here?!”","Everyone looked at Gao Mingjiang.","Gao Mingjiang stepped out at that moment and smiled obsequiously at the soldier. As he spoke, he put a silver ingot into the soldier’s sleeve.","After weighing it in his hand, the soldier was satisfied with the size of the silver ingot, and his attitude improved a lot.","“Follow me!”","The soldier led Gao Mingjiang to a remote corner, took something out of his chest pocket, and showed it to him. “Have you seen this person on your way here?”","Gao Mingjiang’s stomach lurched when he saw the portrait.","He recognized the person in the painting!","It was his savior.","That was the girl who had saved Xiaoshu and Sanya from the river. She was wanted?!","It was obvious that the soldier wasn’t just any ordinary man. He stared at Gao","Mingjiang. “You’ve met her before?”","Luckily, Gao Mingjiang had seen enough of the world to be able to stay calm in a tense situation like this.","“Of course, I haven’t.”","“Then why do you look stunned?” The soldier stared at Gao Mingjiang.","Gao Mingjiang smiled bitterly. “She’s so pretty that no one can resist her.. Weren’t you amazed the first time you saw her face?”"]},{"number":3749,"title":"Chapter 3749: Fugitive (8)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3749: Fugitive (8)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","The soldier gave Gao Mingjiang a sidelong glance.","But he didn’t know what to say, because he had been astonished by the girl’s beauty as well when he had first laid eyes on her portrait. No man could resist her face.","“You really didn’t see her?” The soldier’s face darkened.","Gao Mingjiang smiled obsequiously. “She’s too beautiful to be forgotten. I’m sure of it.”","The soldier didn’t believe Gao Mingjiang. He asked around and saw that everyone shook their heads in bewilderment.","The soldier was secretly disappointed.","Gao Mingjiang lowered his voice. “Who’s in this portrait? Is she a criminal?”","Of course, the soldier wouldn’t tell him. He only snorted. “If you don’t tell the truth, you’ll all be decapitated!”","Everyone nodded obediently.","The soldier snorted and left with the drawing.","Feng Wu saw the portrait in the soldier’s hand.","Little Phoenix was right. They were indeed looking for her, but they didn’t dare to do it openly and were only asking around in secret. That was to say, Princess Rao and her brother might not be in the same boat.","Feng Wu felt much better at that thought.","Soon, it was their turn.","Everyone passed the checkpoint in order.","Old Mrs. Gao went through first, followed by each branch of the family.","Gao Mingjiang had already handed in the Gao family’s household registration booklet, so everyone was waiting for their name to be called.","“You’re my niece. Don’t worry.” Li was a little scared, but she still tried to comfort Feng Wu.","Feng Wu was touched.","In fact, what she did could easily bring harm to the Gao family, especially Li. However, she had been so kind to her when they were total strangers.","When the soldier reached the fourth branch of the family, he saw that there was an additional member next to Li.","“Who is she?”","The soldier frowned when he saw the sallow girl, whose clothes were in rags.","Li tugged at Feng Wu, telling her to bow.","“She’s my niece and was living with us when the plague broke out. Because of the emergency, I took her with me when we escaped from Gao Village in Maple","Forest City.”","Gao Mingjiang went up to them as well.","The soldiers had received Gao Mingjiang’s silver before, so they didn’t try to make things difficult for him. They nodded and were ready to let them pass.","Everyone was about to heave a sigh of relief when they heard the sound of hooves.","It was so loud that many people were attracted by it.","Three horses quickly arrived, led by a girl wearing a red cape.","She was a pretty girl with an air of nobility about her. One look at her and everyone fell silent!","“Kneel! On your knees!”","With a whip in his hand, the soldiers lashed down at the people behind them.","Feng Wu tugged at Li to dodge the whip. Otherwise, she would have been hit for nothing.","Li asked in a trembling voice, ‘Who’s that?”","Someone said, “What a grand entrance. Is she the princess?”","Feng Wu glanced at the girl in the red cape and shook her head inwardly. That didn’t seem to be the case.","But the others believed that conclusion.","The two junior Spiritual Overlords on either side of the checkpoint turned to look at the girl in the red cape.."]},{"number":3750,"title":"Chapter 3750: Adventure (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3750: Adventure (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","The two junior Spiritual Overlords on either side of the checkpoint turned to look at the girl in the red cape.","“Miss Caixia.” The Spiritual Overlord on the left nodded at her.","Although he didn’t get up, it was enough to show his respect.","Caixia had no intention of dismounting. She glanced at the Spiritual Overlord and asked casually, “You still haven’t found her?”","“Not yet.” The junior Spiritual Overlord shook his head.","“Useless!” Holding her whip, Caixia glared at the junior Spiritual Overlord. “Keep your eyes open. If you let that person go to the Northern Yan Kingdom, you’ll know what the princess will do to you!”","After that, she rode off without looking at the others.","She was here to warn these people.","It was indeed very effective. Everyone held their breaths when she arrived, but after she left, they didn’t even dare to breathe loudly either.","Feng Wu thought to herself,","“It seems that Princess Rao wants to stop me from entering the Northern Yan","Kingdom and going to the capital. But why? What’s her purpose?”","Would her appearance affect the princess’s interests in some way?","Or had Master Linghu known all along and sent her to the Northern Yan Palace on purpose?","Feng Wu was a little confused.","However, she knew the time and place, so she decided to go. She wanted to see what was going on.","“Go! Now!”","Seeing the look on the Spiritual Overlord’s face, the soldiers knew that he had been humiliated by the princess’s senior maid and was in a foul mood.","He reminded Gao Mingjiang in a low voice, “Just go!”","Gao Mingjiang took the hint right away. He cupped his hands at the soldier and said, “Thank you.”","He left with his wife and children after that, and Feng Wu followed him. Gao Mingkun was quick-witted as well and jumped out like a fish.","They didn’t dare to take a carriage and all walked as fast as they could.","At that moment, they heard a loud noise behind them.","They wanted to look over their shoulders, but Feng Wu whispered, “Run! It’s dangerous!”","Hearing that, the others didn’t dare to look back. They only had time to look over their shoulders when they reached the corner of the plankway.","One look and their hearts raced.","The Spiritual Overlord was furious after being humiliated by Miss Caixia, and everyone behind them was in trouble.","The Spiritual Overlord was attacking the ordinary people like a madman.","Thump, thump, thump!","Hearing the three loud sounds, Feng Wu deduced that the Spiritual Overlord had made three strikes.","He was a Spiritual Overlord!","The people queuing up in front of him were defenseless commoners. How could they withstand three strikes from him?","Hence, a large group of people fell to the ground. Many of them were beaten to a pulp. “Oh god!”","They couldn’t believe their eyes.","Were they really all ants?","Would they become cannon fodder as soon as a big shot lost his temper?","Feng Wu sensed a cold gaze looking in her direction. It was obviously the furious junior Spiritual Overlord.","She whispered, “Stop shouting. Let’s go. Otherwise, that Spiritual... the powerful man is going to kill us!”","The others were amazed at first, but they shuddered when their own lives were in danger.."]},{"number":3751,"title":"Chapter 3751: Adventure (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3751: Adventure (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","“Let’s go!” Just like Feng Wu, Gao Mingjiang also sensed the man’s bad mood, so he grabbed his wife and children and ran as fast as he could.","The others trusted Gao Mingjiang the most. Seeing that he was running as fast as he could, they ran as well.","The Spiritual Overlord snorted when he saw the family running away.","“Good for you!”","After venting his anger, the Spiritual Overlord went back to his cultivation with his eyes closed.","Not only were they cultivating, but they were also sensing the spiritual essence of these people.","Feng Wu should have been detected, but she had been ruthless to herself and destroyed her own cultivation ability. No one could detect it, because she was a cripple now.","The Gao family rode for tens of kilometers before they stopped in a wide meadow to catch their breath.","“Oh my god...”","Old Mrs. Gao still hadn’t calmed down. She smacked her thigh and cried. “Those people behind us are all dead! How can they do this to people like us?!” No one answered her, because they were still in shock.","In the end, Gao Mingjiang heaved a long sigh. “Things have always been like this. You just didn’t see it when you were in the village.”","Everyone fell silent.","Gao Mingjiang didn’t say anything either, for he was still thinking about the portrait, and he wondered what his savior had done. How should he repay her?","“Brother Mingjiang, I didn’t know you still had any silver ingot left” Gao Mingkun, who hadn’t said anything, suddenly spoke.","Only then did the others realize that Gao Mingjiang had given away a silver ingot.","Old Mrs. Gao realized it as well. “I have all our money. Where did you get the silver ingot? Did you stash it away?”","Gao Mingjiang frowned.","His second eldest brother glanced at him. “Mingjiang, I don’t think that’s a good idea. We’re still living in the same room. Even if you earned some money of your own, you have to give it to mother. Why did you have it to yourself? None of your other brothers has done such things. Plus, our eldest brother is like a father to me. Even if we have used that kind of money, it has to be from him.”","Their eldest brother’s face darkened.","Old Mrs. Gao stared at Gao Minziianz. “ExDlain vourself!”","Was she going to interrogate him now? Gao Mingjiang almost lost his temper.","Gao Mingkun was so angry that he laughed. “Mother, Brothers, what’s that supposed to mean? If Brother Mingjiang hadn’t reacted in time and handed that soldier some silver, that soldier would never have warned us!","“If he hadn’t reminded us out of kindness, we would all have turned into a pulp by now. A silver inglot should be the last thing on your minds!”","His second eldest brother said, “It’s not like we won’t let him give the silver away, but we never knew he had such a big chunk. Are we still his brothers or not?”","Feng Wu shook her head in resignation. These people just couldn’t do it. Once they were a little safer, they would start fussing over the money.","They were still too close to the checkpoint. If they made too much noise, the Spiritual Overlords would know.","Therefore, Feng Wu had to step out.","“I lent the silver to Uncle Mingjiang.” Feng Wu glanced at the old lady.."]},{"number":3752,"title":"Chapter 3752: Adventure (3)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3752: Adventure (3)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","“There are ten taels in total. Uncle Mingjiang said that he would pay it back himself, but since you’re all one big family, why don’t you pay it back together? After all, I’ve saved over 30 lives.”","Gao Mingjiang didn’t expect Feng Wu to step out now, but she was a smart girl.","Feng Wu and Gao Mingjiang looked at each other and knew what to do next.","Gao Mingjiang heaved a long sigh. “Little Feng, we’ve agreed that we’ll keep it a secret. I’ll pay you back when I earn some money. Why do you have to...”","Feng Wu waved him off. “Uncle, I know we’re good friends, but we still need to settle our accounts. It’ll be a very long time before we get to Northern Yan alive and settle down. You’ll then be able to earn some money. Maybe I’ll starve to death by then.","“Isn’t it your family’s money? I don’t understand. Why do you have to pay it back all by yourself?”","Feng Wu turned to old Mrs. Gao. “Mrs. Gao, you heard me. That’s what happened. Give it to me.”","“Give you what?” The old lady was a little flustered.","Feng Wu looked at her in bewilderment. “Ten taels of silver! Aren’t you the head of the Gao family? You said so yourself, and I heard it with my own ears!","It’s the right thing to do. Pay up.”","Old Mrs. Gao was furious. She was talking about ten taels of silver, not ten copper coins!","If her third son hadn’t brought it up on purpose, she wouldn’t have...","At that thought, she glared at her third son.","Not only was the old lady staring at him, but his two older brothers were staring at him as well.","The third son wanted to cry, but no tears would come. “Mother, Brothers, I...”","Gao Mingjiang said to old Mrs. Gao, “Mother, that’s what happened. I was worried about the burden on us because we’re poor, but since things have turned out this way... Mother, please give the money to Miss Feng.”","“Over my dead body! I don’t have any money!” Holding her bag, old Mrs. Gao wouldn’t pay up.","Feng Wu rolled her eyes at the old lady. “You’ll have to pay me back sooner or later.”","She then went back to Gao Mingjiang’s carriage.","Gao Mingjiang gave his mother a resentful look. “From now on, I won’t be bothered to do such things. I’ll only take care of my own family. That’s it!”","After that, he went up to the carriage, patted the board, and told the two kids, “Get in.”","Li had always been an obedient wife. She picked up Sanya first, then Xiaoshu. She then told Feng Wu, “Miss Feng, please get in.” Feng Wu nodded and climbed into the carriage.","Gao Mingjiang and Li sat in the driver’s seat.","Old Mrs. Gao was exasperated. “What’s that supposed to mean? What are you doing?!”","Gao Mingjiang ignored her and was going to start the carriage.","His brothers panicked, as did their wives and children.","They had been able to get here in one piece because of Gao Mingjiang. If he left without them, then...","At that moment, they heard wolves howling in the distance.","The third son was almost in tears. He ran up to the horse and said to Gao Mingjiang, “Mingjiang, Mom was only angry, and she didn’t mean it. Please don’t take it seriously!”","The second son nodded immediately. “That’s right. Come down from your carriage. Why are you leaving in the middle of the night? Get back here..”"]},{"number":3753,"title":"Chapter 3753: Adventure (4)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3753: Adventure (4)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","The eldest son was still pulling a long face and acting like a father. He didn’t say anything.","Gao Mingjiang sneered. “We’re spending money together, but I’m the only one paying back the money? Do you think that’s reasonable?”","“No, of course not!” Fearing that his brother was really gone, Gao Mingjiang’s second eldest brother panicked. He turned around and glared at his mother.","Unfortunately, she didn’t take the hint.","The eldest son didn’t know what to do. He was supposed to be the boss of the family, but everyone listened to Gao Mingjiang.","The second son was dropping so much hint with his eyes that his eyeballs were about to have cramps. Finally, his mother finally realized what he meant. She looked at her eldest son inquiringly.","Should she pay up?","The eldest son was so frustrated. He didn’t want to part with the money!","It just so happened that without Gao Mingjiang, they wouldn’t know where to go next. So...","“It’s only ten taels of silver, isn’t it? Since Mingjiang borrowed it, just pay up.” The eldest son stormed off after that.","Old Mrs. Gao rolled her eyes at Feng Wu. “You’re just a beggar. Where did you get the money? Did you steal it?”","If the girl had stolen the silver, why should she give it back? No!","Feng Wu smirked. “I have some flour, too. Did you think I stole it, too? You ate it, so spit it out now!”","The old lady said, “You!”","The sharp-tongued girl was infuriating.","Sanya looked at Feng Wu in admiration. Sister Feng was amazing...","Her grandmother was the most unreasonable and vicious-tongued grandmother. Usually, she would make Sanya and her mother so frustrated that they couldn’t retort. But now, Sister Feng was so glib!","The girl’s eyes lit up as she stared at Feng Wu.","Old Mrs. Gao was furious, but Feng Wu wasn’t done yet. She stared at the old lady and said, “I don’t have to travel with you, alright? Now, give me back my money and the pancakes. I’m leaving!”","The pancakes?!","Immediately, the daughters-in-law and their children panicked. They had been enjoying the show, but now, their cheese had been touched.","“Mother, look...” The wife of the eldest son had always considered herself a kind woman. She stepped out and helped the old lady to her feet. “Everyone, please calm down.”","She smiled at Feng Wu. “Mom didn’t say she wasn’t going to give it back. Kiddo, don’t worry. Let’s talk like civilized people.”","The other daughters-in-law of the Gao family chimed in as well.","They all tried to persuade the old lady to return the money.","Didn’t they care about the money? Of course, they did. Each family would get two taels of silver if the money was divided, but they were fugitives, and money couldn’t buy food at the moment.","Her eldest daughter-in-law whispered something in the old lady’s ear, and the old lady’s eyes lit up. Finally, she gave Feng Wu ten taels of silver.","She glared at Feng Wu. “Just this once. Lend it to Mingjiang again and I won’t pay you back!”","Feng Wu took the silver and nodded. “I won’t lend Uncle Mingjiang any silver even if I have to watch you die.”","The old lady was furious.","Meanwhile, Gao Mingjiang’s brothers were trying to talk Gao Mingjiang out of it. “Mingjiang, look, hasn’t Mom given the money back to the girl? Come down here.”","The brothers had never been so friendly before, but now, they were helping Gao Mingjiang off the carriage.."]},{"number":3754,"title":"Chapter 3754: Adventure (5)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3754: Adventure (5)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Gao Mingjiang knew when to stop.","“I guess I’m not completely innocent. I shouldn’t have given the silver to that soldier. It’s all my fault. I won’t do it again.”","His brothers blanched. If he hadn’t given the soldier the silver...","“No, you didn’t do anything wrong! Mingjiang, you’ve done a great job this time!”","Gao Mingjiang only smiled bitterly, obviously hurt.","An idea struck the second eldest brother, and he told old Mrs. Gao, “Mum, give Mingjiang ten taels of silver!”","Old Mrs. Gao’s eyes popped. That was all the money her family had!","Her second son walked up to her and took ten taels of silver from her. “Mom, which is more important, the silver or your sons and grandsons?”","The old lady was speechless.","In the end, ten taels were taken away from her.","The second son stuffed ten taels of silver into Gao Mingjiang’s hands. “Brother, here’s some silver for you. If something like this happens again, just use them whenever you find necessary. Our life is more important.”","Gao Mingjiang forced a smile and said, “It’s late. Let’s boil some hot water and eat some pancakes. We’ll get some rest and leave early tomorrow. It’s still dangerous here. The further away from here, the better.”","“Yes!” Only then did his brothers relax.","The second son grabbed the third son away.","They walked to a corner, and the second son slapped his younger brother.","The third son was furious. “Good job!” said the eldest son.","“Brother!” The third son protested.","The eldest son slapped his brother as well. “Ten taels of silver! You just can’t keep your mouth shut!”","He walked away after that.","The second son also cast a stern look at his younger brother. “I know you and your wife don’t like Mingjiang, but we can’t leave this place without him! You’ll have to figure it out yourself!”","He stormed off after that, leaving the third son behind.","He was just jealous of Gao Mingjiang and had only said those things in passing. Why did everyone slap him?","Just then, the old lady jumped up and slapped him as well.","“Mom!” The third son stared at his mother in disbelief. His mother had always doted on him!","“Twenty taels of silver! I just gave away twenty taels of silver for nothing! Shut up from now on!” Old Mrs. Gao stormed off.","The third son was really crying now.","Meanwhile, the fourth branch of the Gao family was enjoying themselves.","Gao Mingjiang had deliberately stopped his carriage at the outermost area, so as to keep watch for the others, but in fact, he didn’t want to get too close.","They had built their own campfire and were sitting around, boiling water and warming themselves.","“Thank you.” Gao Mingjiang sat down opposite Feng Wu and mouthed those words.","Feng Wu chuckled. Gao Mingjiang was such a smart guy.","“Sister Feng, you’re amazing! You talked back to Grandma and won!” Sanya went on worshiping Feng Wu.","Feng Wu rubbed her head.","Due to malnutrition, although Sanya was ten years old, she still looked like a seven-year-old. Her hair was as yellow as straw.","Feng Wu chuckled. “Your grandmother is just unreasonable. If you’re with reason, you can win all the arguments.”","In the end, Feng Wu asked, “You’re living such a miserable life. Why haven’t you split up with the other branches?”","Once they were separated, Feng Wu could hunt some wild game for Gao Mingjiang’s family. All the pancakes were simply too bland. Li smiled bitterly.. “Do you think we don’t want to do that?”"]},{"number":3755,"title":"Chapter 3755: Adventure (6)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3755: Adventure (6)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","“Do you think we don’t want to? It’s just we can’t.” Li smiled bitterly and pointed at the old lady. “Every time we brought it up, she threatened to kill herself. We could never succeed.”","Feng Wu rubbed her chin. “It’s really hard to do it while we’re still seeking refuge...”","But those people were indeed her burdens.","Li smiled bitterly. “It’s all fate. What can we do? Alright, kids, go to bed. We still have to travel tomorrow morning.”","After that, Li took out the only bedroll in the carriage and laid it out in the lee of the wind so that Feng Wu and the two children could get in.","“What about you?” Feng Wu asked.","Li waved her off. “We’ll just sleep on the ground for the night. You little ones can easily catch a cold. We adults will be fine.”","Feng Wu didn’t know what to say.","No matter what Feng Wu said, Li insisted that they take the bedroll, and Feng Wu couldn’t turn her down.","Feng Wu sighed as soon as she was under the duvet.","“Why are you sighing? You’re too young to do that. You’ll grow into a little old hag.” Little Phoenix teased her.","Feng Wu’s eyes lit up. “You’re awake!”","Although Feng Wu had lost her cultivation ability, she still had Little Phoenix. It was injured, but it could still fly and ask around. That was to say, it hadn’t lost much of its ability.","Seeing this, Little Phoenix knew that Feng Wu was going to give it trouble again.","It gave Feng Wu a resigned look. ‘What do you want from me?”","Feng Wu said, “I need to go with them, at least as far as the Northern Yan Kingdom. It’ll take us at least another ten days... The further north we go, the colder it gets. I can barely stand it myself, let alone them.”","Little Phoenix looked at Feng Wu in resignation. “Do you want me to bring back a bedroll?”","It was doable, but...","“How are you going to explain the extra bedroll?”","Feng Wu rubbed her chin. “I don’t need you to bring back a bedroll. Look around and see if you can find any houses. Make it look like we’re just passing by, and I’ll buy an extra one.","“If you can’t find any houses, just make it look like someone has left it there, and I’ll pick it up.”","Little Phoenix mimicked Feng Wu and nodded. “Alright. They won’t see me anyway.”","Little Phoenix was soon out of sight.","“Get me some more supplies!” Feng Wu reminded Little Phoenix in her head before she went to bed.","Little Phoenix rolled its eyes at Feng Wu.","It was just a little bird. Not only did it have to find the bedroll, but it also had to prepare the supplies. There was so much to do!","However, at the thought of Feng Wu’s pathetic state, Little Phoenix felt sorry for her.","This family was very poor, but because of that, they were too poor to be spotted.","Little Phoenix spent a lot of effort to find a bundle, two old duvets, and some rice, flour, and oil. It even prepared a bow.","That way, Feng Wu could shoot arrows.","Little Phoenix had painstakingly prepared everything and put them on top of an old tree. After everything was ready, it flew into Feng Wu’s sleeve and told her everything.","Feng Wu smiled and went back to sleep.","She woke up early the next morning.","The Gao family was so poor that they couldn’t afford breakfast.."]},{"number":3756,"title":"Chapter 3756: Adventure (7)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3756: Adventure (7)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","The Gao family was so poor that they couldn’t afford breakfast. Therefore, they got up early in the morning, cleaned themselves up, and got into the carriage. They went as far as they could.","They didn’t have a chance to stop for lunch until noon.","At noon.","They were almost at the spot Little Phoenix had pointed out. Feng Wu held her stomach.","“What’s wrong?” Seeing the change in Feng Wu’s expression, Li asked in concern.","Feng Wu said, “It’s nothing...”","Li said, “I can tell by the look on your face. Are you hungry?","Feng Wu chuckled.","“Teehee.” Li was amused. She realized that although the girl wasn’t very pretty, she was very likable.","“Mingjiang.” Lady Li came out of the carriage and whispered something in Gao Mingjiang’s ear.","Their carriage led the way, and Gao Mingjiang nodded at his wife’s words. “It’s indeed almost noon. It’s time to take a break.”","He raised a red flag, and the carriages behind him stopped as well.","They stopped and started cooking.","Feng Wu was a member of the fourth branch of the family, and the branches took turns doing chores every day. Today, it just happened to be their turn to gather firewood.","Feng Wu already knew that.","After they got off the carriage, Feng Wu took the two children from the fourth branch. “Xiaoshu, Sanya, let’s go get some firewood.”","Li said, “Why are you three kids picking up firewood? I’ll go get it!”","Of course, Feng Wu wanted to go. If she didn’t go, she wouldn’t be able to pick up her provisions.","Hence, Feng Wu suggested, “Let’s go together.”","Li said, “I can go with you, but you have to behave and stay where you are. It’s dangerous up there. What if a wolf comes out?”","Feng Wu nodded immediately.","The two kids nodded as well.","Only then did Li relax a little.","The wife of the third son arrived at that moment. Seeing that they were going to fetch some firewood, she suggested with a smile, “Sister-in-law, how about you stay here with the kids to make lunch, and I’ll go fetch some firewood?” She wanted to make it up for what her husband did the day before.","Picking up firewood was much more tiring than cooking.","Li hesitated.","Feng Wu turned her down with a smile. “Aunt, I was going to take a look in the woods. What if I catch a wild rabbit?”","“Oh my!”","Hearing that, Lady Gu almost burst out laughing. “You’re such a braggart. How could you catch a wild rabbit? I’ll kneel down in front of you if you can find an egg.”","The others all looked in that direction.","After all, they had been out in the wild for so long and didn’t have much chance to eat meat or fish. They couldn’t stand the mention of wild rabbits. “I’ll take a walk in the woods, too.” The third son ran into the woods as soon as he heard that.","The second son said, “Brother, wait for me!”","The eldest son frowned and shouted, “Be careful! Don’t go too deep! Come back if you can’t find any rabbits!”","“Alright!” The two brothers said in the distance.","“You’re stuff is that way! They’re heading for it!” Little Phoenix was anxious. “Let’s go before they take it away. I’ve painstakingly collected everything myself. It couldn’t be too new or too old. That was so hard!” God knew how many houses it had to visit to find everything.","As for stealing...","How could it be considered stealing? It had done as Feng Wu said and left behind a silver ingot!","Everything was bought!"]},{"number":3757,"title":"Chapter 3757: Adventure (8)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3757: Adventure (8)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Hearing that, Feng Wu took the two kids’ hands and headed for the woods.","According to Little Phoenix, in order to let Feng Wu pretend that she found the bundle by accident, it didn’t hide the bundle very well.","When Feng Wu and the kids walked into the woods, the two men were already gone.","Feng Wu ignored them and headed for her destination.","There were quite a few fruit trees in the woods, and there was even a persimmon tree covered with ripe persimmons.","“Persimmons!”","Sanya was the first to notice it, and she was so excited that she tried to climb up the tree.","Li noticed it as well. She immediately took off her outer robe and spread it out on the ground to hold the persimmons.","They were so close to the edge of the woods that everyone outside could hear them.","Persimmons?!","Hearing the noise, the wife of the third son tossed the wok to her sister-in-law and rushed in.","Seeing that Li had taken off her outer robe, the third daughter-in -law took off hers as well. They had been wearing all the clothes they had, so taking off a layer didn’t really matter.","As she picked, the third daughter-in-law shouted at her three sons, “Jinzhu, Yinzhu, and Tongzhu! Do you want some nice persimmons or not? Give me a hand!”","Unfortunately, most of the persimmons had been destroyed by the wind and rain, and only a few were still edible.","While they were picking the persimmons, Feng Wu said, “I’ll go have a look and see if I can catch a pheasant or a hare.”","Li smiled bitterly. “You’re making things up again. Don’t go too far.”","Feng Wu nodded. “I’ll walk around and get some firewood.”","Only then did Li agree.","As the third daughter-in-law fought over the persimmons with Li, she teased the latter. “Sister-in-law, your niece is so funny. Why did she have to look for a rabbit instead of picking all the persimmons? Haha, what kind of rabbit can she possibly find? Even if she can find it, will she be able to catch it?”","Li was a little displeased, for she really thought of Feng Wu as her niece now.","The third daughter-in-law was elated to see that Li was upset, and she said deliberately, “Sister-in-law, she’s such a poor girl. She’s brought so much bad luck to you all.”","Li threw a dirty look at her sister-in-law. “That’s bullshit!”","Her sister-in-law said, “I’m not. Look at her ragged clothes. She looks like a beggar. She can’t have a good life. I’m telling you...” Just then, they heard a surprised cry a short distance away.","It was Feng Wu!","“What’s going on?! What’s going on?!”","Thinking that Feng Wu had been bitten by a snake, Li slid down the tree and tripped.","It hurt...","Li was almost in tears, but the girl’s safety was at stake and she couldn’t care less about the pain.","She shouted, “Mingjiang! Mingjiang! Come here!”","She ran toward Feng Wu as she shouted, so fast that her shoes flew off.","“Mom! Mom!”","Her two children followed her in a hurry.","However, the third daughter-in-law panicked a little... Was there a snake over there? Well, she wouldn’t go, then. That was so scary...","Now that Li was gone, all the persimmons were hers!","Hence, she went back to picking the persimmons. Li panicked when she saw that Feng Wu wasn’t there.","“Little Feng! Little Feng!”","Li was worried sick.","Hearing her voice, Feng Wu stuck her head out of the tree.. “Aunt, I’m right here!”"]},{"number":3758,"title":"Chapter 3758: Adventure (9)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3758: Adventure (9)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Seeing Feng Wu sitting on the tree, Li felt her knees buckle, and she almost fell to the ground.","“Are you alright?” Li was still anxious.","Feng Wu waved at him. “I’m fine. I’m fine.”","Hearing that, Li let out a breath of relief. At the same time, she wanted to grab the girl and spank her.","“Why did you scream! You’re scaring me out of my wits!” Li pressed a hand on her chest and gasped for air.","The two children imitated her and patted their chests. Their faces were ghastly pale.","Feng Wu smiled and raised the rabbit. “Look! What’s this?!”","“Wow! It’s a gray rabbit!”","“It’s so fat! Let’s roast it!”","The two kids’ eyes were twinkling, and they were almost drooling.","What? A rabbit?","After picking the last persimmon, the third daughter-in-law was about to leave when she heard this. She quickly walked toward Feng Wu and saw the rabbit in her hands.","“Oh my!” She shuddered and almost fell to the ground. “There really is a rabbit!”","Feng Wu looked down at her. “What did you say when we were outside?” The third daughter-in-law said, “What did I say?”","Feng Wu chuckled. ‘You said even if I found an egg, you would kneel in front of me. I’m ready. Kneel.”","The third daughter-in-law was speechless.","Li was amused. “What are you talking about? Get off the tree.”","Feng Wu tossed the hare to Gao Mingjiang and told Li, “I can’t come down yet.”","Li asked anxiously, “Why can’t you come down?”","Feng Wu pointed at something over her head. “There’s something over there.","I’m going to have a look.”","Everyone followed Feng Wu’s gaze.","But from their angle, the leaves were so dense that they couldn’t see anything.","The third daughter-in-law said to Feng Wu, “You’re already very lucky to have a rabbit, Do you expect to find gold or what?”","Feng Wu ignored her and jumped up the tree like a cat.","Although she had lost her spiritual essence, she was still strong enough to handle the tree.","When she was ten meters away, she grabbed something and shouted, “Out of my way! I’m going to throw something down!” Was there really something in the tree?","Everyone moved away when they heard that.","With a thump, Feng Wu threw the bundle on the ground.","Because Feng Wu was dozens of meters above ground, and the ground was damp, the impact left a mark on the ground.","“A bundle? Why is there a bundle on the tree?!” The third daughter-in-law couldn’t believe her eyes.","Immediately, all eyes were on Feng Wu.","Feng Wu looked equally confused. “I was just trying to catch a rabbit, but it was quick-witted. It jumped into a tree, so I climbed up here to catch it. That’s when I saw the bundle. I wonder what’s inside.”","That was right. It was wrapped up tight... What was inside?","“Is it something bad? Something that can get people killed?” The third daughter-in-law couldn’t stand it when other people weren’t better off. She gave Feng Wu a sympathetic look. “Little Feng, you’d better move back.. What if there’s a dead body inside?”"]},{"number":3759,"title":"Chapter 3759: Adventure (10)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3759: Adventure (10)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Feng Wu seemed genuinely frightened. “Aunt, don’t say that!”","The third daughter-in-law glanced at Feng Wu. “I’m telling the truth! Some people don’t bury bodies properly and just put them up on trees! Why did you have to take it down? You’re so evil!”","Feng Wu feigned a frightened face, took a step back, and hid behind Li.","Li looked like a mother hen protecting a chicken. She threw a dirty look at her sister-in-law. “Stop talking nonsense. What if you scare the children?!”","All three children were ghastly pale.","Just then, the Gao family heard the noise and rushed in.","“What’s going on? What’s all the noise?”","The eldest son glared at the others.","The third daughter-in-law said, “I’m so glad you’re here. You can be the judge. Isn’t she a bad girl?”","She pointed at Feng Wu as she spoke. “Someone hid a dead body in a tree, but this girl rushed over and threw it down. It fell to the ground! How can anyone be so wicked? She’s just a little beggar!”","Infuriated, Li wanted to hit the woman.","Old Mrs. Li flared up and glared at Feng Wu. “How dare you touch a dead body? Don’t you know that it’ll poison us if it’s been dead for too long? Your hands are dirty. If you touch our food, we’ll be poisoned to death!”","The third daughter-in-law nodded. “Mother, you’re right. She’s so ill-bred.”","Feng Wu glanced at the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law. Great. That was what she had been waiting for. They had walked into a trap on their own.","“Who told you it was a dead body? I pinched it just then, but it wasn’t a dead body...” Feng Wu feigned a weak voice.","“Who told you it wasn’t a dead body? How could anyone put such a big bundle on a tree? What else could it be?!” The third daughter-in-law wouldn’t believe it. Right now, she had her hands on her waist and was ready to go all out.","“We’ll know what’s inside after we open it.” Gao Mingjiang glanced at his mother and sister-in-law.","Old Mrs. Gao smirked. “No matter what’s in there, it’s Feng’s. Whatever bad luck it is, it’s hers!”","Lady Gu nodded. “That’s right. We can’t let that girl ruin our family’s good luck! ”","Feng Wu frowned. “I think there’s something good inside!”","The third daughter in law smirked. “Good stuff? That’s hilarious!”","Granny Gao was still thinking about the 20 taels of silver, and she was furious at Feng Wu. “Even if it’s gold and silver, the Gao family won’t take anything from you! If it’s bad luck. I hope God won’t blame it on the Gao family.” After that, she cast a stern look at her sons. “Dig a hole in the ground!” Dig a hole? Why? Everyone looked at her in bewilderment.","Old Mrs. Gao glared at her third son. “Didn’t your wife tell you? There’s a dead body inside! Bury it!”","After that, she turned to leave.","Gao Mingjiang didn’t know what to say. They hadn’t even opened it yet, and they were already talking about dead bodies.","Without another word, he unwrapped the bundle.","The contents spilled all over the floor.","“Ah!!!” The third daughter-in-law screamed.."]},{"number":3760,"title":"Chapter 3760: Surprise (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3760: Surprise (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","“Ah!!!” The third daughter-in-law screamed.","Everyone jumped at her voice.","They were astonished when they saw what had rolled out of the package.","“The bedroll! It’s so thick!”","“And what’s this? Rice! Fine rice!” “What’s that? There’s a bow!”","“And...","Everyone was astonished when they examined everything.","Before they knew it, everyone had gathered around.","“There are so many of them! Where did they come from?!” Old Mrs. Gao was the first to react and tried to take them away.","Seeing the old lady run toward the bundle, her other three daughters-in-law all take off, trying to outrun the old lady.","The old lady was furious. “Get out of my way! This belongs to the family! Stop trying to take it! I’m not dead yet!”","Feng Wu gave them a half-smile.","Gao Mingjiang frowned and shouted, “Stop it!”","He was the most capable man in the team.","Moreover, he was infuriated, and his voice frightened everyone. Everyone fell silent.","Old Mrs. Gao was a little scared of her fourth son as well, so she turned to Gao","Mingjiang. “Mingjiang, what are you doing...”","Gao Mingjiang stared at the old lady. “Is that yours? You can’t take it!”","Old Mrs. Gao wouldn’t have it. “Of course it’s mine! Didn’t you find it? What’s yours is ours!”","Li almost laughed. “But we don’t own it!”","The old lady glared at her. “Shut up! You have no right to speak here!”","Li felt aggrieved. Despite her grievance, she toughened up and said, “Why can’t I say anything? Miss Feng found it, so it has to be hers. No one is allowed to take it away!”","Of course, the old lady wouldn’t accept it!","But before she could say anything, Gao Mingjiang spoke again. “My wife is right. Miss Feng found the bundle, so everything is hers. No one is allowed to take anything from her!”","The old lady wouldn’t admit it. “But isn’t she ours now?!”","Li was so angry that she laughed. “How can she be ours? She’s only pretending to be my niece from my mother’s side!”","The old lady didn’t know what to say. She had made up an identity and thought that it was real.","The old lady said, “She’s teamed up with us before!”","Li said, “She’s paid you for your service. If that doesn’t count, just spit out all the flour you ate!”","That woman! Old Mrs. Gao wanted to slap Li.","Li smirked. “Go ahead! I dare you! Touch me, and my husband will split up with you! We’ll go our separate ways!”","She had never been this tough before, but for some unknown reason, she felt that she shouldn’t have been bullied like this when Feng Wu was around.","Miss Feng was right.","Kind? Why bother? She didn’t want to make other people happy anymore.","At that thought, she glared at Old Mrs. Gao and wouldn’t give in.","Old Mrs. Gao was a little frightened.","Why was her daughter-in-law, who used to be so easy to bully, so angry all of a sudden? She couldn’t control Li anymore.","Just then, the third daughter-in-law mumbled something.."]},{"number":3761,"title":"Chapter 3761: Surprise (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3761: Surprise (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Just then, the third daughter-in-law mumbled, “Stop saying the bundle belongs to the girl. I think you just want it for yourself.”","She wasn’t loud, but Li heard her.","Li smirked. “We’re still one family. If I take the bundle, you’ll only take advantage of me. I’m not that stupid.”","The third daughter-in-law said, “You!”","The third son didn’t want the quarrel to go on, fearing that Gao Mingjiang would say that they were going to split up and abandon them, so he tried to smooth things over. “Fine, fine. It’s just a few things. There’s no need to argue. We’re all family here.","“How about this? I’ll give all the big pieces to Mingjiang. As for the condiments, Mother will be in charge of them.","“I went through a lot of trouble to find those things!” Little Phoenix shouted in Feng Wu’s ear. “How dare these people take it? Slap him!”","Feng Wu smirked and said, “You can take half of the condiments. I’ll take everything else. No one is allowed to take anything from me without my permission!”","Although Feng Wu didn’t have any spiritual essence now, she was still very intimidating when she exerted her power.","In the end, most of the things were moved to Gao Mingjiang’s carriage.","“Rabbit! Fat rabbit!” Xiaoshu and Sanya almost jumped to their feet.","“Come, let’s roast some rabbits.”","Feng Wu led them to where the stove was set up.","Gao Mingjiang went to the creek, washed the rabbit paper, and handed it to Feng Wu. Feng Wu then smeared a layer of honey on the rabbit. As for where it came from, of course, it was in the big bundle.","The rabbit was roasted with honey, and the aroma filled the air.","The fourth branch of the family had its own stove, and the rest of the family shared a bigger stove nearby. The aroma soon filled the air.","Other people might be able to stand it, but the third daughter-in-law couldn’t stop complaining. “Why are they eating rabbits and we’re eating plain pancakes? I won’t have it!”","Old Mrs. Gao was equally frustrated.","The others weren’t too happy either.","However, Feng Wu only glanced at them and showed no intention to share the food with them.","She divided the rabbit into four parts. One for herself, one for Gao Mingjiang, one for Li, and one for the two children.","There wasn’t much meat left after the entrails were removed, and the meat had shrunk significantly after it was cooked. Therefore, the rabbit in Feng Wu’s hand was only the size of her palm.","Gao Mingjiang looked over his shoulder and sighed when he saw how eager his mother was. He went up to old Mrs. Gao and said, “Mother, you can have mine.”","The others thought that the old lady would at least pretend that she didn’t want it.","But in fact, the eldest son, who hadn’t eaten meat for a long time, snatched the meat out of Gao Mingjiang’s hand and said coldly, “You’re useless! Is that all you got?”","The other three families had a lot of children!","Gao Mingjiang smiled bitterly and cursed himself for being so stupid. It had been a while since he ate meat, and he had just been scolded for sharing.","He shook his head and went back to the fire. As for how to split the rabbit, it was up to old Mrs. Gao.","After Gao Mingjiang went back, Li and the two children felt sorry for him.","Gao Mingjiang patted their hands. “Don’t worry. Mom has always been like this.”","Li said grumpily, “I can’t control my temper anymore.”","Gao Mingjiang smiled bitterly. “We’ll see when we get to our destination.","Nothing can be predicted while we’re on the road..”"]},{"number":3762,"title":"Chapter 3762: Fright (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3762: Fright (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Li nodded. She knew what Gao Mingjiang meant.","“We haven’t settled down in the Northern Yan Kingdom yet, and we don’t know if we’ll live or die...” She heaved a long sigh, her eyes filled with sorrow.","Both children gave their mother concerned looks.","Sensing their uneasiness, Li rubbed their heads and smiled bitterly. “You guys should eat now. We’ll be on our way when you’re full.”","Sanya asked, “Mom, will we be in danger?”","Before Li could say anything, Gao Mingjiang said, “Dad’s here. There’s no danger. Just eat and sleep. Everything will be fine when we get to Northern","Yan.”","Sanya and Xiaoshu nodded solemnly.","Seeing that Sanya had stopped eating after two bites, Li asked, “Why won’t you eat?”","With a solemn look on her face, Sanya said, “Mother, we don’t know how dangerous this journey will be, and we don’t know if we’ll have anything to eat in the future... I want to save my food and take another bite when I’m starving...”","“Honey...” Li sighed and pulled Sanya into her arms. “Things will get better.","We’ll have enough food and warm clothes when we get there...’","It was late autumn, and the air was colder in the middle of the night.","Gao Mingjiang’s family was better prepared. They used to have two bedrolls, but because the other families didn’t have enough bedding, the old lady took one of them and gave it to her third son.","Before Feng Wu arrived, Gao Mingjiang’s family had been shivering on their","1.5m bedding. The two children slept in the middle, while Li and Gao Mingjiang, who had been sleeping on either side of the bed, were mostly exposed.","Now that Feng Wu had found a new bedroll, she took the two kids and shared a bed. Li and Gao Mingjiang shared another. Everybody slept well now.","The family found a leeward spot behind a big rock and were ready to sleep when they heard footsteps.","“Sister-in-law...","It sounded like the second daughter-in-law, who didn’t talk much. Feng Wu yawned and thought to herself.","Sanya, who had been sleeping soundly in Feng Wu’s arms, woke up right away and was on the alert! She looked like a bristling cat.","Xiaoshu was alarmed as well.","Feng Wu looked at them in bewilderment and asked in a low voice, “What’s wrong?”","Throwing her arms around Feng Wu, Sanya asked nervously, “Sister Feng, are we going to lose our bed?”","In the dark, Feng Wu saw that Sanya was looking at her nervously, and so was","Xiaoshu.","Feng Wu was confused. “How can someone take our bed?”","Sanya said, “Can we keep our bed, then?”","She knew by now how capable Sister Feng was. Even her grandmother wouldn’t be her match.","Feng Wu nodded. “Of course. Why should we give our own bed to someone else? What should we sleep on?”","In order to avoid detection, Feng Wu had destroyed her own cultivation and was too weak to withstand the cold.","The two kids nodded immediately, their eyes twinkling.","By then, Li had left with her sister-in-law.","They didn’t go very far because it would be dangerous.","That distance was enough for Feng Wu to hear their conversation.","After praising Li’s family, the second daughter-in-law went on crying about how difficult it had been for them. In the end, she turned to Li for help.","“Sister-in-law, there’s nothing else I can do.. Otherwise, I wouldn’t have...”"]},{"number":3763,"title":"Chapter 3763: Fright (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3763: Fright (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","“I really have no choice. Otherwise, I wouldn’t have come to beg you at this hour...","The second daughter-in-law said anxiously, “Sister-in-law, I know you don’t have much either, but there are so many people in my family, and we only have one bedroll. We don’t have enough duvets for the children alone, but you have two...”","Li frowned.","Before, she was a cowardly woman, but after the near-death experience with her two children, and after seeing how tough Feng Wu was, she had unknowingly become tougher.","She used to never say no, but now, she shook her head. “Sister-in-law, as you know, I don’t have much either...”","Her sister-in-law said, “I know, but you can turn the duvet sideways. That’ll cover you all.”","Li frowned. “Sister-in-law, what are you talking about? There aren’t just the four of us. Feng is with us too. How can she sleep in the same bed with me and my husband? You’re talking nonsense!”","The second daughter-in-law said, “She’s just a little beggar. We’re not family. You don’t have to...","“Sister-in-law!” Li scolded her. “She’s my niece! Not an outsider! Moreover, we’ve given away a bedroll already! Why should we give away another one? I won’t have it!”","Her sister-in-law was a little displeased. “Li...”","Li waved her off. “You don’t have to say another word! I’m not lending you anything!”","She then turned to leave.","They raised their voices this time, so many people heard them.","So, it really was about the bedroll... Many people thought to themselves.","The look on the second daughter-in-law’s face kept changing as she watched Li leave.","However, the anger soon disappeared from her face, and she went up to the old lady with a smile.","When she walked past Gao Mingjiang’s family, she smiled at the others and seemed to be in a great mood.","However, Sanya grabbed Feng Wu’s hand anxiously, as did Xiaoshu.","After she left, Sanya and Xiaoshu looked nervously at Feng Wu.","Feng Wu smiled. “No one can take away what’s ours. Don’t worry.”","A few steps away, the third daughter-in-law smirked at her husband. “I told you already. Your second brother’s wife isn’t as simple as she looks. Look how capable she is. She can ask for a bed with a wave of her hand.”","Her husband threw a dirty look at her. “Shut up! Have you forgotten? Who did you take that bedroll from? The one we’re sleeping in now belongs to Mingjiang!”","Her wife cringed and didn’t dare to speak, fearing that her bedroll would be taken away.","Just then, the second daughter-in-law went up to the old lady, who had been angry at the noise, but the second daughter-in-law was able to appease the old lady with a few words.","The old lady frowned and stared at her. “Are you sure?!”","The second daughter-in-law nodded. “I saw it. It’s really two meters long. It can fit a lot of people.","“Mum, look at my seven children. They’re all freezing. If there’s a two-meter-long duvet, they’ll be able to get through. Mum, what do you think...","The old lady rolled her eyes at her daughter-in-law. “You know what Li is like now. She’s so tough that she can talk back to me!”","The second daughter-in-law cajoled the old lady until her head swam.","“Mom, all seven of them are your grandchildren...”"]},{"number":3764,"title":"Chapter 3764: The Row (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3764: The Row (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","“Mum, my seven children are all your grandsons and granddaughters...” The second daughter-in-law gave the old lady a pleading look.","Old Mrs. Gao didn’t like Gao Mingjiang’s family to begin with, and she was infuriated by her second daughter-in -law’s provocation. She rose to her feet and grabbed a stick as thick as her arm.","Gao Mingjiang had made it for her so that it would be easier for her to walk around.","“Bring out the three boys!” Leaning on a stick, old Mrs. Gao walked very fast.","The second daughter-in-law was secretly elated and immediately had her three boys follow the old lady.","The three boys didn’t like the idea at first, but their mother whispered in their ears, telling them that there were warm duvets in the fourth branch.","It was late autumn, and they were in the middle of nowhere. Everyone was freezing, and the three boys couldn’t stand the cold. They all ran toward the old lady.","By then, old Mrs. Gao was standing next to Gao Mingjiang’s family.","Gao Mingjiang’s family must have heard all the noise, but no one wanted to talk to the old lady and wanted her to leave as soon as possible. As a result, Gao Mingjiang ignored her.","Old Mrs. Gao couldn’t stand her son’s attitude, so she hit the bedroll with her stick.","She couldn’t bring herself to hit her son, so she hit Li instead.","Gao Mingjiang shielded Li with his own body. With a thump, the thick stick hit him on the back. “Mom!”","Gao Mingjiang had a temper as well. He threw a dirty look at the old lady. “What are you doing in the middle of the night? Are you going to let us sleep or not?!”","Seeing that she had hit her fourth son, the old lady felt a little guilty, but she flared up when she saw what Gao Mingjiang was doing. “Sleep? I want to sleep, but you won’t let me!”","After that, the old lady told the three boys of the second branch of the family, “Do you see that bedroll? You can sleep there!”","She turned to leave after that.","Seeing the warm bed, the three boys cried out in joy and rushed toward it.","The old lady smirked inwardly.","If Li wouldn’t lend the bedroll, she could just let the boys sleep here. She would let them freeload off Gao Mingjiang’s food and finish all the flour.","Both Xiaoshu and Sanya looked furious.","“Dad!”","“Mom!”","The three boys were tugging at the duvet, but so were Xiaoshu and Sanya. It was obvious that the two kids weren’t the three boys’ match, and they were almost in tears.","Li was exasperated and yelled at the three boys. “What are you doing? Let go of the duvet!”","The old lady struck down at Li with her thick stick. “This is the Gao family’s business. It’s none of your business! Let go of the bedroll!”","Seeing that a fight was about to break out over a bed, Feng Wu was speechless.","She really didn’t expect that they would quarrel over a bed.","Little Phoenix didn’t know what to say.","On second thought, Feng Wu realized that surviving in this vast wilderness was probably their biggest problem.","It was precisely because of this that the people monitoring the sky and trying to find her would never expect that she would be in such a team, which was why she was safe.","Feng Wu had wanted to kick the three boys away, but she didn’t plan to do that now. With Gao Mingjiang around, he would definitely protect his wife and children.","As expected..."]},{"number":3765,"title":"Chapter 3765: The Row (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3765: The Row (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","As expected, Gao Mingjiang grabbed the thick stick and bellowed at the old lady. “Mother! What are you doing?!”","After that, he snatched the stick from the old lady and threw it at the three boys.","They all burst into tears when they were hit by the stick.","“Dad!”","“Mom!”","“My uncle is killing us! Help!”","The old lady was shocked by what she saw.","Her fourth son...","Gao Mingjiang had never been obedient, but he had never been this merciless either!","“Go away!” Gao Mingjiang tossed the three boys to their father, who had just arrived.","“Mingjiang!” The second eldest son was furious. “What kind of uncle are you?”","Gao Mingjiang smirked. “I’d like to know what kind of a father you are! You lost your bedroll, so you’ve been asking my family for everything all the time!”","His brother blushed.","That was indeed the case.","They didn’t have much money to begin with. Moreover, they were in such a hurry that they didn’t bring many belongings with them when they took off. As a result, they had to rely on Gao Mingjiang for almost all their expenses on this trip.","However...","“Yours is the Gao family’s, isn’t it? You don’t own anything!” Old Mrs. Gao glared at Gao Mingjiang.","Gao Mingjiang smirked. “I’ll leave without taking anything, then! I don’t want anything! I’m leaving this family!”","“No!” Old Mrs. Gao refused outright.","Gao Mingjiang was in charge of everyone’s well-being and safety, and he wouldn’t be allowed to leave.","The other brothers shook their heads as well.","Gao Mingjiang smirked and told his wife, “Pack up. We’re leaving tonight.”","Li was bewildered, but she still followed Gao Mingjiang’s order and started moving the things into the carriage.","Feng Wu was amused. These people were so unreasonable. Since they all depended on Gao Mingjiang, why did they pick on him all the time?","Did these people think that Gao Mingjiang wouldn’t abandon them just because they were his mother and brothers? They were too confident in themselves.","Feng Wu felt sorry for Gao Mingjiang.","Soon, everything was packed. Li walked up to Gao Mingjiang and tugged at his sleeve.","Gao Mingjiang looked at old Mrs. Gao, who was so angry that her face was livid.","She stared at Gao Mingjiang. “Are you really leaving?”","Gao Mingjiang nodded. “I have to protect my wife and children because no one else will.”","Old Mrs. Gao asked, ‘What about your mother? Are you going to leave me behind?”","Gao Mingjiang said, “My three brothers can look after you.”","Old Mrs. Gao said, “No, they won’t.”","Feng Wu snickered. The old lady knew perfectly well how unreliable her other sons were.","Gao Mingjiang remained unperturbed.","Seeing the determination in her son’s eyes, old Mrs. Gao panicked for no reason. It was as if she had lost her faith.","Old Mrs. Gao burst into tears.","“Gao Mingjiang, how could you do this? How could you abandon your mother? How could I have such an unfilial son? If I had known, I would have drowned you in the toilet! You heartless man!” Old Mrs. Gao pounded her chest and stomped her foot, rolling around on the ground.","Gao Mingjiang gave her a long look and suddenly dropped to his knees.."]},{"number":3766,"title":"Chapter 3766: Leave (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3766: Leave (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Gao Mingjiang gave her a long look and suddenly dropped to his knees.","Thump, thump, thump.","Gao Mingjiang kowtowed three times, then jumped into the carriage.","“Hya!”","Gao Mingjiang drove the carriage away.","What?!","The Gao family was dumbfounded.","Gao Mingjiang had mentioned several times that if they picked on his family again, they would go their separate ways, but no one believed him. They thought he wouldn’t leave them behind.","Even if he would abandon his brothers and sisters-in-law, he would never abandon his mother!","But now...","“Mom! Mom! Mingjiang is gone!”","Seeing that the old lady was still standing there in disbelief, her second son rushed over, grabbed her by the shoulder, and shook her. “Mum, wake up!” For a moment, everyone was shouting at her.","Only then did old Mrs. Gao come back to herself. She was frustrated when she saw that the carriage was only a black dot in the dark.","“So be it! We’ll do just fine without him!” The old lady smirked. “We don’t need to follow them! Just let them go! We won’t die without them!”","She sat down on the ground and snorted.","Realizing that Gao Mingjiang had really abandoned them, the others were angry as well. They snorted and said, “Mother is right. So be it. I’m sure we’ll be fine.”","After that, they all went back to bed.","“Brother, I...” The second son looked at his older brother guiltily.","The oldest son patted him on the shoulder. “Brother, it’s not your fault. Mingjiang is heartless.”","The third son nodded as well. “That’s right. How can he do that? He’s so protective of his wife and children! Aren’t our children his nieces and nephews? He’s so selfish!”","“Stop it!”","An angry voice broke the silence. Everyone looked up and saw that it was Gao Mingkun.","His eldest brother glared at him. “Gao Mingkun, what are you doing?!”","Throwing a rod over his shoulder, Gao Mingkun smirked. “I’m going to find my brother.”","“How dare you?!” This eldest brother glared at him.","None of the other three could fight. If Gao Mingkun was gone, no one would be able to protect them.","Gao Mingkun snorted and wanted to leave.","However, old Mrs. Gao stopped him with teary eyes. “Mingkun, are you leaving me as well? Do you not care about me anymore?”","Gao Mingkun frowned. “Mother, it’s not that I don’t want to look after you, but you’ve crossed the line!","“Brother Mingjiang has been doing everything for us this whole time. We’ve been eating his food and spending his money. Mother, why did you take all the money from him and insist on keeping it to yourself? Is that even fair?”","“Of course, it’s fair!” Old Mrs. Gao smirked. “He’s my son, so he has to work for me. What’s his belongs to the family. So what if we all use it together? If I don’t take the money from him, your other brothers will starve to death!”","The other sons all nodded.","Old Mrs.. Gao said, “If he’s so capable, it’s only natural that he looks after his brothers and their children!”"]},{"number":3767,"title":"Chapter 3767: Leaving (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3767: Leaving (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","The other sons nodded again.","Gao Mingkun was furious.","“You leeches! You’ve been feeding him money without even saying thank you! My brother is right to leave! I wouldn’t give you a dime if I were him! I’m leaving, too!”","Gao Mingkun stared at them.","All his three older brothers were lazy, hypocritical, and selfish. They took advantage of Gao Mingjiang and never appreciated his kindness.","“I’m leaving, too!” Gao Mingkun stormed off.","“You’re not leaving!”","“You can’t leave!”","Her brothers and sisters-in -law grabbed him in unison.","Without Gao Mingjiang, they could only count on Gao Mingkun. If even Gao Mingkun abandoned them, they wouldn’t be able to survive.","“Mother...” The second daughter-in-law tugged at the old lady.","Old Mrs. Gao found her second daughter-in-law quite annoying at the moment. Had it not been for her, Gao Mingjiang would never have left.","But under the circumstances, the old lady didn’t have time to blame anyone.","She stared at Gao Mingkun. “Are you leaving? If you do that, I’ll kill myself in front of you!”","But Gao Mingkun only smirked.","This wasn’t the first time that the old lady had threatened to kill herself. Every time Gao Mingjiang wouldn’t do as she said, she would threaten him with that. Gradually, Gao Mingjiang became distant from his mother.","Anyway, she was all bark and no bite...","Gao Mingkun didn’t think much of it and still wanted to leave.","Old Mrs. Gao gritted her teeth. She recalled how decisive Gao Mingjiang had been when he left, and the thought pained her. Somehow, she summoned up her courage and cried out.","Thump!","She smashed her head into a wall nearby.","“Mom!”","The second daughter-in-law only cried out after the old lady smashed her head into the rock. She could have stopped the old lady in time.","With what had happened to the old lady, everyone turned around in a hurry, only to see blood gushing out of the old lady’s forehead.","The eldest son smacked Gao Mingkun on the head. “Are you trying to kill","Mom?!”","“Mom, Mom... Please don’t die!” The second daughter-in-law rushed over and threw her arms around the old lady.","Old Mrs. Gao was actually fine. She was about to scold Gao Mingkun when her second daughter-in-law whispered something in her ear. The old lady immediately changed her mind and pretend to be very weak.","“Mum’s breathing is very weak! She’s dying!” Her second daughter-in-law shouted at Gao Mingkun.","Gao Mingkun rushed to her side. “Mom! Mom!”","Old Mrs. Gao opened her eyes and gave Gao Mingkun a long look. She only said, “Mingkun, I want to see your brother one last time...” Tears rolled down the old lady’s cheeks as she spoke.","Gao Mingkun was flustered.","He had thought that the old lady was only putting on an act, but...","“I’ll go get him now!”","Gao Mingkun jumped into a carriage and dashed off.","Old Mrs. Gao only sat up after Gao Mingkun left.","Everyone looked at her.","Old Mrs. Gao snorted. “Did he think he could take off with his little family and leave all of us behind? In his dreams!”","“That’s right!” The third daughter-in-law nodded. “Don’t even think about abandoning us! We’re his responsibility!”","However, no matter how long the old lady waited, Gao Mingkun never showed up.","A few hours passed... They woke up at dawn, but Gao Mingkun still hadn’t come back, nor had Gao Mingjiang What was going on?"]},{"number":3768,"title":"Chapter 3768: What’s Going On? (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3768: What’s Going On? (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","What was going on?","However, old Mrs. Gao and the others couldn’t care less about Gao Mingkun now, for they had run into some new trouble.","Because while they were sleeping...","A group of people were sneaking toward them.","“Boss, I’ve figured it out. They have two capable sons, but they’re nowhere to be found. That family is very vulnerable now!”","The speaker was a young man.","He had approached the third daughter-in -law of the Gao family, pretending to be weak. He then gave her a steamed bun and got everything he needed to know from her.","He knew Gao Mingjiang was gone, Gao Mingkun had gone to look for him, and everyone else was very upset.","The young man named MO Ping told everything to his leader.","They were a team of bandits that had entrenched themselves in Flying Tiger Mountain.","They used to be from good families, but because they couldn’t survive in the wilderness anymore, they turned into bandits and robbed passersby in this area.","However, there weren’t many of them, so they only robbed small groups.","If a passing group seemed tough, they wouldn’t dare to make a move.","“Have you gathered all the information? Is it correct?” The leader stared at MO Ping.","MO Ping grinned. “Boss, I handed a woman a steamed bun, and that stupid woman told me everything. They’re a family. There’s an old lady, her five sons, and their wives and kids. The two youngest sons are the most capable ones, but they’re gone. The rest of them are all useless.”","‘Good!” Boss Ding patted MO Ping on the shoulder. “If you succeed this time, you’ll be rewarded!”","MO Ping asked excitedly, “Boss, can I have a horse?”","“Why not?!” With a wave of his hand, Ding said, “Follow me!”","There were only over a dozen or so bandits, and they carefully made their way toward the Gao family’s campsite.","Had it been any other day, someone would have kept watch, and Gao Mingjiang would have arranged everything.","But now that Gao Mingjiang was gone, no one else was there to give instructions. They went to bed, snoring loudly.","Seeing that the members of the Gao family were fast asleep, MO Ping looked at Ding and made a throat-slitting gesture.","“Should I cut their heads off?” That was what MO Ping meant.","Ding pondered for a moment.","He couldn’t help but recall how intimidating Gao Mingjiang was, and he shuddered.","“If we don’t wake them up, we’ll grab the thing and leave. If we wake them up, we’ll kill them!” Ding decided not to go too far.","The others nodded in agreement.","They weren’t born criminals, so they didn’t try to kill anyone.","The members of the Gao family were fast asleep. They didn’t even wake up when the carriage was driven away, let alone the horses.","Someone cried out, “Stop!”","It was Gao Mingkun!","Not only did he frighten Ding and his men, but it also woke up the Gao family.","“Who’s there? What’s going on?”","The eldest son didn’t like being woken up.","By then, Gao Mingkun had dashed off with a stick. “The robbers have taken the carriages! Stop them!” Robbers?","The carriages?","The sleepy members of the Gao family woke up from their reverie. They were dumbfounded when they saw what was going on.."]},{"number":3769,"title":"Chapter 3769: What Was Going On? (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3769: What Was Going On? (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","They were astonished when they saw what was going on.","The carriages carrying all their luggage were gone.","Gao Mingkun was chasing after them.","In front of Gao Mingkun, a group of people were driving the carriages away. They were moving so fast that Gao Mingkun couldn’t keep up.","Those people seemed to be very pleased with themselves, and they all turned around to show off.","“The robbers! !! ”","Only then did the members of the Gao family realize that they had been robbed.","“Ahhh! Our carriages!”","“Food! All our food is there!”","“And everything we’ve saved! And the silver!”","Without the carriages, how were they supposed to travel?","How were they going to survive without food?","Without money, what would they do from now on?","Even old Mrs. Gao’s silver was in the carriage, so she ran as fast as she could.","She shouted at the top of her lungs as she ran, asking the carriages to stop.","The other members of the Gao family finally heard her scream. They ran as fast as they could and shouted the same thing.","They tried everything, from threats to bribes, but to no avail.","Not only weren’t they going to give back the carriages, but half a dozen people even jumped out and surrounded Gao Mingkun, beating him up.","“We’re taking these carriages. If you don’t want to die, get lost!”","In the end, MO Ping kicked Gao Mingkun, jumped into the carriage, and left with the others.","Gao Mingkun curled up to protect his head and internal organs. He was injured in many places and even had a broken bone.","He lay on his stomach and couldn’t even move a finger.","He could only watch as the group of people rode off in their carriages until they turned into black dots in the distance...","By then, the Gao family had finally caught up with him.","Seeing Gao Mingkun lying on the ground, the second son was worried sick. He bellowed at Gao Mingkun, “Where are our carriages?!”","Immediately, everyone gave Gao Mingkun accusing looks.","Gao Mingkun was covered in wounds, and it was so painful that he couldn’t utter a word.","The second son shouted at Gao Ming, “I’m talking to you! Where are the carriages?!”","Gao Mingkun shook his head. “They’ve taken the carriages away.”","Gone?!","The second son was furious. He pointed at Gao Mingkun and scolded him. “How could you let the carriages get stolen? Do you know that they contain everything we have?”","The third son shouted anxiously, “There’s food up there! We’ve saved up so much!","“How are we supposed to proceed without a carriage? Are we going to walk on foot?!”","Poor Gao Mingkun. He was so angry that he could barely breathe.","“You...”","At that moment, his sisters-in-law finally arrived with old Mrs. Gao. Hearing that the carriages had really been taken and that everything was gone, the old lady was so furious that she fainted.","“Mom!”","The second son steadied the old lady and scolded Gao Mingkun.. “Mingkun, you lost the carriages! Do as you see fit!”"]},{"number":3770,"title":"Chapter 3770: Vomiting Blood (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3770: Vomiting Blood (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Gao Mingkun cried out and spat out a mouthful of blood.","Somehow, he found the strength to stand up.","Sensing the change in Gao Mingkun’s attitude, the second son felt intimidated. He glared at Gao Mingkun. “What now? I’m your second eldest brother. Are you going to defy me now?!”","Gao Mingkun stood there unsteadily and smirked at his second brother.","The second son gave the oldest one a pleading look and tried to ask the latter for support.","The eldest son stepped out and frowned. “Let’s treat Mingkun’s wounds first.” “But where can we find the medicine?” The second son shook his head.","The eldest son frowned. “We have to treat him even if I don’t have any medicine. Here are my clothes. Tear it into strips and bandage Mingkun’s wound.”","He then took off his top, tore it into pieces, and bandaged Gao Mingkun’s wounds himself.","Gao Mingkun was going to leave, but his brother stopped him. Moreover, he was too severely injured to leave, so he had to stay.","“What are we going to do now?” Everyone turned to the eldest son for help. The eldest son frowned. “What do you think we should do?”","The third son said, “No matter what, we have to get our luggage back! And the food and the carriages!”","His wife said, “That’s right! It belongs to our family! We can’t let them take those things away!”","The eldest son glanced at her. “Are you going to take it back yourself?”","“Well...” The fierce couple stopped talking altogether.","“Well, we can let Mingjiang do that...” the third daughter-in-law mumbled. “He was able to take our horses back from those people, and he can do the same now.”","“That’s right! Let’s go find Mingjiang!”","Old Mrs. Gao was furious. “No!”","She had made it clear that she had fallen out with her unfilial fourth son!","“Mom, are we going to starve to death just like that? Do you know how far we have to go?”","Her three sons glared at her, and there was nothing she could do.","Just like the old lady herself, those sons could be ruthless to their family members.","“Where’s your brother? Take us to him!” Everyone looked at Gao Mingkun.","Gao Mingkun knew that he had to go to Gao Mingjiang now. After all, they were all family. Seeing how miserable they were, his brother would probably give in.","“I know where my brother is. I’ll show you the way.” Gao Mingkun’s right arm was broken, but his legs were fine, so he could still walk.","He led the team, and the others followed him.","At first, they were all high-spirited and only wanted to catch up with Gao Mingjiang, so they ran as fast as they could.","But...","They were lazy people in nature. As they grew tired, their high spirits soon faded.","They had been traveling in carriages the whole time and had never needed to walk on their own. “I’m starving...” “I’m so thirsty...”","“I’m so tired...","Many of them were frustrated.","Before long, the third daughter-in-law couldn’t take it anymore. She sat down on the ground and said, “I’m not taking one more step! I’ll die if I keep going!” As soon as she sat down, the others sat down as well and didn’t want to move.."]},{"number":3771,"title":"Chapter 3771: Vomit Blood (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3771: Vomit Blood (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","As soon as the third daughter-in-law sat down, the others sat down as well and wouldn’t move a muscle.","They were in a sorry state.","They were covered in sweat, and they were hot, thirsty, and exhausted...","“I can’t walk anymore. I can’t feel my legs. My carriage...” The third daughter-in-law started crying.","Her second sister-in-law looked exhausted as well. Seeing this, she couldn’t help but ask, “Our carriages have been fine this whole time. Why was it stolen last night?”","The third daughter-in-law said, “It’s all because Mingjiang is gone! If he’s here, these thieves won’t dare to pick on us!”","Her second sister-in-law nodded. “It’s all Mingjiang’s fault...”","However, before she could finish, the third daughter-in-law asked, “What did you say?”","Her second daughter-in-law said, “Am I wrong? It’s all Mingjiang’s fault. He left us behind...’","It was already evening, and they had been walking for most of the day without any food or water. They were all exhausted. However, the third daughter-in-law suddenly jumped up and slapped her sister-in-law!","There was a crisp smack!","The second daughter-in-law was dumbfounded. “You!”","The third daughter-in-law said, “You’ve reminded me! Why did Mingjiang leave? It was all because of you! If it hadn’t been for what happened earlier, would his family have left?!”","The second daughter-in-law felt a little guilty. “What are you talking about?","What did I do? I only tried to borrow the duvet. What did I do?”","“Borrow a duvet? You were fine when there was no duvet around! Why did you have to borrow one now?!”","“You make it sound like you’ve never tried to take things from Mingjiang before. You took advantage of them just the same!”","“Not only won’t you admit your mistake, but you’re also blaming me! Wang","Cuihua, I’m going to make you pay!”","“Wu Caimiao, I’m not afraid of you!”","“Ah!”","The two of them ran into each other and started tearing each other’s hair. It was a fierce fight.","The two of them used to be on friendly terms because they had worked together to set up Li, their common enemy. However, now that Li was gone, the two of them started fighting.","“Stop it! Aren’t we having enough trouble already? Stop it!” The eldest daughter-in-law was speechless. She didn’t know what to do because no matter which one she tried to stop, it would be like she was siding with","someone.","“Mother, aren’t you going to do something about it?” She turned to the old lady for help.","The old lady had a cold look in her eyes, and no one knew what she was thinking.","As for her sons, they had all gone out to look for food, saying that they were going hunting... No one knew when they would be back.","The two daughters-in-law were finally tired. They lay on the ground and gasped for air.","No one made a sound, and no one knew what the others were thinking.","The first day...","They survived the cold and starvation.","The second day...","They woke up from their despair and resumed their journey.","But they still couldn’t find Gao Mingjiang’s family. They were so hungry that they couldn’t see straight. “If only Mingjiang was here...”","“If Mingjiang were here, we wouldn’t be like this...”","“If it hadn’t been for Brother Mingjiang, we would have been in this state two days after we set out,” Gao Mingkun said indifferently.","No one said a word.","“Brother Mingjiang saved our lives! You knew that, but you just wouldn’t admit"]},{"number":3772,"title":"Chapter 3772: Plague (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3772: Plague (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Gao Mingkun glared at them. “You just won’t admit it! You’ve been giving him a hard time, bullying him, and stealing from his family! If I were my brother, I","would have abandoned you already! I wouldn’t have waited until now!” Before, none of the others would admit that.","But now, without Gao Mingjing, they were all starving. Their legs were unsteady, and they were so thirsty that they thought their mouths were on fire. All they wanted to do was cry.","The third son said, “But where is Mingjing? Where is my brother?”","The second son said, “If we find Mingjing, I won’t take advantage of him anymore.”","The others nodded as well and pleaded, “Where is Mingjing? I know we deserve this, but he has abandoned our mother as well.”","Gao Mingkun said indifferently, “Who knows? I didn’t catch up with him either.”","Hearing that, the others lost all hope.","They hadn’t eaten anything in three days. When they were hungry, they would eat the grass on the ground, but the grass was dry, and they spat it out as soon as it hit their mouths.","“Look! There’s a rat!”","The third son suddenly shouted and dashed off.","There was indeed a rat a short distance away, but it was obviously dead and already stank.","But for the sake of a dead rat, the brothers almost tried to kill one another. Old Mrs. Gao sat on the ground and cried, but there was nothing she could do. “Let’s make some soup for everyone with this rat!”","They carried the pot with them earlier, so it wasn’t stolen with the carriage. Gao Mingkun frowned. “No, it’s a dead rat. You can’t eat it. You’ll get sick!”","However, the people of the Gao family were so hungry that they couldn’t see straight. They didn’t care if they would get sick. If they didn’t eat, they would die.","Hence, the dead rat was thrown into a pot, and everyone drooled over it.","Gao Mingkun couldn’t let that happen.","Hence, when no one was looking, he kicked the pot and spilled the soup.","“Argh! My rat meat!”","The Gao family was furious and tried to take the rat meat.","However, Gao Mingkun picked up the rat and ran as fast as he could. He then tossed the rat into a creek in the distance.","The Gao family was so hungry that they couldn’t run as fast as Gao Mingkun. It took them a while to catch up with him.","“Where’s my rat? Where is it?!”","They surrounded Gao Mingkun and were worried sick. Gao Mingkun pointed into the distance. “There.”","A dead rat was indeed lying in a creek a short distance away.","It was a dead rat with a tempting smell!","But the creek was deep in the valley, so they couldn’t go down.","“Argh!”","The third son, who was starving, smacked Gao Mingkun on the head.","“Why did you do that? I’m going to kill you!","“That’s our life-saving meat! How could you throw it away?! “Gao Mingkun, I hate you so much! Why can’t you be dead?","“You’re going to get us all killed!”","Everyone was blaming Gao Mingkun, including old Mrs. Gao, who was hitting him with the pot.","Gao Mingkun said stubbornly, “It’s a dead rat! You can’t eat it! It’ll kill you!”","‘Who told you that?”","Just then..."]},{"number":3773,"title":"Chapter 3773: Plague (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3773: Plague (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Just then, two people showed up at the foot of the mountain.","Both of them wore tattered clothes and looked as filthy as beggars.","They found the dead rat.","The two of them were over the moon and immediately picked it up.","They divided the meat into two halves and stuffed it into their mouths.","The Gao family was so jealous.","The eldest son glared at Gao Mingkun. “Look! Someone has eaten rat meat! Why can’t we eat it?!”","“That’s right. We’ve been starved for days. What’s wrong with eating some rat meat? Gao Mingkun, are you trying to starve us to death? Fine, we won’t eat rat meat, but you have to make us something to eat!”","Gao Mingkun blushed and wanted to retort, but he couldn’t. He only mumbled, “You can’t eat it. You just can’t.”","“Who told you that?”","“I heard Miss Feng talking about it with Brother Mingjiang,” said Gao Mingkun.","“It’s that Feng girl again!” The third daughter-in-law flared up at the mention of that name. “She’s such a troublemaker! If it hadn’t been for her, Li would never have been so stubborn! Mingjiang would never have fallen out with us because of his wife’s pillow talk! It’s all Feng’s fault!”","Gao Mingkun glanced at her. “Sister-in-law, you still haven’t realized your mistake, and you’re still blaming other people. I don’t think anyone will help you when you starve to death.”","His sister-in-law stared at him. “What did you say?!","Since Gao Mingkun had made it so clear, he couldn’t say anything else. He only smirked and said, “You can savor what I said!”","After that, Gao Mingkun sat down on the side and didn’t say another word.","The Gao family didn’t find any dead rats anymore because even those were in high demand. They couldn’t just find them everywhere.","They had to dig up wild grass and vegetables, as well as white clay, to keep themselves alive.","“Come, let’s go find Mingjiang. We’ll only survive if we find him.”","They struggled to their feet and stumbled forward, shouting “Mingjiang” all the way.","Occasionally, carriages or ox carts would pass them and keep moving forward.","Old Mrs. Gao burst into tears of jealousy. They used to have carriages as well, and Mingjiang had found them.","As for the rest of her sons...","Her sons had been too busy taking care of their own families to care about her. Old Mrs. Gao missed Gao Mingjiang even more.","She even saw that her sons all ate some wild fruit on their own without leaving anything for her. That wasn’t what Mingjiang was like back then...","She would have starved to death if it hadn’t been for Gao Mingkun’s help every now and then.","In the most difficult situation, they finally realized how good it was to have Gao Mingjiang around.","“If we find Mingjiang, I won’t pick on him again.”","“Actually, Feng is a nice girl. She’s very lucky and knows how to pick up things.” “Not only that, but she also knows how to hunt. She has hunted rabbits before.”","“It’s been a while since I ate meat. My stomach...”","“We don’t even have any chaff, let alone meat!”","Seeing that they had finally changed their attitudes, Gao Mingkun went up to old Mrs. Gao said casually, “Mum, I think I saw Brother Mingjiang.”","What?! The old lady was shocked.."]},{"number":3774,"title":"Chapter 3774: Meet Up (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3774: Meet Up (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","What?! The other members of the Gao family were thrilled to hear that.","“Where is he?” “Just tell us where he is!”","“Say it!”","They were already exhausted, but after hearing what Gao Mingkun said, they were all excited and almost jumped to their feet.","Everyone stared at Gao Mingkun with eager eyes.","Gao Mingkun cleared his throat. “If you can change your attitude, I’ll take you to my brother. If you still behave like before, even if you can find him...”","The third son immediately said, “I understand. If we’re still as greedy, hypocritical, and selfish as before, even if we find him, he’ll still abandon us!”","Gao Mingkun thought, “So, you know how greedy, hypocritical, and selfish you were.”","He looked at the others.","The exhaustion and starvation had worn them out. They would agree to everything.","The third daughter-in-law said, “I shouldn’t have said those things! I shouldn’t have bullied Mingjiang’s family! They had been helping us all along, but I... I’m sorry...”","The others apologized as well and asked Gao Mingkun to tell them where Gao Mingjiang was.","They had made up their minds. They would never let Gao Mingjiang leave when they found him again.","Gao Mingkun glanced at his mother, who was the most stubborn one. She had always wanted to share wealth with her family because they were all her sons. Since Gao Mingjiang was doing better than his brothers, she wanted to share some of his wealth with her other brothers.","Old Mrs. Gao glared at Gao Mingkun. “Why are you looking at me? Am I that kind of old lady who can’t tell right from wrong?”","Gao Mingkun thought, “You really are that kind of a person.”","The old lady knew by now that Gao Mingjiang was the only one she could count on, so she snorted. “After we find Mingjiang, I’ll let you live separately! I’ll stay with Mingjiang’s family! As for the others, it’s none of my business!” “Mum...” The other sons panicked.","Just then, the eldest daughter-in -law tugged at her husband’s sleeve and whispered, “Our top priority now is to find Mingjiang. We’ll talk about the rest later. ”","Her husband.","“Mom, you can do whatever you want after we find Mingjiang. You’ll call the shots.” The eldest son turned to Gao Mingkun. “Can you tell me where Mingjiang is now?”","Where was Gao Mingjiang","Led by Feng Wu, the fourth branch was living in a treehouse in the woods.","On her way here, Feng Wu noticed that someone had set up an inescapable trap to catch her. If she had set out on her own or revealed a little spiritual essence, they would have caught her by now.","Luckily, she was with the team and was still safe.","As for the Gao family... Feng Wu looked at Gao Mingjiang and knew that he wouldn’t stop caring about them,","Before he left with his family, he was more aggrieved than angry.","After everything he had put in, his mother was still biased, and his brothers were still picking on him... No one could stand that, but when he calmed down again, he was a little worried.","“What do you think will happen to them?”","Under the treehouse, Gao Mingjiang was making charcoal according to Feng Wu’s instructions, while Li was busy making bacon.."]},{"number":3775,"title":"Chapter 3775: Meet Up (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3775: Meet Up (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Li glanced at Gao Mingjiang and asked indifferently, “What do you think they’ll","Gao Mingjiang asked, “Mingkun is with them. I think they’ll be alright.”","Despite that, he still climbed up the tree again. It had been so long, but they still hadn’t arrived.","They only traveled for two days before taking camp here, and they had only covered about 50 km. It had been three to five days since he left the others. Where were they?","“Could something have gone wrong?” Gao Mingjiang frowned.","Li heaved a long sigh. “I knew it. You’re not heartless. You still care about them.”","Gao Mingjiang smiled bitterly. “After all, they’re my mother and brothers. Even if they’re unkind to me, I can’t just ignore them..","Li said, “That’s why we’ve been waiting here. We’re only two days’ ride from them. Without you, they’ll have a hard time. That way, they won’t be so unreasonable when we meet again.”","Gao Mingjiang said, “I thought the same. I’ve told Mingkun how to get here. He should have brought them here already.”","The two of them were perplexed, but Feng Wu knew the answer.","Little Phoenix had snuck out and told Feng Wu what happened in the Gao family.","Feng Wu was dumbfounded. The carriages were stolen, the luggage was taken, and there was no food. With a whole family of lazy people, it was so frustrating just to think about it.","However, the Gao family would never forget this lesson.","Feng Wu didn’t care if the Gao family traveled with them.","In terms of living comfortably, it would be best if the Gao family weren’t around.","However, to stay safe, the more people there were, the less likely Feng Wu would be spotted. Therefore, she didn’t mind having the Gao family with them.","Therefore, when Gao Mingjiang turned to Feng Wu for help, Feng Wu said indifferently, “Don’t worry. They’ll be here soon.”","After some thought, Feng Wu said, “Make some porridge. I don’t think they’ll have the stomach for pancakes.”","Gao Mingjiang and Li nodded.","Feng Wu’s capability in the past few days was enough to impress them and make them follow her orders.","In the past few days, Feng Wu had gone hunting, made charcoal, and found a place for the cabin. Her ability to survive in the wild was unmatched.","Feng Wu had hunted countless animals and even caught a boar! The whole family was over the moon.","Normal people wouldn’t dare to go into the woods. Even Gao Mingjiang wouldn’t survive. However, Feng Wu went in and came back with a pile of","games.","However, Feng Wu still reminded him to give all the credit to Gao Mingjiang, and she only wanted to be an inconspicuous nobody.","Li had cleaned up the wild boar and turned it into dried meat. She then put each piece in a sack so that they could take a bite when they were hungry. It was getting cold, so the meat could last for a long time.","Meanwhile, the Gao family was 5km away and was at a loss.","They were dumbfounded when they saw the dead bodies on the ground.","The dead bodies were obviously rotten and gave off a foul smell.","Just then, two people staggered out.","Their faces were scarlet red, and they couldn’t stop shaking."]},{"number":3776,"title":"Chapter 3776: Contagious (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3776: Contagious (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","The third daughter-in-law of the Gao family cried out, “Why do these two people look so familiar?”","Her husband said grumpily, “Of course they do! They’re the two people that took the rat meat!”","Everyone took a look and saw that it was true!","“What’s wrong with them?” the third daughter-in-law cried out. “Why do they look sick?”","“And they’re coming our way. What do they want?”","Wrapped in thin, worn cotton, the two men were stumbling toward the Gao family as if they were going to fall at any moment.","“Please give us something to eat... We...”","Seeing how pitiful they were, the eldest daughter-in-law felt sorry for them. She took a vegetable pancake out of her chest pocket and was about to hand it to them when Gao Mingkun cried out, “Don’t touch them!”","The eldest daughter-in-law glared at Gao Mingkun. “Mingkun, you’re so mean!","He’s...”","However, Gao Mingkun cut her off. “Fall back! Everyone, fall back! He’s been infected by the plague! Don’t let him touch you!”","The plague? How was that possible...","However, before they realized what was going on, the person who had been stumbling around suddenly found the strength to throw himself at them. He wrapped his arms around the eldest daughter-in-law’s thigh!","“Ah!” She screamed.","Gao Mingkun and the eldest son tried their best to help her.","But that person wouldn’t let go!","“Ouch!”","Not only did he hold her thigh, but he also bit down, and blood gushed out.","“Argh!”","The eldest daughter-in-law panicked. She could still hear Gao Mingkun’s voice in her head: plague, plague, plague...","She was so frightened that she fainted.","Gao Mingkun took out a rod and smashed it down on the head of the man holding the eldest daughter-in-law’s thigh. The man swayed and finally let go.","The eldest son quickly dragged his wife to the side.","Upon closer inspection, he saw that there was a row of tooth marks on her ankle, and blood was oozing out...","And it was black blood..","What kind of toxin was that?","Seeing that his friend had been killed, the other man spat at the Gao family.","“I’m going to infect you...”","Caught off guard, the women of the Gao family were spat all over their faces.","Gao Mingkun had been chasing the man, but because of his injury, it wasn’t easy to catch up with him.","Moreover, this person had some martial arts skills, which made it even harder for Gao Mingkun to hit him.","Gao Mingkun shouted at his brothers, “What are you waiting for? Standing around won’t stop him! Fight him if you want to protect your wives and children!”","The Gao brothers were indeed very timid and didn’t dare to go near the infected person. However, Gao Mingkun was right. If they didn’t join the battle, none of their wives or children would be safe.","Hence, all four sons joined hands and finally defeated the man.","However...","“My face...”","“My hand...’","“Does he really have the plague? What are we going to do?”","“Mom, is the plague really that bad?” The others asked old Mrs. Gao, the oldest of them all.","Old Mrs. Gao had been through a lot.","She had heard about the plague before.."]},{"number":3777,"title":"Chapter 3777: Contagious (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3777: Contagious (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Old Mrs. Gao’s face was ghastly pale. She didn’t want to believe it.","“That’s impossible! How can they have the plague? That’s impossible! That’s not true!” She shook her head.","“But, Mom...” Gao Mingkun wanted to say something, but the old lady cut him","off.","“No one is allowed to talk about it! And you!” She glared at Gao Mingkun. “Don’t tell Mingjiang anything after we find him!”","Gao Mingkun said, “Mom, if that’s the case, we won’t be able to find Brother Mingjiang.”","“You!” Old Mrs. Gao hit him with her stick.","But Gao Mingkun remained unperturbed. “Mother, if that’s the case, I won’t take you to him.”","The old lady knew that if Gao Mingkun didn’t show them the way, they would never be able to find Gao Mingjiang.","“Are you going to watch your brothers die?!” The old lady was so angry that she was almost in tears.","Gao Mingkun looked from the sorry state of the Gao family to the old lady without saying a word.","The old lady told Gao Mingkun to lead the way, but he shook his head and refused.","The old lady was furious.","The eldest son glared at Gao Mingkun. ‘We don’t have to go, but you need to talk to Mingjiang. If he agrees to take us in, I’ll listen to him for the rest of my life.”","The other two sons also looked solemnly at Gao Mingkun, indicating that they would do the same.","Gao Mingkun frowned. “It’s very likely that we’ve been infected. If we get in touch with Brother Mingjiang now, we may infect him and his family. So, I’m not going.”","Old Mrs. Gao had no choice but to compromise. “Go ask him on your own. If he wants to come, that’s all the better. If he doesn’t want to come, we’ll leave him to his fate!”","Gao Mingkun looked at the others. There was hope, sadness, and regret in their eyes.","Right now, they were probably all regretting parting with Gao Mingjiang’s family.","If they didn’t go through this, they would never repent.","At that thought, Gao Mingkun rose to its feet. “Alright. I’ll go find my brother. You guys wait for us in the valley. As for these two people, set them on fire before...”","It was very likely that they had contracted the plague.","The eldest son nodded. “Off you go. We’ll do it.” Gao Mingkun quickly left.","Old Mrs. Gao looked at her eldest son, dropping hints.","Boss Gao smiled bitterly. ‘Mum, it won’t make any difference even if we follow Mingkun. If Mingjiang really doesn’t want to come, what can we do?”","Old Mrs. Gao burst into tears and was filled with despair.","As a matter of fact, she knew better than anyone else that those two people had to have the plague. When she was little, there was a plague in the village once, and more than 70% of the population died...","“Why are we so unlucky...” Old Mrs. Gao burst into tears.","The third daughter-in-law said, “If we hadn’t chased them away, we wouldn’t have been reduced to this state.”","The second daughter-in-law said, “I’m sorry. I shouldn’t have tried to take advantage of them. I thought we were all family, so what if he lost a little? He was forced to leave.. It’s all my fault...”"]},{"number":3778,"title":"Chapter 3778: Found Him (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3778: Found Him (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Because Gao Mingkun already knew where his brother was, and they weren’t too far apart, he soon found the latter.","“Brother Mingjiang...’","Standing some distance away, Gao Mingkun looked up and shouted at a cabin.","The family had been building a cabin when he last saw Gao Mingkun. It was finished and was buried in the thick growth of leaves. Neither the sun nor the rain could touch it, and it was indeed very comfortable.","Feng Wu knew that Gao Mingkun was here when she heard his footsteps, but she didn’t move.","Right now, she was recuperating, for she knew that the journey to the Northern Yan Kingdom would only get more dangerous.","Hearing his brother’s voice, Gao Mingjiang jumped off the treehouse.","“Mingkun!” Gao Mingjiang sounded both excited and anxious.","After all, they were family, and Gao Mingjiang had no intention of abandoning them. He had done that because he wanted the old lady and the others to know how difficult it was to survive on their own so that they wouldn’t make trouble for him in the future.","It had been a few days, and he wondered how they were doing.","Gao Mingkun didn’t go any closer but stood some distance away.","Gao Mingjiang ran as fast as he could, but Gao Mingkun waved him off. “Brother, stay away from me!”","“Mingkun, what’s wrong? What happened?”","Gao Mingjiang panicked when he saw his younger brother, who was covered in wounds, had a bruised face, and was limping.","“Stay away from me! I may have caught the plague!”","Seeing that Gao Mingjiang was coming, Gao Mingkun stumbled back.","“The plague?!” Gao Mingjiang frowned and asked anxiously, “What’s going on?","Is the situation out there so bad already?”","Gao Mingkun didn’t waste any time. He quickly told his brother what happened.","Li and her children stood by Gao Mingjiang’s side and were dumbfounded.","“Someone has taken the carriages?","“And all the food?","“And the luggage too?","“How did that happen...”","Gao Mingjiang and Li looked at each other in bewilderment. When they heard that the others were fighting over the dead rat, Gao Mingjiang’s family was in tears.","“It was all my fault... I shouldn’t have... I shouldn’t have...”","Gao Mingjiang’s eyes were filled with tears.","Li took Gao Mingjiang’s arm. “No, it’s all my fault. I was narrow-minded. That’s why... I... I...”","Seeing that Gao Mingjiang and his wife were blaming themselves, Gao Mingkun said bitterly, “Brother, that’s what we’re facing now. What do you think we should do?”","Gao Mingjiang said, “I’ll go with you!”","Li said, “I’ll go with you too...”","But Gao Mingjiang shook his head and said affirmatively, “No, what if you and the kids catch the plague? I can’t let that happen!”","Li looked at Gao Mingjiang with teary eyes. “But if you’re killed, how am I supposed to live?”","Gao Mingjiang tried to appease her. ‘What if it’s not the plague? Don’t worry. Even if it is, I’m healthy enough to pull through. My mom has given you and the kids a hard time, and you’re too weak to survive it.”","He was going to follow Gao Mingkun after that.","Just then, Feng Wu sighed. “It’s a mess out there.. Why don’t we let them come here?”"]},{"number":3779,"title":"Chapter 3779: Found Him (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3779: Found Him (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","As for whether or not it was the plague, Feng Wu could tell right away.","Only then did Gao Mingjiang remember that he had a genius doctor with him.","Gao Mingjiang finally knew how capable the girl was.","But Gao Mingkun didn’t know that, so he frowned. “What if this place is infected...","Hearing Feng Wu’s words, Gao Mingjiang was relieved. ‘Great! We’ll bring them here!”","After that, Gao Mingjiang left with his brother.","Gao Mingkun was still worried. After walking for a while, he frowned and asked, “Brother, are we really going to take them back? What if...’","Gao Mingjiang waved him off. “Don’t worry. With what Feng said, you can rest assured!”","Gao Mingkun smiled bitterly. The plague could wipe out an entire city...","“The plague should have come from Maple Leaf City.” Gao Mingkun looked at","Gao Mingjiang in concern. “If Northern Yan knows about it, will they still let us","Gao Mingjiang was baffled for a moment before he realized the same thing.","If Northern Yan knew about this, the city gate would be closed, and no one would be allowed inside.","“Let’s go!”","At that thought, Gao Mingjiang quickened his pace. “Take my mother and the others to the treehouse. Treat them if they’re sick. If they’re not, we should be on our way! If we’re late, it’ll be like you said. We’ll be locked out of the city!”","The two brothers took the carriage, so they moved very fast.","It only took them 15 minutes to get there.","The Gao family almost lost their minds when they saw the carriage.","Old Mrs. Gao, who had been lying down, almost jumped to her feet. “It’s him! He’s here!”","The Gao family rushed forward in excitement, except for the eldest daughter-in-law, who couldn’t move.","Gao Mingjiang drove the carriage closer, jumped off, and walked up to the old lady. “Mother...”","Something seemed to occur to old Mrs. Gao, and she stumbled back. “Mingjiang, back off! Quickly! You’ll catch it!”","Gao Mingjiang was touched.","Before, his mother wouldn’t have stayed away from him but forced him to save her brothers.","“Mum, Xiao Wu has told me everything on the way. It’s an emergency. Let’s go back to the woods first.’","After that, Gao Mingjiang tried to help her into the carriage.","But the old lady still struggled. “Does your wife know you’re out here like this? Isn’t she mad at you? This is such a nice carriage.. What if you catch the plague?”","Only after losing the carriages then did she realize how precious a carriage was. She would rather die than lose it again.","Gao Mingjiang smiled bitterly. “A carriage isn’t as important as a human life. We don’t have enough space. If you’re too weak to walk, get in. If you can walk, just tag along. We’re running out of time.”","The second and third daughters-in-law looked at each other and both saw guilt in each other’s eyes.","“Mingjiang... ”","As soon as they started talking, Gao Mingjiang waved them off. “Guys, we’ll talk about it later.”","His sisters-in-law nodded.","Although they didn’t say anything, they were very touched.","If they were in Gao Mingjiang’s place, would they come back to save the others when they knew that they might be infected by the plague?","“Where’s my eldest sister-in-law?” Gao Mingjiang realized that someone was missing.."]},{"number":3780,"title":"Chapter 3780: Rescue","paragraphs":["Chapter 3780: Rescue","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","“Where’s my eldest sister-in-law?” Gao Mingjiang realized that someone was missing.","The eldest son immediately said, “She’s here. Your sister-in-law was trying to give someone some food, but that person bit her. She was worried that she might catch the plague, so she wrapped herself up like this.”","Seeing his sister-in-law bundled up in the carriage, Gao Mingjiang rubbed his forehead.","Feng Wu arrived at that moment and was rendered speechless by what she saw.","Feng Wu didn’t want to attract too much attention, so she checked the eldest daughter-in-law’s pulse when she was helping her to her feet.","Judging by her pulse, it really was the plague...","Feng Wu looked at the crowd.","She knew that if she stayed here with them, she could be stopped outside the city wall. However, she knew that she had to save these people.","Right at that moment...","There was a loud bang in the sky.","It was so loud that the mountains and rivers seemed to shake!","It was as if an earthquake had taken place.","“What happened? What happened?! ”","Members of the Gao family were shocked. They were bewildered and flustered.","They were so exhausted that they couldn’t take much more.","But now...","Large chunks of rock rolled down the slope.","They were on a gentle slope at the bottom of the hill and would be easily affected.","Boom!","There was another loud noise, which made them uneasy.","“Is there an earthquake? Have we run into one?”","After finally finding Gao Mingjiang, the old lady and the others were still eating porridge. Although they were unsteady on their feet, they still held their bowls so that they wouldn’t break them.","Gao Mingjiang jumped onto a tree and looked into the distance.","Meanwhile, Feng Wu was talking to Little Phoenix.","“Capable cultivators are fighting.” Little Phoenix was pleasantly surprised. “I think it’s Jun Linyuan.” Feng Wu was ecstatic!","Jun Linyuan?","Was he here?!","Standing on top of a tree, Feng Wu couldn’t see clearly because of the shaking ground. Even so, she could still see two black dots fighting in the distance.","At the top of the mountain!","That was right. It really was Jun Linyuan..","He really was here.","However...","Feng Wu recalled that a lot of people were after her. There were the Northern","Yan Kingdom. the Dongsang Kingdom. and the Tunwu Emnire...","Feng Wu had no idea why she was in such a miserable state, but it was reality.","“Who’s the one fighting Jun Linyuan?” Feng Wu asked.","Little Phoenix shook its head. “I don’t know, but it’s a quite capable person.”","Feng Wu couldn’t agree more. Jun Linyuan was already very capable, and even","General Xuezhi of the Dongsang Kingdom wasn’t his match. The fact that Jun Linyuan was able to fight him to a standstill showed how capable the other person was.","“Shit!” Little Phoenix cried out.","Even if Little Phoenix didn’t cry out, Feng Wu could still see it.","She saw a person flying toward Jun Linyuan’s battlefield and joined hands with the first one to fight Jun Linyuan.","Feng Wu said, “How can they do that?!”","Jun Linyuan was supposed to be on par with the first person, but with the addition of another capable cultivator, Jun Linyuan was in grave danger!","Feng Wu narrowed her eyes and clenched her fists.."]},{"number":3781,"title":"Chapter 3781: Jun Linyuan","paragraphs":["Chapter 3781: Jun Linyuan","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Feng Wu narrowed her eyes and clenched her fists.","Just then, Gao Mingjiang raised his voice.","Feng Wu knew what he said. He told her to come back as soon as possible.","But Feng Wu didn’t want to.","was right here, and he had to be here for her. How could she walk away from him?","Right now, Feng Wu regretted the fact that she barely had any cultivation ability left.","Even so...","Feng Wu still ran toward the top of the mountain.","Her action frightened the others.","Gao Mingjiang stared at Feng Wu in disbelief. She was gone?","Not only wouldn’t she back off, but she was also charging forward!","“Little Feng! Come back here!”","Exasperated, Gao Mingjiang tried to drag Feng Wu back, but Feng Wu was too fast. She ran through the woods like a cheetah and was soon out of sight among the thick leaves.","Only then did Li realize what had happened. She rushed over and asked,","“Where’s Feng?”","After interacting with Feng Wu for the past few days, Li genuinely considered","Feng Wu to be her niece. She was worried sick when Feng Wu went missing.","Gao Mingjiang frowned. “She’s gone in.”","Li was so anxious that she burst into tears. “Why? Why?”","“Ah! Where’s Xiaoshu?”","Li said anxiously, “Xiaoshu is missing! When did he run off? Sanya, where’s your brother?! ”","Sanya sounded like she was going to cry, “He said he was going to fetch some firewood when we heard my grandmother and the others were coming. There was no firewood, so I told him to wait for me. I would go with him after I relieved myself, but he was gone in a moment...”","Li said, “Little Feng must have found out that Xiaoshu was missing and went to look for her. My heart...”","The thought of her two children in danger almost gave her a heart attack. She wanted to run into the woods as fast as she could.","“You can’t go!” Gao Mingjiang stopped Li and gave the job to Gao Mingkun.","“Stop your sister-in-law!”","After that, Gao Mingjiang was going to rush into the woods to save the two kids.","Seeing this, the other three brothers of the Gao family realized that they couldn’t let Gao Mingjiang leave. They dropped what they were eating and rushed over to stop him.","“Mingjiang, don’t! Calm down!”","“Calm down? He’s my son!” Gao Mingjiang threw off his three brothers’ hands.","The next moment, Gao Mingjiang charged into the woods like an angry bear.","“Take care of my sister-in-law and the girl! I’ll go find my brother!” Gao Mingkun dashed off as well.","Soon, Gao Mingkun was gone as well.","The three brothers looked at one another in bewilderment.","Why did it happen so suddenly...","The old lady was much calmer.","She had a bowl of porridge and a piece of sweet potato. She had recovered a little and could speak again.","“Cut the crap. Let’s get out of here and find a safer spot. Otherwise, we’re going to die here...”","Meanwhile, Feng Wu ran in the direction of the battle after she ran into the woods.","Little Phoenix’s voice kept ringing in her ears.","“You’re out of your mind! Don’t you know how weak you are now?","“Don’t you know what level they are?","“Compared to them, you’re as weak as an ant!","“How are you going to help anyone? You’re going to get yourself killed!”","But nothing Little Phoenix said could stop Feng Wu.","“He’s here for me, and you want me to abandon him?” The more anxious Feng Wu was, the calmer her voice became.."]},{"number":3782,"title":"Chapter 3782: Battle on the Mountaintop","paragraphs":["Chapter 3782: Battle on the Mountaintop","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","It was a fierce battle!","Right now, Feng Wu couldn’t get closer.","Gravel kept rolling down the slope, and Feng Wu couldn’t even stand still, let alone go up.","“Fly me there,” Feng Wu told Little Phoenix.","Little Phoenix frowned and looked troubled. “Your current cultivation level...","They were still talking when they heard a smirk.","“Patriarch Zuo?” Jun Linyuan’s voice rang out.","The Zuo family? The Patriarch?","Feng Wu remembered that the old master of the Zuo family had been killed by Jun Linyuan when he was in the imperial capital. So, was this one the legendary patriarch?","The old man removed the cloth covering his face and revealed his face.","“That’s right.” The old man stared at Jun Linyuan with an indecipherable look in his eyes.","“You’re not dead?” Jun Linyuan frowned and looked confused.","The old man smirked. “How can I die when the Junwu Empire has a talented young man like you?”","It was a creepy smile.","“That old monster isn’t dead, is he?” Patriarch Zuo smiled at the other man.","It was a swordsman.","He wore a bamboo hat, straw shoes, and a vine sword basket on his waist. Despite his simple appearance, he was very powerful.","The middle-aged swordsman was the one who had fought Jun Linyuan to a draw.","Patriarch Zuo glanced at him. “Gui Qulai, after all these years, you’re still dressed like this.”","Gui Qulai glanced at the patriarch with an emotionless face. He pointed his sword at Jun Linyuan. “Make your move.”","Jun Linyuan shook his head. “You’re not as good as me.”","Gui Qulai was furious, but he still pointed his sword at Jun Linyuan. “Strike!”","He had drawn out his sword, but he hadn’t forced Jun Linyuan to draw out his.","Patriarch Zuo was on the side, ready to join the battle at any moment.","Gui Qulai glanced at the old man. “Go away.”","Patriarch Zuo wouldn’t have it. “Why? I’ll just stand here and watch. I won’t interfere.”","After that, he crossed his arms and leaned back on the wall.","But they both knew that the patriarch was only taking advantage of the situation.","Gui Qulai glanced at Patriarch Zuo and asked Jun Linyuan, “Shall we have the competition in a month at Norland?”","Norland was the capital of Northern Yan.","Jun Linyuan nodded indifferently. “Sure.”","Gui Qulai frowned, glanced at the old man, and left.","He came and went without a trace.","Once Gui Qulai was gone, Patriarch Zuo looked displeased. It was obvious that Gui Qulai didn’t want to see him here, so he had left. He had even made an appointment to fight Jun Linyuan at the top of Norland.","Jun Linyuan glanced at the old man. “Are you going to fight me?”","Jun Linyuan wouldn’t be intimidated if the two of them joined hands, not to mention that there was only one of them left.","The old man smirked. “Let’s fight!”","Feng Wu heard those last words when Little Phoenix carried her up the mountain.","The battle at the top of Norland?","And...","Jun Linyuan and Patriarch Zuo were flying away.","Feng Wu said, “They’re gone? Just like that?”","The ground was covered with broken rocks, withered green plants, and they were disappearing into the distance.","Feng Wu didn’t know what to say... Jun Linyuan was right in front of her, and he was gone before she could say a word to him.","She wondered how the battle would turn out.."]},{"number":3783,"title":"Chapter 3783: Gui Qulai","paragraphs":["Chapter 3783: Gui Qulai","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Feng Wu looked eagerly at Little Phoenix.","But now, the bird shook its head. “No!”","It knew what Feng Wu meant. She wanted to go to Jun Linyuan, but that couldn’t happen.","Little Phoenix tried to persuade Feng Wu. “All of Jun Linyuan’s enemies are Spiritual Saints, and they can easily crush you. Apart from becoming his burden, there’s nothing else you can do.","“You heard it yourself. The battle of the top of Norland is going to take place a month from now. Jun Linyuan is going to fight Gui Qulai.","“Do you know who Gui Qulai is? He’s Master Juesha, one of the four kings of Northern Yan. He’s known for his sword, Strike One.","“Do you know why his sword is called that name? Because he never makes a second strike.","“There’s also the Zuo family’s patriarch and other people hiding in the dark. Even if we can catch up with Jun Linyuan and find him, do you know how much pressure you’ll put on Jun Linyuan just by showing up?","“You have the Divine Phoenix Blood, and Jun Linyuan has the Dragon Phoenix Blood. If the two of you really become a couple, what will it mean? Other forces won’t stand by and do nothing!","“Xiao wu...”","“And you have to go to Norland because you’ll find something you really need there!” Little Phoenix finally told the truth.","Feng Wu frowned. “Is that what Master Linghu was talking about?”","Little Phoenix nodded. “Your master left it for you. You have to have it!” Feng Wu nodded.","She finally knew why Little Phoenix had led her to the Northern Yan Empire.","“So, although you didn’t say it explicitly, you’ve been leading me to Norland, haven’t you?” Feng Wu glanced at the bird.","“Ahem.” Little Phoenix pretended that it didn’t understand and looked away.","Feng Wu said grumpily, “I knew it. You’ve recovered a lot of your memories from your previous life, but you wouldn’t tell me.”","Little Phoenix sounded anxious. “It’s not that I don’t want to tell you, but I can’t.”","Feng Wu asked, “Why not?”","Little Phoenix stomped its foot. “Well, I just can’t tell you...’","Seeing that Little Phoenix was worried sick, Feng Wu let it go.","So, it really couldn’t tell Feng Wu, could it? Would it harm its own life if it did? Feng Wu gave Little Phoenix an excuse.","“I won’t ask you, but you have to tell me everything in advance,” Feng Wu warned the bird.","Little Phoenix nodded immediately.","Feng Wu mumbled, “You’re right. If I show up in front of Jun Linyuan now, I’ll attract a lot of powerful enemies, and most of the capable cultivators of the Junwu Empire are fighting the Dongsang Kingdom. They won’t have time to help us.","“Isn’t the competition in a month? Let’s go to see Jun Linyuan then.”","Moreover, she didn’t know if Gui Qulai would try anything funny, so Feng Wu decided to check up on him in advance.","At that thought, Feng Wu was filled with enthusiasm. She told Little Phoenix,","“Come. Let’s go to the Gao family.”","Little Phoenix looked at Feng Wu in bewilderment. “Aren’t you going alone?”","She looked up at the sky and saw that people were monitoring the ground every now and then.","She could sense a pair of eyes staring at this area.","It was as if they could see everything!"]},{"number":3784,"title":"Chapter 3784: Let’s Go Back (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3784: Let’s Go Back (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","“Let’s go.” Feng Wu patted Little Phoenix.","Only then did Little Phoenix let out a breath of relief. If Feng Wu insisted on going to Jun Linyuan, there was nothing it could do.","“Little Feng.”","Feng Wu and Little Phoenix quickly went down the mountain to find a boy crying on the ground. His face was covered with dirt, and Feng Wu almost couldn’t recognize him. It was none other than Gao Xiaoshu, the son of Gao Mingjiang.","“Xiaoshu, what are you doing here?” Feng Wu went up to him in a hurry, crouched down, and rubbed his head.","It was obvious that the kid was frightened by what had happened. A stone had smashed into his head, creating a bloody gash. Feng Wu wanted to pick him up but realized that one of his legs was pinned down by a stone.","Feng Wu pushed the stone away and examined his right leg.","His right leg was badly injured, but luckily, she had discovered him in time. Otherwise, Feng Wu was worried that he would lose his leg.","“Sister...” The boy looked excited. He buried his head in Feng Wu’s arms and cried even harder.","Feng Wu picked him up and asked, “Why are you here all by yourself? Where are your parents?”","Gao Xiaoshu was too busy crying and hiccupping to speak.","Before Feng Wu could ask another question, she saw two people a short distance away.","One was Gao Mingjiang, and the other was Gao Mingkun.","With weapons in their hands and serious looks on their faces, they looked as if they weren’t afraid of death at all. Rocks kept falling down as they wandered in the woods, and it was very dangerous.","“Uncle Gao?”","Feng Wu greeted him.","Gao Mingjiang had lost all hope.","Gao Xiaoshu had been lost in the woods, and Feng had rushed in to save him. No one knew if they were still alive. Judging by how dangerous the woods were, they probably weren’t going to make it...","Gao Mingjiang was getting more and more desperate when he heard a pleasant voice.","He froze on the spot and didn’t dare to move, fearing that he was hallucinating. Gao Mingkun nudged him in excitement. “Brother Mingkun, it’s them! Look!”","Only then did Gao Mingjiang turn around, look at Feng Wu, and see the boy in her arms.","“Xiaoshu!”","Gao Mingjiang was so excited that he almost passed out. He charged at Feng Wu like a shooting arrow.","“You, you...”","Seeing that Gao Mingjiang was so excited that his lips were trembling, Feng Wu knew that he was losing control. She stuffed Gao Xiaoshu into his arms.","“Xiaoshu’s foot was caught by a rock, and he needs immediate treatment. It’s too dangerous here. Let’s get out first.”","“Sure, sure...","Gao Mingjiang nodded at Feng Wu in excitement. “Little Feng, I can’t thank you enough. If you need my help in the future, I’ll do anything!”","Feng Wu nodded. “Let’s go out first.”","On her way out, Feng Wu grabbed a few herbs.","When they arrived at the campsite, they saw that they were confronting a group of people.","The bandits that had taken their carriages were standing right in front of them. The leader of the bandits was Ding, and he was heading for Northern Yan with over a dozen men.","They had been traveling from the south to the north to run away from the plague. Captain Ding and the others knew that they would only survive if they went to Northern Yan.","They had used up a lot of things on their way here, but now..."]},{"number":3785,"title":"Chapter 3785: Let’s Go Back (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3785: Let’s Go Back (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Just when they were running out of provisions, they saw someone they knew.","The Gao family...","They had a carriage with them.","Not only was there a carriage but there was also a lot of food!","There was even meat!","Ding and the others were thrilled.","“You! Move everything into our carriage!” MO Ping, Ding’s most trusted subordinate, stepped out before Ding could say anything.","The Gao family was furious.","Gao Mingjiang Imew some martial arts, but he wasn’t here...","The remaining three sons were as weak as before.","Seeing how scared the eldest son was, MO Ping smirked. “What? Are you going to fight back now? Come and take these carriages. They used to belong to your family, don’t they?”","Those around him laughed after MO Ping said that.","The Gao brothers felt like they had been slapped.","Infuriated, old Mrs. Gao couldn’t take it anymore. She picked up the wok and slapped MO Ping with it.","With a thump, the old lady hit MO Ping in the face.","“You old hag! How dare you?!” MO Ping kicked the old lady away.","“Mom!”","“Mom!”","Seeing that the old lady had closed her eyes, the others were worried sick.","Just then, MO Ping and the others started taking the food.","With Feng Wu’s help, Gao Mingjiang’s family accumulated quite a lot of food.","“Not only are there steamed buns, but there’s also dried meat. Guys, you’re going to be in for a treat.” Ding gave MO Ping an appreciative look.","Because of MO Ping’s sharp eyes, he immediately spotted the food hidden behind the rocks.","MO Ping’s eyesight was unbelievable. Not only did he see food, but he also saw Li.","Li’s clothes were shabby as well, but she was pretty enough to catch MO Ping’s eye right away.","MO Ping glanced at Ding.","Ding rubbed his chin.","MO Ping lowered his voice. “Boss, she’s a nice-looking woman. She’s like a ripe peach, and she’s so eye-catching. You can take her to bed at night and let her cook during the day...”","Ding nodded, liking the idea.","MO Ping stared at Li with his shifty eyes, and Li was terrified.","The three brothers of the Gao family realized what was going on as well, and they pulled Li behind them.","MO Ping smirked. “Do you think you can protect her?”","He then turned to Li. “If you come with us, we won’t kill them. If you resist, we’ll kill them all!”","Li was filled with despair.","The other members of the Gao family lost all hope as well.","If Li was taken away, Gao Mingjiang would go berserk when he came back.","Hence, the eldest son glared at MO Ping and gritted his teeth. “You can take the food and the carriage, but not her!”","MO Ping smirked. “I’m not making a suggestion. We want food, carriages, and her. ”","After that, he tried to drag Li away.","The Gao brothers wouldn’t let Li go.","However, MO Ping wasn’t alone. He had over a dozen capable brothers with him. Right now, they had all gathered around the three brothers. “Gosh, I didn’t know you could be so tough. You were so soft before..”"]},{"number":3786,"title":"Chapter 3786: Suppression (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3786: Suppression (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","The three brothers weren’t their match.","They were bandits, and there were over a dozen of them. If the Gao brothers could defeat them, they wouldn’t have lost the two carriages.","Before long, the Gao brothers were lying on the ground with bruised faces.","“Didn’t I tell you to hand it over as soon as possible? Otherwise, you won’t be able to handle the consequences. Why did you have to go through such pain?”","MO Ping glanced at the group of people in front of him with a taunting look on his face. He then grabbed Li with an evil smile. “Come with us!”","At that critical moment, Li suddenly slashed down at her throat with a dagger!","Gao Mingjiang had given the dagger to her for self-defense. She knew that she would wish she were dead if she went with these people, so she might as well die now.","She moved so fast that MO Ping didn’t have time to react. Before he realized it, the dagger had cut Li’s neck.","“How dare you?!”","MO Ping grabbed Li’s arm and broke it.","Because Li had no experience when she tried to take her own life, she missed the artery when she cut her neck. At that critical moment!","Whoosh!","An arrow flew out.","It pierced MO Ping’s heart.","Everyone was astonished and turned to look behind Li.","Feng Wu had a bow in her hand and a cold look in her eyes.","It was obvious that she was the one who had shot MO Ping.","“You!” Ding was so shocked that he couldn’t utter a word.","By then, Feng Wu had drawn her bow again.","This time, her target was Ding.","Feng Wu knew that if she could kill Ding, the team would collapse.","Someone in the sky glanced in their direction.","Because it was a battle between ordinary people with no spiritual essence, the eyes didn’t pay much attention to it.","Little Phoenix was relieved and told Feng Wu, “He’s gone.”","Feng Wu nodded slightly.","It seemed that she had made the right choice by blending into the crowd. Otherwise, she would have been spotted very easily.","Whoosh !","The arrow flew through the air and aimed at Ding’s face.","Ding tried to dodge, but for some unknown reason, he couldn’t move a muscle.","Whoosh!","The arrow was buried in Ding’s heart.","Oh god...","Everyone was dumbfounded.","Old Mrs. Gao stared at Feng Wu in astonishment. All she knew was that the little beggar was lucky, but she didn’t know that she could shoot so well. The other members of the Gao family were astonished as well.","“Let’s go!”","Gao Mingjiang took out an ax from behind his back and struck down all the enemies.","Gao Mingjiang had practiced martial arts before. When he saw that the Gao family was almost destroyed and that his wife had been humiliated, he was furious. He charged at the bandits with an ax in his hand.","Naturally, the bandits wouldn’t wait for Gao Mingjiang to kill them. They tried to fight back.","But Feng Wu was there to help.","Whoosh!","Arrows just kept coming!","Seeing that Feng Wu didn’t have enough arrows, old Mrs. Gao rushed over and began to pull the arrows out of Ding’s body. Blood gushed out.."]},{"number":3787,"title":"Chapter 3787: Suppression (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3787: Suppression (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","On any other day, old Mrs. Gao would have been scared out of her wits. However, she couldn’t care less now.","Seeing this, the wives of the second and third sons rushed over to pull out the arrows as well.","Feng Wu was so accurate that she could kill an enemy with each arrow she shot. Right now, she was running out of arrows.","As expected, when Feng Wu reached into the quiver on her back again, she found nothing.","“Over here!”","Holding the three arrows, old Mrs. Gao stumbled toward her.","Poor old Mrs. Gao. She was still dizzy from MO Ping’s kick. She handed the arrows to Feng Wu and asked, “Will they work?”","Seeing that the old Mrs. Gao was stumbling around, Feng Wu nodded solemnly.","“Yes.”","“Good, good...” Old Mrs. Gao’s voice was trembling.","It was both from the pain and how nervous she felt.","By then, Feng Wu had picked up the bloody arrows and went on shooting.","Ding’s men weren’t stupid. They panicked when they saw that over a dozen of their men had been killed.","“It’s you!”","Wang Yu stared at Feng Wu.","Seven of the ten dead bandits had been shot in the chest, three had been killed by Gao Mingjiang, and seven were still alive.","“Three of you, hold this man down. The rest, come with me and kill her!”","Wang Yu pointed at Feng Wu. “We can still win if we kill that archer. Otherwise, she’ll kill us all!”","The others saw it as well and all nodded.","The next moment, they all charged at Feng Wu.","Gao Mingkun rushed over, tripped Wang Yu, and beat him up on the ground.","The other three couldn’t care less about Wang Yu and kept running.","Feng Wu kept shooting as she fell back.","Another person fell to the ground.","However, the two men were only ten meters away from her.","Their faces twisted.","Once that person was dead, the rest of the team would be defenseless. Hence, she had to die!","Little Phoenix, who was in Feng Wu’s arms, said in resignation, “Tell me about it. What kind of battle is this? They’re all rolling around on the ground and beating each other up. A battle between ordinary people is so boring...”","Not only couldn’t Feng Wu use her spiritual essence, but the bird also couldn’t use it either...","As soon as Little Phoenix flapped its wings, these people would be blown away. Feng Wu lowered her voice. “Don’t do anything.”","Little Phoenix mumbled, “I know. There’s a pair of eyes watching this land. I won’t do anything... Well, look, they just think you’re too weak to fight in close combat and want to kill you.”","As a matter of fact, although Feng Wu had lost her spiritual essence, she was still physically strong enough to defeat an ordinary man with a single punch.","By then, the two of them had reached Feng Wu.","“Kill her!”","Both men grinned maliciously.","Just then, two people rushed over and held the two criminals in their arms. They were none other than the second and third sons of the Gao family.","“Feng, do something!”","The third son bellowed.","Infuriated, the bandit tried to stab the third son in the back.","Feng Wu frowned a little. She grabbed the bandit’s saber and slit his throat.","The bandit couldn’t believe his eyes when he hit the ground.."]},{"number":3788,"title":"Chapter 3788: Treatment (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3788: Treatment (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","All the bandits were taken care of.","Seeing this, old Mrs. Gao let out a breath of relief and almost fainted.","All the members of the Gao family were injured or sick, and they looked miserable.","The three eldest sons were all injured.","The eldest daughter-in -law’s condition was unclear.","Gao Mingjiang was fine, but Li was still bleeding from the cut on her neck.","Gao Mingkun was covered with wounds, and so was old Mrs. Gao.","The group of people consisted of the elderly and the sick...","Feng Wu rubbed her forehead.","“Little Feng...” Gao Mingjiang gave Feng Wu a pleading look.","Feng Wu looked over her shoulder and saw that the battle was over, and the rocks had stopped falling. She told Gao Mingjiang, “The slope is sheltered from the wind. Let’s go there and treat your wounds. I’m going into the woods.”","Gao Mingjiang nodded immediately.","Luckily, the bandits had left carriages behind, so Gao Mingjiang could take them there.","As for where they were, it was too open for them to stay.","“That Feng girl is amazing.”","After Feng Wu left, the Gao family began to discuss among themselves. The third daughter-in-law said in disbelief, “Did you see her using the bow? She’s amazing! She killed a person with each arrow!”","The second daughter-in-law was still in shock.","She had offended Feng Wu before. If the girl went berserk, no one in the Gao family would be her match.","“But what’s she doing in the woods all by herself? Why hasn’t she come back?","Has she run away because of how burdened we are?”","The second daughter-in-law shook her head at the third daughter-in-law. “That’s not what she’s like.”","The third daughter-in-law said, “Why not? I...”","The second daughter-in-law said, “If that’s the case, she wouldn’t have helped us. She would have left. With her capability, she can go anywhere she wants. Speaking of which, we’ve benefited a lot from her.”","The third daughter-in-law wanted to retort, but when she recalled the way the girl shot the arrows, she realized that Feng Wu was indeed a good hunter. “But we’re all injured... What are we going to do...”","Even the men of the Gao family wanted to cry, let alone the women.","Gao Mingjiang said, “We’ll cook first, then treat the minor injuries. As for the more severe ones, we’ll have to wait until Feng gets back.”","The other four sons all had superficial wounds, and Gao Mingjiang had brought some ointment with him, and it came in handy this time.","Old Mrs. Gao was sitting there with her hands on her stomach and crying out in pain. Sweat covered her forehead. “Mom, how do you feel?”","The old lady waved her off.","She now saw that out of all her sons, only the fourth was useful. She drew in her breath in pain and told Gao Mingjiang, “We’ll set out as soon as Feng comes back.”","Gao Mingjiang said, “But...’","“I can’t say for sure, but a lot of people behind us have caught the plague and are heading for Northern Yan now. We have to leave before the city is sealed","off...","Only then did Gao Mingjiang remember that. “My eldest sister-in-law is...” Old","Mrs. Gao looked at Zhao for a while before shaking her head. “I don’t know... We’ll have to let her stay behind.”","Gao Mingjiang said, ‘Mom!”","Old Mrs. Gao said coldly, “Of course, we have to take care of healthy people first.. If I’m the one infected, I’m going to stay behind as well! Those who are in good health, go to Northern Yan now!”"]},{"number":3789,"title":"Chapter 3789: Treatment (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3789: Treatment (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","At that point, she coughed violently. “Mother, you...” Gao Mingjiang cried out.","Old Mrs. Gao blanched. Was she really infected? If that was the case...","Instantly, everyone in the Gao family froze on the spot with grim looks on their faces.","Feng Wu came back at that moment.","She came back with a broken pot she had found somewhere, and it was steaming.","“Little Feng, you’re finally back!”","Gao Mingjiang let out a breath of relief when he saw Feng Wu. “What’s this?”","Feng Wu said, “I picked some herbs. Since I had nothing better to do, I took some medicine.”","After that, Feng Wu poured the gravy into some boiled water, stirred it a little, and told Gao Mingjiang, “Give everyone a bowl each.”","“This medicine...","Feng Wu looked at him in bewilderment. “Didn’t I tell you before? It specializes in treating the rat plague. It can treat the sick and prevent infection if there’s nothing wrong.”","Gao Mingjiang was worried about the plague, but Feng Wu told him that it was solved.","But the other members of the Gao family didn’t believe her.","The plague was going to kill them, and there was no such thing as a special potion. They would never believe what Feng Wu said.","Feng Wu knew that this wasn’t the time to reason with them, so she frowned at Gao Mingjiang.","Gao Mingjiang and his family knew how capable Feng Wu was, so they nodded and distributed the medicine.","As a matter of fact, Feng Wu didn’t gather the ingredients just now. They couldn’t be found here. It was a potion that Feng Wu made beforehand, and she was only mixing them in the hot water now.","As for whether or not it could treat the plague... Of course, it could.","At Feng Wu’s level, the plague was nothing.","After everyone drank a big bowl of medicine, Feng Wu suggested that they should set out.","Gao Mingjiang agreed.","The sooner they reached Yu City, the better.","Old Mrs. Gao was already having a fever, so she went to talk to Feng Wu.","“Leave me and my eldest daughter-in-law behind.”","Feng Wu looked at her in bewilderment.","Old Mrs. Gao rolled her eyes at Feng Wu. “I know. You’re the only one who can make decisions. That’s why I’m here! Leave me and my daughter-in-law behind!”","Feng Wu asked, ‘Why?”","Old Mrs. Gao said, “We’re both running a fever. It’s obviously a symptom of the plague. We’re going to die, but you’re still alright. We can’t spread it to you or the people of Northern Yan.”","Feng Wu gave her a strange look. Since when was the old lady so selfless?","Old Mrs. Gao snorted. “They’re all my children, so of course I care about them.","I’ve had enough. Just let them live. You guys can leave now.”","Feng Wu chuckled. “So, you know that you can’t spread the plague to Northern","Yan.”","Old Mrs. Gao snorted. “All I know is that if we spread the plague to Northern Yan, even if we can get in, we’ll be decapitated later. So, I’m going to wait here to die!”","Feng Wu waved her off. “Don’t worry. It’ll be alright.”","After that, she grabbed the old lady and dragged her into the carriage.","Old Mrs. Gao was exasperated. “Are you an idiot? Why did you do that?!”","Feng Wu chuckled. “I told you already. You’ll be alright after drinking my medicine.. “"]},{"number":3790,"title":"Chapter 3790: They’re Here (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3790: They’re Here (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","As expected, after drinking the potion Feng Wu gave her, the eldest daughter-in-law, who had been running a high fever, gradually recovered. Feng Wu chuckled. “I told you already. My medicine is amazing.”","Unfortunately, no one believed her.","How could there be such an amazing potion that could cure the plague? If there really was one, the empire wouldn’t have to worry about the plague so much.","Everyone thought that Feng Wu was only joking, except for Gao Mingjiang, who looked at Feng Wu in amazement.","He felt that his sister-in-law’s symptoms were very similar to the plague... So, Feng’s medicine worked, didn’t it?","Little Phoenix was complaining in Feng Wu’s head.","“You’re so... They won’t believe you after hearing what she said. No one will believe that you can treat the plague, nor will they thank you for it.” Feng Wu chuckled. “I don’t need them to give me any credit.”","Little Phoenix said, “Then you...”","Feng Wu went on laughing. “I didn’t want them to know that I was the one who had saved them. That way, I would be able to blend into the crowd and join the team. Otherwise, I would be too outstanding.”","Little Phoenix agreed with her.","Little Phoenix said, “There are more patients coming. Are you going to save them or not?”","Feng Wu shrugged. “We’re in the middle of nowhere, and there’s nothing we can do. Even if we have a prescription, we won’t know where to start. We’ll have to wait until we’re in Northern Yan. I’ll then give them the prescription.” As they spoke, they were getting closer and closer to Northern Yan.","Gao Mingjiang came to tell Feng Wu, “We’ll reach the border city in two days.” Feng Wu nodded.","They had been traveling as fast as they could. Occasionally, they would run into someone who had caught a fever, but it was getting rarer and rarer. Gao Mingjiang was elated when he saw they no longer run into people with symptoms.","As long as they got there before those people did, they should still be able to get into the border city.","“Shall we travel through the night or...” Gao Mingjiang asked for Feng Wu’s opinion.","Feng Wu looked over her shoulder and saw that they had been traveling for three to four days and were exhausted. She waved at them. “Let’s take a break for four hours. We still have some time.”","Gao Mingjiang thought the same, so he nodded and went to make the arrangement.","The Gao family used to be very disobedient and would do whatever they wanted, but after Gao Mingjiang demonstrated what would happen when he was away, they realized that they couldn’t survive without him.","As a result, they didn’t bully his family anymore, nor did they exploit Gao Mingjiang because he was their brother. They were all very obedient.","Therefore, Gao Mingjiang handled things much more easily.","Gao Mingjlang round a spot to let tnem settle down.","It just so happened that there were a lot of rocks here, so they chose a leeward spot, where they could easily start a fire.","Everyone had been eating dry food and drinking cold water for the past few days, and they had been feeling dizzy the whole time. As soon as they got off the carriages, old Mrs. Gao’s legs gave out, and she almost fell.","Feng Wu was the first to react. She picked her up and steadied the old lady.","Feng Wu looked around. They were in a forest, which was very close to Northern Yan. It wasn’t dry like the one in the south.","Feng Wu took out her bow and arrow and said to Gao Mingjiang, “I’m going to take a look in the woods.”","“Be careful,” said Gao Mingjiang.."]},{"number":3791,"title":"Chapter 3791: They’re Here (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3791: They’re Here (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","They weren’t worried about Feng Wu, for she had demonstrated how good a hunter she was.","To Feng Wu, hunting wasn’t a problem at all. She could even hunt large beasts. With Little Phoenix around, she wouldn’t have any problem at all. However, she only managed to kill two rabbits in the end.","She couldn’t let her spiritual essence fluctuate or make a scene.","Luckily, Northern Yan was already very close. Once they were in Northern Yan, she would be like a fish swimming in the sea. It would be very difficult for them to catch up with her.","At that thought, Feng Wu smiled a little.","Once they were out of the woods, Feng Wu saw that the others had started a fire, and the water was bubbling.","She handed one rabbit to Li and the other to Gao Mingjiang.","While Li stewed the fat rabbit with vegetables, Gao Mingjiang roasted the rabbit.","Little Phoenix was anxious for Feng Wu. “We’re almost there. I’m sure there will be an inspection...”","Feng Wu said, “I’ve been hanging out with the Gao family for so long, and I’ve been waiting for this inspection. Don’t worry. I have a plan.”","Little Phoenix mumbled, “We’ve been trying to keep a low profile this whole time, and I’m so bored... This place is so uncivilized. I can’t believe that I’ve lived like this for so long...”","Feng Wu chuckled. ‘When you were with my beautiful master, you were so high up in the air that you didn’t know what the real world was like. This is a great opportunity for you to experience the real world. Maybe you’ll learn something...’","Feng Wu then saw the look on Little Phoenix’s face change. “What?” Feng Wu looked at Little Phoenix in bewilderment. Little Phoenix was giving Feng Wu a strange look.","Feng Wu asked, “What’s wrong?” Little Phoenix said, “You’re right.”","Feng Wu said, “Are you going to...”","Little Phoenix nodded. “That’s right. I didn’t think much of this trip at first and even felt aggrieved, but with your guidance just then, I think I’ve really learned something incredible. No, I have to do it now. Protect yourself!”","After that, Little Phoenix entered the ring space through Feng Wu’s sleeve and went into seclusion.","It had a feeling that it was going to have an epiphany... It would be very impressive when it came out!","Feng Wu was astonished as well. Little Phoenix had an epiphany just like that and was going to make a breakthrough!","Feng Wu cleared her throat.","That was good news, wasn’t it?","However, Feng Wu was glad to hear that. After all, Little Phoenix was as capable as she was. If Little Phoenix had learned something, so did she, and it would only make her more enlightened.","Feng Wu recalled what Master Linghu said earlier.","Travel the world and comprehend it. What was it that he wanted her to comprehend?","What would she get after she found Master Huyan?","Somehow, Feng Wu was looking forward to this trip.","Just then, they heard the sound of hooves.","Although Feng Wu had lost her cultivation ability, she still had a sharp hearing.","She could hear the sound of hooves.","There was more than one horse. There had to be three!","As expected, three horses soon arrived.","Feng Wu frowned when she recognized the three horses.","Weren’t they Princess Rao’s maids?","These people were known for their wanton killing!"]},{"number":3792,"title":"Chapter 3792: The Maids","paragraphs":["Chapter 3792: The Maids","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","They arrived as fast as they could in their scarlet capes.","Feng Wu wasn’t the only one who had noticed it. Everyone else had their eyes on them.","Gao Mingjiang’s stomach lurched, and he told the others in a hurry, “Quickly, move to the side. Don’t disturb the noble ladies!”","The others also recognized the three horses. Back at the checkpoint, if they hadn’t run away in time, they would have been killed by now.","The others didn’t dare to look at them and only pretended to be busy, hoping that they would leave as soon as possible.","Things didn’t go as planned.","They wanted these three people to leave, but the latter suddenly stopped.","The girl named Caixia was the chief maid working for Princess Rao. She stopped the horse and was the first to jump off.","The members of the Gao family felt their stomachs lurch. They all lowered their heads and didn’t dare to move.","Miss Caixia was satisfied with what she saw. She was used to intimidating other people.","She scanned the crowd with her cold eyes. “Who’s the leader here?”","They all looked at Gao Mingjiang.","Gao Mingjiang stepped out.","“We’re requisitioning this place. Get lost.”","She was chasing them away!","However, the Gao family couldn’t reason with these bossy nobles anymore.","Gao Mingjiang nodded. “Alright, alright. We’re leaving now.”","Gao Mingjiang gave his friends a warning look, telling them to put the things in the carriage and leave.","However...","“I said requisition. Do you not understand?” Another girl behind Caixia asked in a cold voice.","Gao Mingjiang said, “What?”","“I’ve requisitioned everything. Just get lost.” The girl in the blue dress looked like she was going to lose her temper at any moment.","Gao Mingjiang said, “But we can’t live without them...’","“Well, that’s interesting. How dare a commoner try to bargain with us?” The girl in the blue dress clicked her tongue and glanced at Gao Mingjiang contemptuously. “It’s your honor that we even want to use your things! Now get lost!”","Just then, the third girl said, “Sister Caixia, Sister Zilan, we need someone to take care of our horses and our food. It’s not appropriate to chase them all away. How about we leave someone behind to look after us?” Caixia agreed. She glanced at the crowd and frowned.","These people were so filthy... They looked like beggars.","“It’s your call.” Caixia left it to Muli, while she sat down on a warm rock and began to cultivate.","Muli looked around and pointed at Feng Wu. “You stay here and serve us. The rest of you...”","Seeing the frightened looks on their faces, Muli said grumpily, “Do you really think we’ll take your trash? When you come back in a few hours, you can have everything back! ”","Fearing that Feng Wu would be bullied if she stayed, Li said in a hurry, “My girl is a little clumsy. How about... I take her place?”","Muli glanced at Li and said, “You two stay here, then!”","Seeing that Gao Mingjiang still wanted to say something, Muli noticed the impatient look on Caixia’s face, so she frowned at Gao Mingjiang.. “Leave now! If you offend Sister Caixia, you’ll all be killed!”"]},{"number":3793,"title":"Chapter 3793: Primary Heaven Pill","paragraphs":["Chapter 3793: Primary Heaven Pill","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Muli impatiently chased the others away.","Gao Mingjiang darted a concerned look at Feng Wu, but Feng Wu only waved at him, telling him that she would take care of it.","In the end, Gao Mingjiang had no choice but to lead the team away.","They didn’t go very far but stopped a few hundred meters away where they could stay out of the wind.","Meanwhile, Cai Xia and the others had gathered around.","Seeing that Feng Wu and Li had nothing better to do, Muli frowned. “We don’t have enough firewood here, nor do we have enough food. You two, do your job.","If you offend Sister Caixia, I’ll cut your heads off!”","Fearing that Feng Wu would be displeased, Li tugged at her sleeve to calm her down.","Feng Wu shook her head at Li, indicating that she wasn’t mad.","She was trying to come up with a plan.","Feng Wu pretended to be busy with the chopping board, but she kept her ears open, for the three of them were eating rabbits around a campfire while sipping the steaming hot soup in the pot.","Muli was the first to speak.","“Sister Caixia, we’ve been running for thousands of miles, but we still haven’t seen her. Do you think she’s not here?”","Caixia frowned but didn’t say anything.","Zilan, on the other hand, shook her head. “That won’t happen. According to our princess’s divination, that person will definitely come to Northern Yan, and it’ll be in the near future.”","Feng Wu’s stomach lurched.","A divination? That Princess Rao knew how to do that? Was she so sure that Feng Wu would come to Northern Yan?","Putting Master Linghu’s words together with Princess Rao’s action, Feng Wu felt that a big secret she didn’t know was slowly unfolding.","Muli went on. “The thirteen paths that lead into Northern Yan have all been blocked, and Her Royal Highness’s secret guards are all scattered around. But we haven’t heard from her yet. How strange.”","Zilan said, “I’ve been wondering... How did Miss Feng Wu offend our princess? By the sound of it, our princess wants to kill her at all cost...”","Muli shook her head. “I heard that the assassins of the Guillotine Inn were involved as well.”","“That’s right...” Zilan turned to Caixia. “Sister Caixia, you’re the princess’s favorite. Do you know why that is?”","Caixia didn’t reply.","Zilan was still curious. “I’ve been with the princess for so long, but I’ve never seen her so determined to kill a person. I heard that Feng Wu is just a girl, and we’ve put in so much effort...”","Caixia looked at her two deputies and shook her head. “That’s because you don’t know. ”","“So, Sister Caixia, you know the answer, don’t you? Just tell us. What’s going on?” The two girls cajoled Caixia.","In the end, Caixia had no choice but to say, “If I tell you, you’ll have to keep it a secret.”","“Yes!” The other two nodded repeatedly.","Caixia said, “I don’t know much, but I have some leads.","“Have you heard of the Primary Heaven Pill?”","Both girls shook their heads.","Caixia said, “It’s only natural that you don’t know because there’s probably only one such pill left in this world.”","She smiled bitterly. “Let’s put it this way. There are ten levels in total in the physical enhancement of one’s body, but if one takes this pill...” “What will happen, then?!” The two girls asked in unison.","Feng Wu pricked up her ears as well.."]},{"number":3794,"title":"Chapter 3794: Level Eight","paragraphs":["Chapter 3794: Level Eight","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Feng Wu pricked up her ears as well.","The Primary Heaven Pill? She had never heard of it before.","Feng Wu wanted to ask Little Phoenix in her head, but she suddenly realized that Little Phoenix had had an epiphany along the way and had gone to cultivate and make a breakthrough.","Hence, Feng Wu pricked up her ears and listened to them.","Just then, Caixia, the chief maid, snorted at Feng Wu. “Why isn’t there any hot water?”","“Bring us some hot water!” Zilan scolded Feng Wu.","“One moment...”","Fearing that they might get angry, Li fetched some hot water in a hurry. She was so nervous that she almost spilled it.","“I’ll do it.”","Feng Wu took the wooden bucket from Li, smiled at her, and handed it to the maids.","Muli was still asking curiously, “Sister Caixia, what will the pill do? It’s so difficult for us to train our bodies.”","Caixia snorted. “With that pill, if you’re lucky, you’ll be able to rise directly to","Level 8!”","“Level 8?!” Hearing Caixia’s words, the other two maids cried out with envy.","They were so envious that they thought they were going to lose their minds. The three of them had all worked so hard in physical enhancement, but they had only reached a few levels.","“What about the pill...” Muli took a deep breath.","“Don’t even think about it. How can you possibly have a share in the pill? There’s only one of them in this world.” Caixia snorted. “It belongs to our princess.”","“If there’s only one of them in the world, of course, it belongs to our princess.” Zilan nodded. “She’s one of the best cultivators of her generation. Even Zuo","Qingluan of the Junwu Empire isn’t her match.”","Muli mumbled, “But... I heard that the Junwu Empire has a genius girl. She has the Divine Phoenix Blood...”","“What Divine Phoenix Blood? Are you going to believe her just because she says she has the Divine Phoenix Blood?” Zilan was very supportive of her princess and couldn’t stand the compliments of other people. She smirked and said, “If that Feng Wu really is that amazing, why did she stay quiet for so many years and only came out to promote herself when His Royal Highness was getting married? Sister Caixia, don’t you think Feng Wu is so scheming?”","Next to her, Feng Wu was speechless.","But what Caixia said surprised Zilan.","“Not really.” Caixia frowned. “Miss Feng Wu isn’t to be underestimated.” “Why?” Zilan was displeased.","Caixia said, “If she’s as useless as you say, why would our princess need secret guards like us to track her down? And after so long, we still haven’t found anything. That alone makes me think that she’s something.”","“Sister Caixia, you’re amazing.” Muli nodded. “I think so, too.”","Zilan didn’t like the sound of that. “I don’t think she’s all that capable.”","Cai Xia smirked. “Our princess isn’t the only one that’s after her. The Zuo family of the Junwu Empire, the Hua family, and the Dongsang Kingdom are all looking for her, and they’ve all sent some very influential people. We haven’t heard anything yet. She’s done a great job of staying hidden.","“But...” Caixia smirked.. “If she keeps hiding like this, she won’t be able to keep that treasure!”"]},{"number":3795,"title":"Chapter 3795: Don I t Tell Anyone","paragraphs":["Chapter 3795: Don I t Tell Anyone","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","“What treasure?” Everyone turned to look at Caixia.","Meanwhile. Caixia lowered her voice. “I’m onlv telling vou. Don’t tell anvone","“I swear! I won’t tell a soul. Otherwise, I’ll be struck by lightning.”","“Me, too! I won’t let anyone else know!”","They both raised their hands to make an oath.","Only then did Caixia nod. “That’s a secret. I wouldn’t have told you if we weren’t outside. I heard that the Primary Heaven Pill isn’t our princess’s yet.”","Muli frowned. “What do you mean by that?”","Caixia said, “The pill belongs to someone else, but it’ll be our princess’s after a month.”","Muli’s eyes flickered, and she asked, “Someone else? Do you mean Miss Feng Wii?”","Zilan spat on the ground. “Bullshit! How can that one-of-a-kind pill be Feng","Wu’s? That’s impossible!”","However, Caixia said indifferently, “Maybe it really is hers.”","What? Zilan stared at Caixia in disbelief.","Meanwhile, Feng Wu, who had gone back to the chopping board and pretended to be busy, was amazed as well. A Primary Heaven Pill?","It was hers?","She couldn’t believe it...","Could it be because of her Senior Brother Huyan?","Feng Wu still had a lot of questions, so she listened carefully.","However, Li didn’t understand a word. She looked utterly confused and was terrified.","Zilan said anxiously, “How’s that possible? What does that pill have anything to do with Feng Wu? How can it be hers?”","Caixia said, “Our princess has dropped some hints, so we have to find Feng Wu and kill her. If she gets to the imperial capital safely... If she takes the pill, the princess will be so mad that she’ll kill us!”","Caixia was very serious, and so were the other two.","Zilan said, “Our princess is a very talented cultivator, but she’s physically weak, so she needs that pill.”","The other two nodded in unison.","Feng Wu thought to herself, “I need it, too...”","If the pill really was hers, she would never give it up.","If it wasn’t her, she still wouldn’t let Princess Rao have it because that woman had been trying to kill her.","“The two of them...","Just then, Zilan made a hand gesture. Caixia frowned and rose to her feet. “That’s enough. Let’s go.”","She then gave Zilan a warning glance.","Zilan nodded.","Cai Xiao and Muli jumped onto their horses and galloped off, their scarlet capes stirring up the wind in the dark.","Zilan glanced at Feng Wu and Li and said indifferently, “Your service is quite nice. Here’s a reward for you.”","After that, she tossed out two silver ingots.","She tossed one piece to Li and the other to Feng Wu.","“Catch it!” Zilan gave them a threatening look.","Seeing the shiny silver ingot in the night sky, Zilan smiled and nodded. “You’ve done a great job. Come with me. I need to talk to you.”","Feng Wu had an idea, but Li had no idea what Zilan was going to do next.","Feng Wu was alarmed, and a dagger appeared in her sleeve.","She and Li followed Zilan through the woods.."]},{"number":3796,"title":"Chapter 3796: Clean up the Mess (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3796: Clean up the Mess (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Feng Wu and Li followed Zilan through the woods.","“Come here.” Zilan waved at Li.","Despite her fear, Li still forced herself to walk toward Zilan. Zilan glanced at Li and smirked. “You have the plague. Die!” As soon as she said those words, Zilan struck Li’s head with a knife.","“Ahhh!”","Li’s stomach lurched.","Just then, there was a whooshing sound.","A dagger cut Zilan’s throat.","Zilan turned around and looked at the people behind her.","Feng Wu stood behind her with an indifferent look on her face and a calm look in her eyes. She was holding a dagger, and blood was trickling down the blade.","“You...” Zilan was dumbfounded.","She was supposed to be the one in control and could decide who lived or died, but now...","Feng Wu watched as Zilan fell.","“Little Feng...” Frightened, Li grabbed Feng Wu’s hand and burst into tears. She was too scared to speak.","Had it not been for Feng Wu, she would have been dead by now.","Feng Wu patted the back of her hand.","“I need to take care of this. Otherwise...” Feng Wu recalled that there were still a lot of people in the Gao family.","Things would have been much easier if she was all by herself. She could run as fast as she wanted into the woods, but what about the Gao family?","They weren’t just names, but flesh and blood. They had been eating, living, and getting along well with each other... Feng Wu couldn’t just stand there and watch them get killed.","She told Li, “Go back to your family now and set out immediately. You have to reach the border city at noon tomorrow. Otherwise, you won’t be able to get in.” “But, but...” Li was at a loss.","Feng Wu said calmly, “If you panic now, so many people in the Gao family will lose their heads. Are you sure you still want to panic?”","Li had been panic-stricken at first, but hearing Feng Wu’s words, she immediately calmed down as if someone had poured cold water on her head.","She knew that Feng was the most capable member of the team, so she listened to the girl.","Feng Wu said, “You don’t have to worry about anything here. Go back to your team and tell them to set out now. As for me... tell them that they’ve taken me away.”","Li said, “But...","Feng Wu said, “No buts. If you tell the Gao family about what really happened, do you think they’ll be able to handle it and keep it a secret? You heard it yourself. They’re Princess Rao’s people.”","Li shook her head anxiously. Her family couldn’t take it, and they would have a nervous breakdown.","Feng Wu nodded. “So, you don’t have to tell them what happened here. Just tell them that the three people have taken me away. As for what happened here... you don’t have to worry about it. And you...”","Feng Wu smeared something on Li’s face. “The ointment will fester your face for a while, but it’ll recover in time. Don’t worry. It’s to keep you alive.” Li was concerned. “What about you? Are you going to turn yourself in?”","Feng Wu chuckled. “Why would I do that? Don’t worry. I have my own plan.","Don’t you know what I’m capable of?”","After much persuasion, Feng Wu finally persuaded Li to leave.."]},{"number":3797,"title":"Chapter 3797: Clean up the Mess (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3797: Clean up the Mess (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","However, Li wouldn’t be able to withstand such pressure. She wouldn’t tell anyone, but she would tell Gao Mingjiang. Feng Wu knew that very well.","After Lady Wang went back, Feng Wu stared at Zilan’s body.","Soon, a fully-dressed Zilan showed up. Needless to say, it was Feng Wu.","As for Zilan’s body, Feng Wu had melted completely with some potion.","After taking care of Zilan’s body, Feng Wu ran to the horse as fast as she could, jumped onto it, and disappeared out of sight.","Before long, she caught up with Caixia on horseback.","“What took you so long? Did you take care of everything?” Muli frowned at her.","Feng Wu had observed Zilan’s behavior, so she had no problem mimicking her.","“It’s been taken care of.” Feng Wu smirked. “It didn’t take me much effort to kill a commoner.”","Muli was confused. “Then why did it take you so long? Sister Caixia thought something had happened to you.” Feng Wu smiled. “You’ll see when we get back.” Muli snorted. “You’re such a poser!”","Feng Wu said proudly, “I’m not telling you.”","This was how Zilan usually bickered with Muli. If Feng Wu was too careful now, she might give herself away.","Neither Caixia nor Muli realized that their friend had been replaced by Feng wu.","Caixia turned around and gave them a stern look. “Quiet! We must hurry up!”","Muli stuck out her tongue and stopped talking to Feng Wu.","Feng Wu was curious. Where were they going?","Shouldn’t they be going back to the imperial capital?","The border city was right ahead of them, but Caixiao took them around a corner. Instead of entering the city gate, they headed for a main road nearby.","Feng Wu and Muli looked at each other. Why didn’t they enter?","“We’re going to see someone.” Caixia narrowed her eyes.","Before long, they arrived at a mountain peak.","Standing by the edge of the cliff, they saw a bottomless pit in the mist.","From afar, they could see the mist rising and falling, and the border city was barely visible through it.","Caixia didn’t get off the horse, so Feng Wu and Muli remained on horseback as well.","Looking around, Muli saw that the three of them were alone, so she asked curiously, “Sister Caixia, who are we here to see?”","Caixia waved at her to calm her down.","Feng Wu narrowed her eyes and pricked up her ears.","She heard footsteps coming their way.","She was right. A moment later, a figure showed up in front of Caixia.","It was obvious that Caixia knew the person.","They nodded at each other.","Feng Wu noticed that it was a woman. She wore a white dress and had a slender figure. There was a white flower on her sideburns. She was a mourner.","Seeing her, Caixia dismounted, walked up to her, and bowed respectfully. “Miss Hua, it’s been a while.”","Hua?","Feng Wu recalled what happened a few days ago.","The Hua family and the Zuo family had joined hands and tried to destroy the Feng family, but Feng Wu had planned everything out. In the end, more than half of the masters of the Zuo and Hua families were killed or injured overnight, and the two families were on the verge of collapse.","Things weren’t so bad for the Hua family, but the Zuo family had collaborated with the Dongsang Kingdom, and the evidence was irrefutable.."]},{"number":3798,"title":"Chapter 3798: Hua Family","paragraphs":["Chapter 3798: Hua Family","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","But the Zuo family had colluded with the Dongsang Kingdom, and the evidence was irrefutable. As a result, the entire Zuo family collapsed. Some of them ran away, but Emperor Wu caught the rest.","The Zuo family’s house was ransacked, and many members were beheaded. It was a boisterous scene.","But the Hua family...","Feng Wu remembered that apart from the capable cultivators who had died in the arena, everyone else in the Hua family was still alive.","However, after this battle, the Hua family had lost most of its members. Who was this young lady?","Caixia and the young woman didn’t try to hide their conversation, so Feng Wu heard everything.","“Still no news of your princess?” Miss Hua frowned at Caixia.","Caixia shook her head. “There were several suspicious cases, but it turned out none of them was Feng Wu.”","“She really knows how to mislead people.” Miss Hua smirked. “With all the traps we’ve set up, I don’t believe that she can get away. She’s probably dead by now!”","Caixia nodded. “That’s possible.”","Miss Hua stared at Caixia. “If you do find anything on her, remember, her head belongs to the Hua family. As for what your princess wants, we’ll hand it over to her on a plate.”","Caixia said, “Of course.”","Miss Wu disappeared as quickly as she showed up, and Caixiao was soon back on her horse.","Muli asked curiously, “Is that Miss Hua, our princess’s best friend?”","Caixia nodded.","Muli said, “She seems to hate Feng Wu.”","Caixia said, “The Hua family is the source of much of our princess’s information on Feng Wu. She has made the Hua family miserable, and more than half of the Spiritual Overlords have been killed. The Hua family will never","forgive her for that.” Muli said, “Is Feng Wu really that capable?”","Caixia frowned. “I hope not.”","Muli said, “You have a point. What if she takes our princess’s pill?”","Caixia nodded.","Muli said, “Apart from us, the Hua family is looking for her as well. I heard that the Zuo family is also looking everywhere for her. If she’s smart enough, she’ll have gone into hiding by now. She’ll never come back to our capital. She’s not stupid.”","Caixia frowned a little. “She’s so different from other people. Even the princess can only divine a fraction of her behavior, and it can only prove that she’s still alive. We can’t tell where she is. Of course, if she’s very close, our princess may be able to divine it right away. She’s a great diviner.”","“You don’t say. She’s the smartest person I’ve ever met. No one can predict the future like her.”","“Come. We’re going to see the princess now.”","Caixia waved the things in her hands. It was something that Miss Hua had told her to bring to Princess Rao.","Feng Wu frowned a little. A prophecy? A divination?","Was this Princess Rao really as good as she was said to be? If she was, she should be able to identify the real Feng Wu.","It seemed that Feng Wu had to leave the team as soon as possible.","That was what Feng Wu thought and what she did.","The three of them had no problem getting into the border city, but tents had been set up outside, and they were filled with people from the south.","Feng Wu asked around and realized that people from Northern Yan couldn’t enter the city all at once. Most of them could only make do with a straw hut outside.."]},{"number":3799,"title":"Chapter 3799: Northern Yan (1)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3799: Northern Yan (1)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","Caixia said, “Go back and get some rest. I’m afraid we’ll have to set out again tomorrow.”","Muli said, “Sure.”","She then waved at Feng Wu. “Sister Zilan, I’ll see you here tomorrow.” She dashed off after that.","Meanwhile, Caixia was rushing into the imperial palace as fast as she could.","Feng Wu didn’t know what to say.","So, she had been left here.","Princess Rao lived in the imperial palace, but because of her influential force, she had a residence outside the imperial city, which was where Feng Wu was now.","Feng Wu thought to herself, “Since I’m here, I might as well have a look.”","Hence, she only walked a short distance before she saw a group of people rushing out.","Feng Wu noticed that they were all soldiers, and each one of them was covered in scales and holding a sharp saber.","Involuntarily, Feng Wu shifted and hid in the shadows.","She heard the leader say, “Where is she? Where is the girl that stood here just then?”","How intimidating!","Feng Wu frowned a little. She remembered clearly that she had been standing there before, and of course, she wasn’t the only one who had been passing by... Just then, an old man arrived. “Master Ling, what’s the matter?”","“Steward Wang, was someone here before?” Master Ling asked in a displeased tone. A yellow fox was circling around the spot where Feng Wu had been standing, wagging its tail.","” “Here...","Steward Wang couldn’t make up his mind because he hadn’t noticed anything.","“Well... I didn’t notice any person. Master Ling, what happened?” Steward Wang didn’t look too happy.","He had always been in charge of the outer courtyard of the princess’s residence, and he didn’t like Master Ling’s attitude at all.","Master Ling cupped his hands at Steward Wang. “I’m not being arrogant, but it’s really urgent! Her Royal Highness has come up with a new divination result. The person she’s looking for has shown up here before!”","WHAT?!","Steward Wang’s stomach lurched.","He had always known that the princess was looking for someone, and a lot of people had been sent out of the manor these days.","And he wasn’t the only one. Feng Wu felt as if she was going to suffocate.","What was this Princess Rao’s divination ability? How could she pinpoint the location? She had indeed been there before!","Luckily, she wasn’t the only one...","What Feng Wu didn’t know was that Princess Rao had spent a lot of time and effort to locate Feng Wu.","However, it was a one-off attempt, and she couldn’t afford to use it all the time. It wouldn’t be so easy to locate Feng Wu again.","Master Ling said, “She might not be here in the residence, but we’re going in the right direction. Steward Wang, please take care of what happens next.”","He then turned to the soldiers behind him. “Search the area within 1.5km from the southeast of the princess’s residence! No one is to be spared!”","‘Yes!”","Only then did Feng Wu relax a little. It seemed that the princess had divined a radius of 1.5km.","But that was already terrifying enough.","After all, Feng Wu hadn’t recovered her spiritual essence yet and couldn’t use it yet.","How frustrating.","If one had to compare them, Princess Rao was like a giant with a bunch of minions, while Feng Wu..."]},{"number":3800,"title":"Chapter 3800: Northern Yan (2)","paragraphs":["Chapter 3800: Northern Yan (2)","Translator: Henyee Translations Editor: Henyee Translations","If one had to compare them, Princess Rao was a colossus with a lot of footsoldiers, while Feng Wu was all alone.","The difference was simply too great. She couldn’t confront the princess just yet.","Feng Wu rubbed her forehead with a wry smile. She had to find Huyan Yanbo as soon as possible and get her strength back.","That way, she would be able to handle Princess Rao, who wanted her dead.","Feng Wu quietly left the princess’s residence, making it look like she was leaving the city.","After she left the city, she faked a scene of fighting and made it look like Zilan was dead.","That way, she could cover her tracks by impersonating Zilan, and the Gao family wouldn’t be incriminated.","Meanwhile, Feng Wu was walking around the city in her ugly girl form.","The capital city of Northern Yan was similar to the imperial capital of the Junwu Empire. The streets were all horizontal and vertical. It was spacious and full of people.","Just then, Feng Wu heard a voice in her head.","“I know how to find Huyan.”","It was Little Phoenix!","As it spoke, a bird with colorful feathers came out of her sleeve.","Feng Wu noticed a tuft of white hair on its head.","She poked it in the forehead. “That’s new”","Little Phoenix raised its chin. “That’s because I’m getting much better.”","Feng Wu asked curiously, “How capable are you now?”","Little Phoenix gloated. “I’m a peak Spiritual Overlord now!”","Feng Wu’s stomach lurched. Before, Little Phoenix was about her level.","Before she lost her ability, she was only a junior Spiritual Overlord. But now, Little Phoenix had reached the peak of the Spiritual Overlord Stage after an epiphany.","“That was fast!” Feng Wu looked at it in amazement.","Little Phoenix looked equally amazed. “That’s right. That was fast. But it’s really strange. Is traveling the world really that amazing?”","Little Phoenix scratched its head. It didn’t know why, but it was always a good thing to make a breakthrough.","Feng Wu thought to herself, “Although I’ve been chased all the way here, Little","Phoenix has made so many breakthroughs already. It’s worth it.”","Little Phoenix said earnestly, “You need to get your body back as soon as possible. I have a feeling that you’re going to make a great breakthrough as well!”","Feng Wu nodded. Little Phoenix wasn’t the only one who had that feeling. She had it as well.","“By the way, what did you say?” Feng Wu remembered what Little Phoenix said earlier.","“Only by taking that pill from Little Yanbo can you get your cultivation ability back. I know where to find him. Come with me!”","Little Phoenix stood on Feng Wu’s shoulder and showed her the way.","Right now, Feng Wu was as ordinary as an ugly girl, and she didn’t have any spiritual essence fluctuation, so no one noticed her.","Feng Wu followed Little Phoenix’s lead and kept walking...","She had lost count of how many tunnels and turns she had taken...","“There!”","Little Phoenix gloated. “I visited Yanbo a long time ago. He lives there!”","Pointing at the woods a short distance away, Little Phoenix said excitedly, “Let’s go!”","However...","As soon as they showed up, a cold shield hit them.","Feng Wu stumbled back with a thump and was almost crushed.","“Ssss...” She drew in her breath.."]}]);
